  <Placemark>
    <name>3 Dollar Deweys Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[3 Dollar Dewey's<br/><br/>📍 421 Commercial Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Located at 421 Commercial Street, 3 Dollar Dewey's was designed in 1852 by Charles A. Alexander. Originally owned by Frank P. Cummings, the first floor was occupied by a wholesale grocery store through the 1920s.<br/><br/>Fast-forward to 1981 when Earl Eames, known as the "Indiana Jones of beer," opened this local watering hole — a favorite for Portland residents and visitors alike.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/3+Dollar+Deweys/@43.650022,-70.2578549,17z]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
