    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Abandoned Ski Lift McFarland Mountain Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Abandoned Ski Lift, McFarland Mountain<br/><br/>📍 Off Route 233 near Eagle Lake, Acadia National Park, ME (coordinate is the Eagle Lake Boat Landing, nearest sourced landmark — not the ruins themselves)<br/><br/>The ruins of a decommissioned ski lift and slope from the 1930s-40s on McFarland Mountain, reached via an unpaved road and field off Route 233 near Eagle Lake. It's essentially unpromoted and undocumented in any mainstream park guide.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- No confirmed coordinate exists for the ruins themselves — the pin here is the Eagle Lake Boat Landing on Route 233, the nearest sourced landmark; expect some additional searching on the ground<br/>- Bring a printed description or GPS track from a source blog before attempting to find it]]></description>
