      <coordinates>-71.13701633576993,44.07425133558177,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Abenaki Tower Tuftonboro NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Abenaki Tower<br/><br/>📍 Edgerly Hill, Tuftonboro, NH<br/><br/>Built by community volunteers in 1924 — Lewis McIntire of Tuftonboro constructed it for $400 after two local outdoor enthusiasts, standing atop Edgerly Hill, decided the view deserved a tower. Despite local legend, it was never a fire tower and was never used to watch for WWII aircraft; it's built where several old Abenaki trails once crossed. Deteriorated and was rebuilt in 1976–78, rededicated in 1978.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- One of the easiest big views in the Lakes Region: a five-minute walk on a graded dirt path from the parking area.<br/>- Views take in Lake Winnipesaukee and the Belknap Range.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.6588%2C%20-71.2828]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
