  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Acadia Mountain Trail Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Acadia Mountain Trail<br/><br/>📍 Acadia National Park ME (Route 102, ~3 miles south of Somesville)<br/><br/>A 2.5-mile loop on the "quiet side" of Mount Desert Island with consistently top-rated summit views over Somes Sound — the only fjord on the U.S. East Coast — and far fewer crowds than Cadillac Mountain or the Beehive. Moderate difficulty with a steady climb.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Note: unlike Beehive/Precipice this isn't an iron-rung trail, but it does have steep, exposed granite slab sections near the summit with real drop-offs — worth knowing given vertigo sensitivity, even though it's not in the same category as the ladder trails.<br/>- Small roadside parking lot on Route 102, opposite the trailhead, fills early in peak season.<br/>- Can be combined with St. Sauveur Mountain for a longer loop (~1,673 ft total elevation gain) if you want more of a day.<br/>- Coordinates above are an approximation of the trailhead — worth confirming against Google Maps before you go, since I couldn't find an authoritative exact figure.]]></description>
