  <Placemark>
    <name>Alligerville Historic District Accord NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Alligerville Historic District<br/><br/>📍 Alligerville, Town of Rochester, NY<br/><br/>Grew up after 1828 around Lock 21 (originally Lock 22) on the Delaware & Hudson Canal, one of the earliest canals in the country. The district holds 81 contributing buildings, 5 contributing sites, and 8 contributing structures in Greek Revival, Gothic Revival, and Italian Villa styles, including the John & Catrina Alliger House (c. 1828), the Reformed Dutch Church of the Clove Chapel (c. 1858), and the Thomas S. Schoonmaker Farm (1830). Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2015.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A drive-through hamlet rather than a visitor site — best appreciated from Lucas Turnpike/Route 213 as part of a broader byway loop.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.7958%2C%20-74.1967]]></description>
