  <Placemark>
    <name>Amenia Village NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Amenia Village<br/><br/>📍 Routes 44 & 22, Amenia, NY 12501<br/><br/>This unincorporated village, formerly Paine's Corners, grew at the crossing of the Turnpike, the Great Rd. to NY, and the NY & Harlem RR. The 19th-century Amenia Island Cemetery on Rt. 343 sits within a lively business hub housed in Victorian commercial buildings. Mechanic St. leads to the Town Hall, site of the former Harlem RR station and the Harlem Valley Rail Trail — scenic paved walking, rollerblading, biking and cross-country skiing linking towns, villages and state parks from Amenia to Copake Falls, NY. The Post Office building dates to 1865; the Greek Revival former Baptist Church on Rt. 22 South (ca. 1851) is now a gift shop. The business center is marked by the stone mansard-roofed M&T Bank with its 1906 fountain/horse trough memorial to Dr. Joseph R. Guernsey.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Park and walk to shops/restaurants at the intersection of Rts. 44 and 22.<br/>- Combine with a walk or bike ride on the Harlem Valley Rail Trail.<br/>- Stop 10 of 17 on the Washington & Amenia Scenic Tour (Tour 4) — no dedicated Amenia, NY destination note exists yet, so it's linked to the tour hub directly.<br/>- Coordinates left blank — no verified lat/lon source found yet for the village center specifically.]]></description>
