  <Placemark>
    <name>Andries DuBois House Wallkill NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Andries DuBois House<br/><br/>📍 Wallkill Avenue, Wallkill, NY<br/><br/>Built around 1769 by Andries DuBois, a local stone mason descended from Louis DuBois, one of New Paltz's original Huguenot settlers — the house's oak timbers were confirmed to that date by 2005 dendrochronological analysis. Destroyed by fire in the late 1700s, rebuilt around 1814, and remodeled in the Greek Revival style around 1845, giving it alternating brick and wood walls, a gambrel roof, and distinctive eyebrow windows. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1998. A local historical society is restoring it for use as a history museum.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Check current renovation status before planning a visit — restoration was ongoing as of the most recent reporting.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.6091%2C%20-74.1859]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
