  <Placemark>
    <name>Ann's Book Bistro Damariscotta ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-10T16:00:00<br/><br/>Ann's Book Bistro<br/><br/>📍 17 Back Meadow Rd, Damariscotta, ME<br/><br/>Full name is Ann's Book Bistro — a northern Spanish restaurant built around authentic paella, run by Chef Chris Padil, who has El Bulli (Barcelona) experience. The space doubles as a bookshop, with a curated collection of books available to browse or borrow — a genuinely distinctive touch, not a gimmick. Menu runs comfort food alongside small plates, with Monday pasta nights (salad, soup, up to 5 pasta small plates for $19). Reviews are overwhelmingly positive on execution and atmosphere, with some flagging the cost as high relative to portion size.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Paella — the signature dish<br/>- Salmon crudo<br/>- Burrata<br/>- Seafood stew (Cazuela)<br/>- Argentinian Churrasco<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Closed Sunday–Tuesday; open Wednesday–Saturday, 11am–2pm and 4pm–9pm. Happy hour Wed–Fri, 4pm–6pm.<br/>- Monday pasta night ($19 for soup, salad, and multiple pasta small plates) is a genuinely different, cheaper way to experience the kitchen — but note it falls on a day the regular menu/hours above don't apply, so confirm this specifically.<br/>- Reservations recommended — small, popular room.<br/>- Budget for higher-than-average pricing relative to portions; go in expecting a special-occasion meal, not a bargain.<br/><br/>More info: https://annsbookbistro.me/]]></description>
