  <Placemark>
    <name>Annandale Hamlet NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Annandale<br/><br/>📍 Annandale-on-Hudson, NY<br/><br/>Annandale's proximity to the Hudson made it a mill site from the mid-1700s, producing everything from flour and woolens to the last venture, ca. 1900, when W.H. Baker built a chocolate factory so successful it had to move to larger quarters in Red Hook.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Stop 11 of 33 on the Rhinebeck, Red Hook & Milan Scenic Tour (Tour 1).]]></description>
