  <Placemark>
    <name>Anvil Trail and Raven's Nest Schoodic ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Anvil Trail & Raven's Nest<br/><br/>📍 Schoodic Peninsula, Acadia National Park, ME<br/><br/>A moderate 2-mile out-and-back hike combining the Alder, Schoodic Head, and Anvil trails that climbs 440 feet to the highest point on the Schoodic Peninsula. Far less trafficked than comparable hikes on Mount Desert Island, with sweeping 360-degree views across Frenchman Bay to Cadillac Mountain, Bar Harbor, and two visible lighthouses (Mark Island Light and Egg Rock Light).<br/><br/>Raven's Nest Detour<br/><br/>On the return, detour to Raven's Nest, a cliff-top sunset and photography spot featuring isolated coves that most day-trippers skip entirely. This is a genuine hidden gem for solitude and dramatic views.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Start early (before 9 a.m.) to avoid afternoon crowds<br/>- Park at the small lot 1.6 miles past the unofficial trailhead to avoid tickets<br/>- The summit is excellent for sunset and golden-hour photography<br/>- Trail is well-marked but somewhat steep; good boots recommended<br/>- Water and snacks important; limited services nearby<br/>- Very low crowding compared to Jordan Pond or Jordan Cliffs on Mount Desert Island]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
