  <Placemark>
    <name>Appalachian Gap Waitsfield VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Appalachian Gap ("App Gap")<br/><br/>📍 Route 17, between Waitsfield and the Champlain Valley, VT<br/><br/>A 2,369-foot mountain pass on Route 17, with sustained pitches over 15% on either side and one of Vermont's best panoramic overlooks — sweeping west across the Champlain Valley to Lake Champlain and the Adirondack Mountains beyond. The Long Trail (Vermont's 272-mile north-south hiking trail) crosses right at the gap, threading between Stark Mountain to the south and Baby Stark Mountain to the north; trailheads nearby lead to viewpoints like Molly Stark's Balcony and the Theron Dean Shelter. A well-known destination for motorcyclists and road cyclists chasing the twisty climb.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A dramatic, winding drive — take it slow, especially with a trailer or in poor weather.<br/>- Right next to Mad River Glen, so easy to see both in one stop.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.2112%2C%20-72.9316]]></description>
