  <Placemark>
    <name>Arethusa Falls Crawford Notch NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Arethusa Falls<br/><br/>📍 Crawford Notch NH<br/><br/>At 200 feet, the tallest waterfall in New Hampshire — a slender ribbon of water dropping through a shadowed granite canyon. The 2.7-mile round trip through hardwood forest is consistently beautiful; the falls reward with scale and setting that exceeds any expectation. Can be extended into a 5-mile loop over Frankenstein Cliff for panoramic Crawford Notch views.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Trailhead is at a pullout on Route 302 in Crawford Notch, 5 miles south of Bretton Woods.<br/>- The trail crosses Bemis Brook twice — straightforward in normal conditions.<br/>- Extend the hike to Frankenstein Cliff (5-mile loop) for one of the best views in the Notch.<br/>- Best flow in May and June; still striking through September.]]></description>
