  <Placemark>
    <name>Artist Bluff Franconia NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Artist Bluff<br/><br/>📍 Franconia NH<br/><br/>A 20-minute scramble above Echo Lake delivers one of the finest views in the White Mountains — Cannon Mountain rising directly overhead, the Notch framed between Cannon and Kinsman ridges, Echo Lake shimmering below, and the Franconia Range extending north. Almost no one does this trail despite the trailhead being at the main Cannon Mountain parking area. The most rewarding effort-to-view ratio in Franconia Notch.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Trailhead is at the Echo Lake parking area off Exit 3 on I-93.<br/>- The round trip is 0.7 miles — allow 45 minutes for the scramble and the views.<br/>- Often done in combination with the Bald Mountain trail next door (adds another 0.4 miles and another viewpoint).<br/>- Best in clear weather — the view is the entire payoff.]]></description>
