  <Placemark>
    <name>Asa Hanson Block Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Asa Hanson Block<br/><br/>📍 548–550 Congress Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The Asa Hanson Block at 548–550 Congress Street is an example of late Victorian architecture, built in 1889. Architects Francis Fassett & Frederick A. Tompson designed the building — it is one of seven surviving commercial designs by Fassett in Portland.<br/><br/>The block was constructed by real estate developer Charles Perry, whose name appears on a panel on the building's facade.<br/><br/>In 2001, the building was added to the National Register of Historic Places.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/548+Congress+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
