  <Placemark>
    <name>Attitash Mountain Resort Bartlett NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Attitash Mountain Resort<br/><br/>📍 Route 302, Bartlett, NH<br/><br/>A two-mountain ski resort (Attitash and Bear Peak, 67 trails combined) near North Conway, mixing classic New England-style runs with wide-open cruisers. In summer, it historically ran North America's longest Alpine Slide (over a mile) plus the Nor'Easter Mountain Coaster, EuroBungy, climbing wall, and water slides — but per recent reports, summer operations haven't run since 2019, with owner Vail Resorts prioritizing winter investment instead.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Verify current summer operating status before planning around the Alpine Slide or other warm-weather attractions — they may not be running.<br/>- Winter skiing is the resort's reliable, currently-operating draw.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0800%2C%20-71.2800]]></description>
