  <Placemark>
    <name>Augusta and Hallowell Day Trip</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Augusta & Hallowell Day Trip<br/><br/>📍 Augusta & Hallowell, ME (~41 miles, 54–57 minutes from Camden via Route 17)<br/><br/>A full day combining state history, a free botanical garden, and one of Maine's most charming small downtowns for dining and antiquing. Offers a distinct experience from coastal destinations—more inland character and local focus.<br/><br/>Itinerary<br/><br/>Late Morning: Maine State House (10:00 a.m.–11:15 a.m.)<br/>Start at the Maine State House, a working capitol built from granite quarried in nearby Hallowell. Tour is free and self-guided (about one hour) through the historic Hall of Flags and up to a rooftop veranda overlooking the Kennebec River. The adjacent Maine State Museum is mid-renovation (not fully open until October 2026), but the Blaine House (governor's residence) still offers tours if interested.<br/><br/>Mid-Morning: Viles Arboretum (11:30 a.m.–12:30 p.m.)<br/>Walk or drive five minutes to Viles Arboretum, a free 224-acre botanical garden with six miles of trails, cultivated gardens, and a peaceful pond loop. Described by visitors as "a peaceful place for a walk and contemplation"—a quiet nature break before heading to Hallowell.<br/><br/>Lunch: Hallowell (1:00–2:00 p.m.)<br/>Drive ten minutes south to Hallowell, a National Historic District along Water Street packed with antique shops, galleries, and restaurants that draw locals rather than tour buses. Have lunch at:<br/>- Slate's Restaurant & Bakery — 25-plus-year local institution<br/>- Or Liberal Cup for brewpub casual dining<br/><br/>Afternoon: Antiques & Galleries (2:00–4:00 p.m.)<br/>Browse Hallowell's Water Street antique and gallery scene:<br/>- Hallowell Antique Mall — 80 dealers with wide variety<br/>- The Rusticator's Emporium — curated vintage finds<br/>- Additional galleries and shops along Water Street<br/><br/>Late Afternoon: Optional Rail Trail Walk (4:00–5:00 p.m.)<br/>If timing allows, walk a stretch of the Kennebec River Rail Trail, which runs from Augusta's waterfront through Hallowell to Gardiner. Perfect for a quiet walk along the Kennebec River before heading back to Camden.<br/><br/>Why This Trip Works<br/><br/>- Drive time: 54–57 minutes from Camden—comfortably under the one-hour limit<br/>- Theme: State capital history and gardens, distinct from coastal trips<br/>- Local focus: Drawn locals rather than cruise-ship tourists<br/>- Free attractions: State House tour and Viles Arboretum are both free<br/>- Variety: Mix of civic/historical, nature, and downtown browsing<br/>- No overlap: Heads inland on Route 17, not competing with Bar Harbor-bound routes<br/><br/>Notes<br/><br/>- Dress for walking and browsing—good shoes recommended<br/>- Viles Arboretum is free but allows donations<br/>- Hallowell is particularly good for antique collectors and vintage shoppers<br/>- The area has strong local restaurant character vs. touristy chains<br/>- Best for a full-day outing rather than a quick stop]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-orange</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>day-trip</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>gem</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>orange</value></Data>
    </ExtendedData>
