  <Placemark>
    <name>Avery Rock Lighthouse Machiasport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Avery Rock Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Machias Bay, near Machiasport, ME<br/><br/>A light station established in 1875 on a bare granite ledge to guide vessels into Machias Bay — one of Maine's harshest lighthouse postings. The original brick dwelling and tower survived decades of storms until a catastrophic gale in January 1928 nearly destroyed the station; it was automated in 1934 and the original structures demolished in 1947, replaced by the steel skeleton tower that stands today.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Boat-only — the rock itself is not publicly accessible and can only be viewed from the water.<br/>- Far Down East (well past Bar Harbor); realistically only seen on a Machias-area boat trip, not a casual detour.]]></description>
