  <Placemark>
    <name>Back Cove Trail Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Back Cove Trail<br/><br/>📍 Back Cove, Portland, ME — trailhead parking at Payson Park, Baxter Blvd<br/><br/>The Back Cove Trail is a 3.5-mile paved loop around Back Cove, a tidal estuary just north of Portland's downtown peninsula. It's one of the most-used recreational trails in Maine — flat, scenic, and accessible to walkers, runners, and cyclists alike.<br/><br/>The trail runs along Baxter Boulevard and offers wide-open views across the cove toward the Portland skyline and, on clear days, the White Mountains. The tidal flats attract shorebirds and waterfowl, making it a casual birding spot as well.<br/><br/>Connections<br/>- Connects to the Eastern Promenade trail at the eastern end for a longer loop around the full peninsula<br/>- Combined Back Cove + Eastern Promenade loop is approximately 6–7 miles<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Completely flat — an easy morning run or sunset walk<br/>- Parking available at Payson Park (Baxter Blvd & Allen Ave) and along Baxter Blvd<br/>- The western stretch near the I-295 overpass is the least scenic — keep going, the cove views open up quickly<br/>- Best at high tide when the cove is full; low tide exposes mudflats<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Back+Cove+Trail/@43.6712,-70.2797,15z]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Footpath</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>footprints</value></Data>
