  <Placemark>
    <name>Back River Bistro Wiscasset ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Back River Bistro<br/><br/>📍 65 Gardiner Rd, Wiscasset, ME<br/><br/>A gastropub built around supporting local farms, fisheries, and foragers, with a seasonal menu that shifts to match what's actually available. Known for fresh oysters on the half shell, calamari, mushroom toast, and heartier plates like pork schnitzel, duck, half chicken with delicata and apple cider glaze, and short rib with potato pavé and gremolata. Crafted cocktails round out the menu. Rated 4.6 on Tripadvisor, ranked around #8 of 23 Wiscasset restaurants.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Oysters on the half shell<br/>- Calamari<br/>- Short rib with potato pavé, soubise, and potato chip gremolata<br/>- Half chicken with delicata, parsnip, and apple cider glaze<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open Tuesday–Saturday, 4:30pm–9pm only — no lunch service, and closed Sunday/Monday.<br/>- Plan for $60–70/person — this is a real dinner-out price point, not a casual stop.<br/>- Menu is genuinely seasonal, so don't expect the same dishes twice across a trip.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.backriverbistro.com/]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
