  <Placemark>
    <name>Bagaduce Lunch Penobscot ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bagaduce Lunch<br/><br/>📍 145 Franks Flat Rd, Penobscot, ME<br/><br/>A takeout stand at the outlet of the Bagaduce River, started in 1946 by Sydney and Berniece Snow and still family-run four generations later. Picnic tables sit on a grassy hill overlooking the water. Rated around 4.6 on Google and by the local Chamber of Commerce — note that individual review-platform scores vary wildly here (one aggregator shows a very low outlier that doesn't match the qualitative reviews at all), so trust the Google/Chamber figures over any single outlier.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Lobster roll<br/>- Shoestring onion rings — specifically and repeatedly called out as a highlight<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- On the Blue Hill peninsula, a genuine detour off the main coastal route — worth building into a day that also includes Blue Hill itself.<br/>- Simple, no-frills operation — go for the food and the river view, not amenities.<br/>- Fair prices and quick service per reviews, consistent with its long-running family-operation reputation.]]></description>
