  <Placemark>
    <name>Baker Forest Newcastle ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Baker Forest<br/><br/>📍 River Road, Newcastle, ME (~1.5 mi south of Route 1, small pull-off)<br/><br/>165-acre forest (donated 2003) with rocky ridges, old grazing land, a beaver-active lowland stream, and large hemlocks/white pines — including a visible storm-damage area from a past microburst. ~1.75 mi of trails, 285 ft cumulative gain.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Small 2-3 car pull-off on River Road — arrive flexible on parking<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/baker-forest/]]></description>
