  <Placemark>
    <name>Baker Island Lighthouse Southwest Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Baker Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Baker Island, Cranberry Isles, ME (part of Acadia National Park)<br/><br/>William Gilley, who settled Baker Island with his family in 1812, became the first keeper when the lighthouse was established in 1828. The original rubblestone tower proved structurally unsound and was rebuilt in 1855 with a 45-foot brick tower and Fresnel lens. Deactivated in 1955, briefly reactivated, and transferred to the National Park Service in 1958. The original lens is on display at the Fisherman's Museum at Pemaquid Point.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds are open but the dwelling and tower are closed to visitors.<br/>- Reached by boat tour (limited availability) or seen from an aerial tour out of Bar Harbor/Southwest Harbor.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
