  <Placemark>
    <name>Bald Mountain Preserve Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bald Mountain Preserve<br/><br/>📍 325 Barnestown Rd, Camden, ME<br/><br/>584 acres taking hikers above treeline to a 1,280 ft summit with views over western Penobscot Bay — home to some of the Midcoast's largest rare subalpine natural communities. The trail connects into the Ragged Mountain network. 1.3 mi one-way, difficult, 660 ft elevation gain.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Rocky footpath, real elevation gain — not a casual stroll<br/>- Connects directly to the Ragged Mountain trail network for a longer combined hike<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
