  <Placemark>
    <name>Bald Rock Mountain Lincolnville ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bald Rock Mountain<br/><br/>📍 Youngtown Road, Lincolnville ME (Camden Hills State Park, north entrance)<br/><br/>An 844-foot summit in the northern part of Camden Hills State Park, accessed from the Lincolnville side via Youngtown Road. AllTrails' most popular route to it carries a 4.7-star average from over 1,700 reviews. Moderate difficulty with some steep stretches, open ledge summit views over Penobscot Bay.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The summit is an open ledge with a real view drop-off, though it's not an iron-rung or narrow-exposure trail — worth weighing given vertigo sensitivity, but much milder than Beehive/Precipice.<br/>- A quieter alternative to Mount Battie with fewer crowds, from the same park system.<br/>- Parking lot on Youngtown Road, just off Route 173 (Beach Road).]]></description>
