  <Placemark>
    <name>Baltic Kitchen Littleton NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Overview<br/>Type: Polish restaurant  <br/>Best known for: Cozy atmosphere, delicious pierogis  <br/>Location context: Mountain-town vibe  <br/>Price level: $10–20 per person  <br/>Visit timing: Not mentioned  <br/><br/>Typical Customers  <br/>Demographics: Not mentioned  <br/>Group types: Couples, families, friends  <br/>Common occasions: Casual dinner, quick bite  <br/><br/>Vibe & Setting  <br/>Atmosphere: Cozy  <br/>Noise level: Moderate  <br/>Decor & setting: Indoor seating, warm ambiance  <br/>Service style: Friendly and attentive  <br/><br/>Recommended Dishes  <br/>Overall dish consensus  <br/>Reviewers strongly recommend the pierogis, kielbasa, and borscht as must-try items, praising their flavor and comforting nature.<br/><br/>How “top dishes” are determined  <br/>Top dishes are selected based on their frequent mentions and strong praise in reviews, as well as their appearance in restaurant photos.<br/><br/>| Rank | Dish              | Why it stands out                                                   | How often it’s mentioned                     | Ideal for            |<br/>|------|-------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|----------------------|<br/>| 1    | Pierogis         | Top tier flavor, comforting texture.                              | Repeatedly called out as a favorite.      | Sharing at the table  |<br/>| 2    | Kielbasa         | Incredible taste and quality.                                    | Mentioned in many reviews.                 | Hearty main          |<br/>| 3    | Borscht          | Scrumptious and highly praised in reviews.                       | Appears in numerous photos.                | Lighter option       |<br/><br/>Good alternates / backup choices<br/>- Tomato bisque: Notable for its warmth and flavor.<br/><br/>Highlights (non‑dish positives from reviews)  <br/>Atmosphere: Customers mention a cozy vibe that enhances the dining experience.  <br/>Service: Staff are described as very kind and attentive.  <br/><br/>Common Issues (from reviews)  <br/>None mentioned.  <br/><br/>Practical Notes  <br/>Reservation / wait: Not mentioned  <br/>Accessibility: Not mentioned  <br/>Parking / transit: Not mentioned  <br/>Best use case: Great for casual dinners with family or friends.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Baltic+Kitchen/@44.2991186,-71.7722191,7702m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m15!1m8!3m7!1s0x4cb469b6187f15c7:0xa9594392bb590b7f!2sLittleton,+NH+03561!3b1!8m2!3d44.3060969!4d-71.7703012!16zL20vMDFtOTV0!3m5!1s0x4cb46f0004d8f049:0xf1873aa650f084b0!8m2!3d44.3011969!4d-71.7684113!16s%2Fg%2F11m64zkwj7?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMy4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
