  <Placemark>
    <name>Banh Appetit Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bánh Appétit<br/><br/>📍 171 Cumberland Avenue, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Bánh Appétit is a family-run Vietnamese banh mi shop in Portland's Bayside neighborhood. The Infatuation named it one of the 13 Best Bánh Mì in America — high praise for a small counter window.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Lemongrass chicken bánh mì — fragrant, tender, and loaded<br/>- Beef bánh mì — a classic done perfectly on a crisp baguette<br/>- Pho — rich and authentic, rarely found this good outside a major city<br/>- Vermicelli noodle bowls for a lighter option<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Pickup only — no interior dining; small tables outside<br/>- Order ahead if possible — it gets busy at peak lunch hours<br/>- Generous portions at very reasonable prices<br/>- A short walk from downtown; worth the detour for the best bánh mì in Maine<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Banh+Appetit,+171+Cumberland+Ave,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
