  <Placemark>
    <name>Bar Harbor Historical Society La Rochelle ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bar Harbor Historical Society (La Rochelle)<br/><br/>📍 127 West Street, Bar Harbor, ME<br/><br/>Housed in La Rochelle, one of West Street's Gilded Age summer "cottages," the Historical Society runs guided tours of the mansion, maintains local archives, and hosts educational programming on Bar Harbor's history — from its cottage-era heyday through the devastating 1947 fire.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open seasonally, late May through October — check hours before visiting off-season.<br/>- A good way to see one of West Street's grand cottages from the inside, not just from the sidewalk.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3877%2C%20-68.2130]]></description>
