  <Placemark>
    <name>Bar Island Bar Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bar Island<br/><br/>📍 Bar Harbor ME<br/><br/>A small island connected to Bar Harbor's town pier by a natural gravel bar that appears at low tide and disappears completely at high tide. Walk across the bar, explore the forested island trails, and watch the tide return around you. The bar is exposed for roughly 3 hours on either side of low tide. Views back to Bar Harbor and across Frenchman Bay from the summit.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Check the tide table before going — the bar is fully covered at high tide and you will be stranded.<br/>- The Bar Harbor tide chart is posted at the town pier and available at any hotel.<br/>- The summit trail through the woods takes about 20 minutes and offers views back over the harbor.<br/>- This is a free, unhurried, quintessentially Maine experience requiring nothing but timing.]]></description>
