  <Placemark>
    <name>Bard College Annandale-on-Hudson NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bard College<br/><br/>📍 30 Campus Rd, Annandale-on-Hudson, NY 12504<br/><br/>Now coed, Bard College was originally founded in 1860 as an Episcopal men's school. In 1933 it was renamed for its founder, John Bard, grandson of Dr. Samuel Bard, physician to George Washington and Benjamin Franklin. A variety of architectural styles found within its boundaries includes the English Gothic Collegiate Chapel of the Holy Innocents, 18th-century Dutch vernacular stone farmhouses, and a ca. 1900 Georgian Revival mansion.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Stop 12 of 33 on the Rhinebeck, Red Hook & Milan Scenic Tour (Tour 1) — see also the Richard B. Fisher Center for the Performing Arts (stop 13) and Montgomery Place (stop 10), both on the same campus.]]></description>
