  <Placemark>
    <name>Barrett Park Boothbay ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Barrett Park<br/><br/>📍 131 Lobster Cove Road, Boothbay Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A 10-acre public waterfront park on Lewis Cove, in continuous use for community events since 1977 — reunions, weddings, and picnics still happen here under its gazebo. It's a genuine locals' park rather than a tourist stop: a small beach for swimming, wading, or launching a kayak, an expansive lawn for games, a memorial garden, granite benches, and shade trees along a rocky shoreline.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open 6am–9pm daily.<br/>- Dog-friendly, with real beach access — a good option if you need a break from harbor crowds with a dog in tow.<br/>- Bring a kayak or paddleboard; the cove is calm and well-suited to launching directly from the beach.<br/>- No food/concessions on site — pack a picnic if you're staying a while.]]></description>
