  <Placemark>
    <name>Bass Harbor Head Light and Lopaus Point Mount Desert ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bass Harbor Head Light & Lopaus Point<br/><br/>📍 Southwest tip, Mount Desert Island, ME<br/><br/>On the southwest tip of Mount Desert Island, the Bass Harbor Head Light is a popular photo spot—but the real hidden gem is nearby. Explore the dirt tracks leading toward Lopaus Point and Mitchell Cove for peaceful beachcombing and coastal exploration away from the lighthouse photo lines.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Lighthouse is picturesque but crowded during peak season<br/>- Head beyond the main viewpoint for quieter explorations<br/>- Dirt tracks and paths explore the rocky coast<br/>- Tide pools and shells to discover<br/>- Dramatic pink granite formations like elsewhere on the island<br/>- Sunset views are particularly stunning<br/>- Bring sturdy shoes for rocky terrain]]></description>
