  <Placemark>
    <name>Bass Harbor Head Lighthouse Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bass Harbor Head Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Acadia National Park ME<br/><br/>The most photographed lighthouse in Maine, perched on pink granite ledges at the remote southwest corner of Mount Desert Island. The classic image — red-shuttered white tower above orange-streaked granite boulders — is at its best at sunset, when the light catches the granite and the lighthouse glows against the darkening forest. Easy 5-minute walk from the parking area.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Arrive 45–60 minutes before sunset for the best light on the rocks.<br/>- A narrow path descends to the granite ledges below the light — the best camera angle.<br/>- The quiet drive around the western side of the island through Bass Harbor and Bernard village is worth the trip on its own.<br/>- Combine with a meal in Southwest Harbor or a visit to Quietside Cafe on the return.]]></description>
