  <Placemark>
    <name>Bass Rock Preserve Round Pond ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bass Rock Preserve<br/><br/>📍 235 Back Shore Road, Round Pond, ME<br/><br/>10-acre preserve (1973/2009) with views of Muscongus Bay and Friendship's islands — a fern-lined trail leads to a rocky beach and a curious ~2-3 ft round hole worn into exposed ledge. Short, ~0.3-0.4 mi, 70 ft gain.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Quick stop — good pairing with a Round Pond village walk<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/bass-rock-preserve/]]></description>
