  <Placemark>
    <name>Baxter Building Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Baxter Building<br/><br/>📍 619 Congress Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Designed by local architect Francis Fassett, the Baxter Building at 619 Congress Street showcases the Romanesque Revival style of architecture. Built in the late 1800s, it served as the Portland Public Library until 1978.<br/><br/>The building sat vacant for several years until it was purchased by Maine College of Art and Design (MECA&D) in 1983. MECA&D sold the building in 2010 and today it houses VIA, a full-service marketing and advertising agency.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/619+Congress+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
