  <Placemark>
    <name>Bear Notch Bartlett NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bear Notch Road<br/><br/>📍 Connecting the Kancamagus Highway to Route 302, Bartlett, NH<br/><br/>A 9-mile seasonal road cutting from the Kancamagus (above Lower Falls and Rocky Gorge) north to Route 302 in Bartlett, through the Bartlett Experimental Forest — a research site for northern hardwood forest studies. Several roadside pull-offs offer expansive White Mountain National Forest views, especially striking during foliage season.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Closed in winter (unmaintained, becomes a snowmobile trail) — only the first mile of the southern end stays open, leading to the Upper Nanamocomuck Ski Trail.<br/>- A good detour to connect a Kancamagus drive with a Route 302/Crawford Notch leg without backtracking.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0434%2C%20-71.3148]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
