  <Placemark>
    <name>Beauchamp Point Preserve Rockport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Beauchamp Point Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Tip of Beauchamp Point, Rockport, ME — water access only, no land route (coordinate approximate — no published GPS pin found, estimated from "just before Indian Island")<br/><br/>A 9-acre headland beach preserve with over 600 ft of shorefront, the longest undeveloped stretch on the eastern side of Rockport Harbor. The gravel-and-rock shoreline is accessible at all tides and makes an ideal picnic stopover on a paddle from Rockport to Camden. No camping or campfires. Donated 2000 by Charles and Mary Chatfield.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Water access only — no land route exists via Beauchamp Point Rd<br/>- ~1.4 mi paddle from Rockport Marine Park (93 Pascal Ave), where there's a public boat launch<br/>- Coordinate is an estimate — no exact GPS pin was found published anywhere; verify locally<br/>- Distinct from the "Beauchamp Point" bike/walk loop route already in this vault — same name, different thing (a road loop vs. this paddle-access preserve)<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org/preserves/beauchamp-point-preserve/]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
