  <Placemark>
    <name>Beauchamp Point Rockport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Beauchamp Point<br/><br/>📍 Rockport, ME<br/><br/>8.4-mile moderate loop starting/ending in Rockport, out to Beauchamp Point — harbor views along the way, coastal vistas at the point itself. Popular for both biking and walking.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- No aggregated numeric rating found across major review platforms — described qualitatively as well-regarded, not independently scored like a restaurant.<br/>- Reddit's specific rec was biking this loop as an activity, paired with kayaking to Curtis Island (already in the vault) the same day.<br/>- Not the same as Beauchamp Point Preserve — a small, separate, water-access-only Coastal Mountains Land Trust preserve at the actual tip of the point, a different thing from this road/path loop]]></description>
