  <Placemark>
    <name>Beckys Diner Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Becky's Diner<br/><br/>📍 390 Commercial Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Becky's Diner is a Portland institution on the working waterfront at 390 Commercial Street. Open from 4am daily (open 363 days a year), it has fueled generations of fishermen, dock workers, and hungry visitors. It is ranked #10 of 440 Portland restaurants on TripAdvisor with over 2,725 reviews.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Lobster roll — classic, generously loaded, priced fairly for the waterfront<br/>- Clam chowder — briny, honest, and deeply satisfying<br/>- Irish Benedict — grilled muffin, crispy hash, perfectly poached eggs, tangy hollandaise; a lunch and brunch staple<br/>- Fried clams — a crowd favorite<br/>- Blueberry pie — Maine-made, worth saving room for<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Ask for the rooftop patio in warm weather for harbor views<br/>- Open early — great for a late breakfast/early lunch before hitting the waterfront<br/>- Expect a wait on weekends; locals go early on weekdays<br/>- Cash and card accepted; fast, friendly counter-style service<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Becky's+Diner,+390+Commercial+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-red</styleUrl>
