  <Placemark>
    <name>Beech Cliff Trail Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Beech Cliff Trail<br/><br/>📍 Echo Lake Beach parking area, Acadia National Park ME<br/><br/>A moderately challenging ~1.7-mile loop on the "quiet side" of Mount Desert Island, near Southwest Harbor. Four iron-rung ladders (three of them back-to-back near the top) climb the cliffs above Echo Lake, opening up to sweeping views of the lake and the ocean beyond — a less-crowded alternative to Beehive/Precipice with similar iron-rung exposure.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Not suitable for small children, anyone afraid of heights, or anyone unsteady on their feet — genuinely exposed in sections<br/>- Sometimes closed March 15–August 15 for peregrine falcon nesting — check current conditions before going<br/>- Trailhead is at the north end of the Echo Lake Beach parking loop<br/>- Often paired with the Canada Cliff loop for a longer outing]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
