  <Placemark>
    <name>Beech Hill Preserve</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-10T09:45:00<br/><br/>Beech Hill Preserve<br/><br/>Summit Road Trail — 0.75 mi each way / 1.5 mi round trip, easy — climbs gently through blueberry barrens to "Beech Nut," a historic 1913 sod-roof stone hut at the summit with panoramic views over Penobscot Bay. One of the best short, easy hikes on the whole Camden–Wiscasset corridor.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free admission, open 9am–5pm daily.<br/>- Longer option: Woods Loop Trail, ~1.9 mi, still easy, more elevation gain through forest.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Beech+Hill+Preserve/@44.1659581,-69.2106881,18827m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m11!1m3!2m2!1sscenic+spot!6e1!3m6!1s0x4cadd0c19e11c51b:0x770a32480499b65a!8m2!3d44.1659581!4d-69.0978767!15sCgtzY2VuaWMgc3BvdFoNIgtzY2VuaWMgc3BvdJIBD25hdHVyZV9wcmVzZXJ2ZZoBI0NoWkRTVWhOTUc5blMwVkpRMEZuU1VSS056WlhTMkpCRUFF4AEA-gEECAAQQg!16s%2Fg%2F11clw07zjf?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDcxMy4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
