    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Belfast Footbridge ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Belfast Footbridge<br/><br/>The Belfast Footbridge, also called the Armistice Bridge in some local descriptions, is one of the defining pedestrian features of the waterfront. City information describes it as part of the larger Harbor Walk and Rail Trail corridor running along the waterfront and up the Passagassawakeag River.[cite:73]<br/><br/>Its appeal lies in the elevated vantage point it gives over the river, harbor, and bay. It also functions as a practical connector, linking scenic walking routes and making the waterfront easier to explore on foot.[cite:70][cite:73]]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Footpath</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>footprints</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>green</value></Data>
