      <coordinates>-69.00824230342724,44.43223453788778,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Belfast Harborwalk ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Belfast Harborwalk<br/><br/>The Belfast Harbor Walk is a paved waterfront path that follows the harbor shore beginning near Front Street Shipyard. Maine’s MidCoast & Islands describes it as a one-mile, wheelchair-accessible walkway that connects harbor views, gardens, and easy access to downtown Belfast’s historic brick buildings and sea-captains’ houses.[cite:67]<br/><br/>Other local descriptions emphasize how flat and approachable the route is, making it well suited to a casual stroll rather than a strenuous hike. The walk also passes working waterfront activity, which gives visitors a feel for Belfast as both a scenic town and an active marine community.[cite:70][cite:73]]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Beach</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>waves</value></Data>
