      <coordinates>-69.00683187972298,44.42892066447699,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Belfast Historical Society &amp; Museum ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Belfast Historical Society & Museum<br/><br/>The Belfast Historical Society & Museum focuses on preserving and interpreting the city’s local history. Visit Maine describes exhibits that include maritime material, ship models, and objects connected to everyday civic life, while noting the museum’s location in a Federal-style brick building on Market Street.[cite:31]<br/><br/>One especially distinctive feature is the adjacent barn, which contains the old jail and a historic hearse. That combination gives the museum a strong sense of place and helps it present Belfast history through original local structures as well as artifacts.[cite:31][cite:34]]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Attraction</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>landmark</value></Data>
