    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Belfast Rail Trail ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Belfast Rail Trail<br/><br/>The Belfast Rail Trail extends the waterfront experience beyond downtown and follows the Passagassawakeag River on a gentle multi-use path. The City of Belfast highlights it as part of a scenic corridor used for strolling, jogging, dog walking, and bicycle riding.[cite:73]<br/><br/>Its main strength is accessibility: the route is easy to follow, visually pleasant, and integrated with the Harbor Walk and Footbridge. For visitors, it offers a simple way to experience Belfast’s natural setting without needing a car once already in town.[cite:73][cite:34]<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Runs from the Armistice Bridge footbridge on the waterfront to the City Point Railroad yard, connecting to the 47-mi Hills to Sea Trail toward Unity<br/>- Passes right by Stephenson Preserve and Pendleton Park's mountain-bike trails — easy to string together a longer outing<br/>- Parking at the trail's terminus, at City Point, and at the Upper Bridge lot near the midpoint<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Footpath</value></Data>
