      <coordinates>-69.0065207,44.4261759,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Belknap Mill Laconia NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Belknap Mill<br/><br/>📍 Laconia, NH (Mill Plaza, downtown)<br/><br/>Built in 1823 and fully operational by 1828, Belknap Mill is the oldest largely unaltered brick textile mill in the country. It converted from weaving to knitting during the Civil War — one of the first mills in the nation to do so — and kept producing hosiery until 1969. By 1890 it had grown to include spinning, dyeing, and knitting buildings, a boiler room, and a machine shop. Now run by the nonprofit Belknap Mill Society as a museum, gallery, and event space, and designated New Hampshire's Official Meetinghouse.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Combine with a walk along the Winnipesaukee River and the adjacent Opechee Bay waterfront.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.5278%2C%20-71.4687]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
