  <Placemark>
    <name>Benjamin Aldrich Homestead Colebrook NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Benjamin Aldrich Homestead<br/><br/>📍 Aldrich Road, near Piper Hill, Colebrook, NH<br/><br/>Colebrook's oldest surviving farm property, and the town's last fully intact 19th-century farmstead. Benjamin Aldrich bought the land in 1844; the ell and barn went up in 1846–47, and in 1861 the main house block was added, with the older house rotated and attached to its south side. The property stayed in Aldrich family hands, seeing continuous agricultural use, until 1988. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2003.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Private property — a drive-past historical landmark rather than a stop with public access.<br/>- A short distance from the Poore Family Homestead, another well-preserved Colebrook-area farmstead.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.9276%2C%20-71.4833]]></description>
