  <Placemark>
    <name>Berlin Wall Long Wharf Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Berlin Wall Long Wharf<br/><br/>Long Wharf is privately owned by the DiMillo family but is open to the public year-round. Walk past a variety of public art installations and historic monuments — including a section of the Berlin Wall.<br/><br/>From Long Wharf you can access many boat tours and read about the history of the DiMillo family and their famous floating restaurant.<br/><br/>Highlights<br/>- Original section of the Berlin Wall<br/>- Public art installations along the pier<br/>- Boat tour embarkation point<br/>- History of the DiMillo family displayed on site<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free to walk and visit anytime<br/>- Connects to the Harborwalk Trail along Commercial Street<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Long+Wharf,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
