  <Placemark>
    <name>Birch Harbor The Anvil Buck Cove Scenic Drive Winter Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[View on AllTrails<br/><br/>Birch Harbor, the Anvil & Buck Cove Scenic Drive<br/><br/>📍 Schoodic Loop Road, Winter Harbor, ME (Schoodic Peninsula, Acadia National Park)<br/><br/>A 13.1-mile loop drive around the Schoodic Peninsula — the mainland section of Acadia National Park, far less trafficked than Mount Desert Island. The roadway itself delivers views of Winter Harbor, coastal islands, Buck Cove, and Schoodic Harbor, with numerous pull-offs and short hikes accessible right from the road for anyone who wants to stretch their legs. Popular with both scenic drivers and road cyclists.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- An Acadia entrance pass is required.<br/>- Dogs welcome on leash.<br/>- Combine with dedicated stops already in this vault along the same loop — Schoodic Point, Schoodic Head, and Schoodic Woods Campground — rather than treating this as a separate outing.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.alltrails.com/trail/us/maine/birch-harbor-the-anvil-buck-cove]]></description>
