    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Bite Into Maine Cape Elizabeth ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bite Into Maine<br/><br/>📍 1000 Shore Rd, Fort Williams Park, Cape Elizabeth, ME<br/><br/>A food truck operating April–November inside Fort Williams Park, with Portland Head Light as scenery — genuinely one of the best settings of any lobster roll in Maine. Serves six different styles of lobster roll, both traditional and inventive, made with lobster that's always fresh, never frozen. Named one of America's Greatest Lobster Rolls by Food & Wine, and featured on both the Food Network and Netflix. Rated 4.8 on Tripadvisor, #1 of 10 restaurants in Cape Elizabeth.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Maine roll — the classic, mayo and chives<br/>- Connecticut roll — served warm with hot butter, a real point of difference from the standard Maine style<br/>- Whoopie pies for dessert<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Seasonal only (April–November) — it's a food truck, not a year-round building.<br/>- Combine with a walk to Portland Head Light itself — it's right there in the same park.<br/>- Order and eat outdoors; there's no indoor seating, so check the weather.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.bringfido.com/restaurant/13410]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
