  <Placemark>
    <name>Black Friar Inn &amp; Pub Bar Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[What It Is & What It's Best Known For<br/><br/>Black Friar Inn & Pub is a charming bed & breakfast and restaurant housed in a historic structure on Summer Street in Bar Harbor, Maine. The property features salvaged woodwork from 1800s mansions and is tucked away on a quiet side street just off Main Street. The venue operates as both a lodging establishment and a casual dining spot, with a well-regarded pub serving cocktails, seafood, and creative entrées.<br/><br/>Typical Customers<br/><br/>The establishment attracts a diverse clientele: overnight guests seeking a cozy, historic B&B experience; couples and small groups dining out for dinner or happy hour; professionals visiting town for work; and tourists exploring Bar Harbor. Guests range from those seeking upscale-casual dining to casual happy-hour visitors. The atmosphere welcomes relaxed, friendly visitors; the owners note in reviews that those who aren't "entitled feeling" will enjoy the experience.<br/><br/>Overall Vibe<br/><br/>Intimate, cozy, and charming with a lived-in historic character. The restaurant side is casual and welcoming, with a relaxed service style that feels genuine rather than formal. Rooms are described as small but quaint, with unique details like spiral staircases and turret rooms. The energy is lively during happy hour and dinner service but maintains the quiet charm of a historic property. Decidedly upscale-casual rather than budget or high-end fine dining.<br/><br/>Strongest Positives (from reviews)<br/><br/>1. Exceptional seafood and cocktails – Multiple guests consistently praise the oysters (particularly the $2 happy-hour oysters), mussels, haddock fish & chips, lobster chimis, and house-made tartar sauce. Fresh, high-quality ingredients are a standout.<br/>    <br/>2. Outstanding hospitality and staff – Reviewers repeatedly highlight the kindness and attentiveness of specific staff members (Jamie, Allie, Julia, Brian) and owners Steve and his wife. Staff are described as friendly, knowledgeable, and genuinely welcoming. The owners are noted as accommodating, even shifting rooms when guests had flight cancellations.<br/>    <br/>3. Excellent breakfast included with stays – Guests emphasize the full breakfast menu as a major draw, with portions so substantial that some guests "rarely needed lunch." Breakfast quality is celebrated as a differentiator.<br/>    <br/>4. Hidden gem status with distinctive charm – The off-Main-Street location, historic character, cozy atmosphere, and unique décor (salvaged woodwork, turret rooms, spiral staircases) make it feel special and memorable. Reviewers repeatedly call it a "must-stop" and "hidden gem."<br/>    <br/><br/>Most Common Issues or Downsides (from reviews)<br/><br/>1. Small rooms – Multiple guests note that rooms are small, though they describe them as "quaint" and "pretty." This is clearly a trade-off of the historic property; guests who appreciate character seem unbothered, but those seeking spacious accommodations may be disappointed.<br/>    <br/>2. Limited and old establishment – One reviewer described it as "a very old and small establishment" and noted "it's not great shakes," suggesting some guests may find the modest scale and historic nature underwhelming compared to larger, more modern hotels.<br/>    <br/>3. Off-the-beaten-path location – While presented as an asset by many reviewers ("hidden gem"), the location off Main Street may be a downside for those seeking walkable proximity to town's main attractions or who prefer high-visibility establishments.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Black+Friar+Inn+%26+Pub/@44.3886138,-68.2123984,594m/data=!3m2!1e3!5s0x4caebf79398c221d:0x760efaa8d0294f9f!4m21!1m7!3m6!1s0x4caebf005b379c81:0xc72ad7b501a68b23!2sDinner!8m2!3d44.3886633!4d-68.2140236!16s%2Fg%2F11vxy0p6s6!3m12!1s0x4caebf7c1a90a0f9:0x92af9849f52ea2e6!5m4!1s2026-09-21!2i4!4m1!1i2!8m2!3d44.3893024!4d-68.2101896!9m1!1b1!16s%2Fg%2F1vd70y24?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
