  <Placemark>
    <name>Blue Hill Farmers Market Blue Hill ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Blue Hill Farmers' Market<br/><br/>📍 Blue Hill Fairgrounds, 233 Ellsworth Road, Blue Hill, ME 04614<br/><br/>One of Maine's oldest farmers' markets, held at the Blue Hill Fairgrounds — the same grounds as the well-known Blue Hill Fair. During the Fair itself (late Aug–mid Sept), the market temporarily relocates to the Down East Family YMCA before returning to the Fairgrounds for the rest of the fall.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Saturdays, 9–11:30 AM, year-round schedule broken into three stretches (confirmed directly via bluehillfarmersmarket.com): May 23–Aug 22 at the Fairgrounds, Aug 29–Sep 12 at the Down East Family YMCA (Lawrence Family Fitness Center) during the Blue Hill Fair, then Sep 19–Oct 31 back at the Fairgrounds<br/>- Dogs (other than service animals) aren't allowed at the Fairgrounds location per facility policy<br/>- SNAP accepted<br/>- Combine with a stop in Blue Hill proper, or with Aldermere Farm-style farm visits elsewhere on the peninsula<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Blue+Hill+Fairgrounds+233+Ellsworth+Road+Blue+Hill+ME]]></description>
