  <Placemark>
    <name>Blue Horizons Preserve Bar Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[View website<br/><br/>Blue Horizons Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Indian Point Rd, Town Hill, Bar Harbor ME (~15 min from downtown Bar Harbor)<br/><br/>An 82-acre Maine Coast Heritage Trust preserve on the quiet western side of Mount Desert Island, donated to MCHT in 2010. A gravel path runs gently downhill through the forest, with a compact ~1.5-mile trail system converging at a cobble beach on Clark Cove — quiet, uncrowded, and a genuine change of pace from the busier Park Loop Road side of the island.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Coordinates are approximate — Town Hill area; parking is roadside near a locked gate marked with an MCHT sign on Indian Point Road, worth confirming the exact pull-off before you go<br/>- Camping and fires not permitted; foot traffic only<br/>- Some sources note a possible seasonal restriction around the preserve's buildings (roughly May–October) even though the trail itself is described as open year-round — worth a quick check with MCHT if visiting in that window<br/>- No parking fee<br/><br/>More info: https://www.mcht.org/preserve/blue-horizons/]]></description>
