  <Placemark>
    <name>Boathouse Bistro Boothbay Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Boathouse Bistro<br/><br/>📍 12 By-Way, Boothbay Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A three-story harborfront restaurant right in downtown Boothbay Harbor — a cozy first-floor dining room, a second-floor tavern, and a third-floor open-air deck with panoramic harbor views. The menu runs 80+ dishes across tapas-style small plates and full entrées, blending Maine coastal traditions (locally caught seafood, organic meats, seasonal vegetables) with internationally inspired flavors, and covers vegan, vegetarian, and gluten-free well. Rated 4.4 on Tripadvisor, ranked around #9 of 46 Boothbay Harbor restaurants — one of the stronger reviewed spots in town.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Tapas plates — the menu's real strength; order several to share rather than a single entrée<br/>- Haddock sandwich — repeatedly praised for its size and how well the fish is cooked<br/>- Fresh local seafood entrées generally — reviewers consistently note perfectly prepared, fresh preparations<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Request rooftop (3rd floor) seating for the best harbor views — go early or reserve ahead, it's the most requested spot in the building.<br/>- Prices are moderate for a harbor-view restaurant in this town — not the premium you'd expect given the setting.<br/>- Good option if part of your group wants a full dinner and part wants to graze tapas-style.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-red</styleUrl>
