  <Placemark>
    <name>Boise Rock Franconia Notch NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Boise Rock<br/><br/>📍 Franconia Notch Parkway (I-93), northbound side<br/><br/>A large glacial boulder with a local survival legend: in the early 1800s, teamster Thomas Boise was caught in a massive snowstorm mid-Notch and took shelter under this rock. Facing a fatal night, he killed his horse and wrapped himself in its hide to survive until a rescue party found him the next morning.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A quick roadside pull-off with an interpretive sign — a two-minute stop, not a hike.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.1533%2C%20-71.6780]]></description>
