  <Placemark>
    <name>Bond Beach Park Laconia NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bond Beach Park<br/><br/>📍 Laconia, NH (Opechee Bay)<br/><br/>A lakeside park on Opechee Bay with about 1,000 feet of shoreline, including a lifeguarded swimming beach of soft, light-colored sand. Picnic areas, restrooms/changing rooms, and fishing access round out the park; most of the parcel stays undeveloped for nature walks and cross-country skiing in winter.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Access requires a beach pass, available from the Laconia City Clerk's office — primarily for residents/taxpayers, so check current visitor policy before planning around it.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.5548%2C%20-71.4766]]></description>
