  <Placemark>
    <name>Boon Island Lighthouse York ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Boon Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Boon Island, ~9.5 miles offshore from York, ME<br/><br/>The tallest lighthouse in New England at 133 feet, with a second-order Fresnel lens. Established in 1811, the current granite tower dates to 1855. It endured a devastating 1898 storm that coated the dwelling and tower in thick layers of ice, and was automated after the Blizzard of 1978. The original Fresnel lens is now displayed at the Kittery Historical and Naval Museum.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned, no access without permission — best viewed by boat or plane.<br/>- Distant views are possible from Cape Neddick (Nubble) Lighthouse; New England Eco Adventures runs cruises past it.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
