  <Placemark>
    <name>Boynton-McKay Food Company Camden ME (BAGEL SHOP)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[⚠️ Boynton-McKay Food Company — CLOSED<br/><br/>📍 30 Main St, Camden, ME (former location)<br/><br/>This restaurant has closed. It was a genuine Camden institution — the building was originally an 1890s pharmacy, and the restaurant itself operated there for roughly 15 years before selling. It was voted best breakfast in Maine by Food Network Magazine and known for chocolate chip pancakes and made-from-scratch comfort food. Reporting around the sale indicated a Bagel Cafe was expected to take over the same Main Street space — but that report is dated, so verify what's actually operating at 30 Main St before planning a visit, rather than assuming either name is currently open.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Do not build a breakfast plan around this name — confirm current status first.<br/>- If a bagel shop or other new tenant is now at 30 Main St, it may be worth a look on its own merits, but it isn't the same business this note originally described.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-red</styleUrl>
