  <Placemark>
    <name>Brady's Boothbay Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Brady's<br/><br/>📍 25 Union St, Boothbay Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A newer arrival (opened in the current wave of Boothbay openings) that quickly earned a spot on Downeast readers' list of Maine's best new restaurants. The building is clean and spacious with nautical-rustic charm, a real harbor view, and outdoor seating — comfort food done well rather than fine dining. Rated 4.4 on Tripadvisor, ranked around #21 of 46 Boothbay Harbor restaurants.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Fish & chips — called out repeatedly for generous portions and quality<br/>- Lobster mac & cheese — a fan favorite on the menu<br/>- Massachusetts-style clam chowder — a distinct, thicker style worth trying alongside the classic New England chowders elsewhere on the harbor<br/>- Haddock BLT — a standout lunch pick, also served as haddock tacos<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Newer spot — book ahead during peak summer weekends.<br/>- Open Tuesday–Saturday 11:30am–8pm, Sunday 7:30am–4pm (brunch); closed Mondays.<br/>- Dinner runs $30–40/person, lunch $10–20 — solid value for the harbor.<br/>- Reach them directly at (207) 315-6555 or bradysboothbayharbor.com.]]></description>
