  <Placemark>
    <name>Branch Lake Public Forest Ellsworth ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Branch Lake Public Forest<br/><br/>📍 6.5 mi north of downtown Ellsworth (Main St/Rt 1A), then 1 mi to a gravel lot<br/><br/>Protects Ellsworth's sole drinking-water source — eastern Maine's largest coastal city relies on this lake. The lake loop trail (2.6 mi network) reaches the water at 1.3 mi. Protected 2010 via a partnership between Frenchman Bay Conservancy, the City of Ellsworth, Trust for Public Land, and Forest Society of Maine.]]></description>
