  <Placemark>
    <name>Brave The Flames Tannersville NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Overview<br/>Type: Restaurant<br/><br/>Best known for: Excellent burgers and vegan options.<br/><br/>Location context: Not mentioned.<br/><br/>Price level: $20–30 per person<br/><br/>Visit timing: Not mentioned.<br/><br/>Typical Customers<br/>Demographics: Mostly locals and groups.<br/><br/>Group types: Friends, families, larger groups.<br/><br/>Common occasions: Casual dinner, gatherings after skiing.<br/><br/>Vibe & Setting<br/>Atmosphere: Casual and welcoming.<br/><br/>Noise level: Moderate.<br/><br/>Decor & setting: Indoor seating with cozy ambiance.<br/><br/>Service style: Friendly and accommodating.<br/><br/>Recommended Dishes<br/>Overall dish consensus<br/>Reviewers recommend the burgers and vegan options, particularly the Black Bean Burger and vegan dishes such as the vegan smash burger.<br/><br/>How “top dishes” are determined<br/>Top dishes are chosen based solely on mentions in reviews and the menu, focusing on popularity and strong praise from customers.<br/><br/>| Rank | Dish                 | Why it stands out                                       | How often it’s mentioned          | Ideal for                  |<br/>|------|----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|----------------------------|<br/>| 1    | Black Bean Burger     | Praised for its flavor and satisfying portion size.   | Mentioned in many reviews.      | Hearty main option.       |<br/>| 2    | Vegan smash burger    | Noted as a standout for vegan diners.                  | Frequently highlighted.          | Lighter option for sharing.|<br/>| 3    | Vegan cheesesteak     | Loved for its taste and fulfilling quality.            | Appears in numerous photos.     | Comfort food.             |<br/><br/>Good alternates / backup choices<br/>- El Gringo Loco Salad: Known for its fresh ingredients and satisfying textures.<br/>- Hummus: Recommended for being a good starter option.<br/><br/>Highlights (non‑dish positives from reviews)<br/>Service: Many reviews mention the friendly and attentive staff, which enhances the dining experience.<br/><br/>Ambiance: The casual and cozy atmosphere makes it suitable for relaxed meals.<br/><br/>Common Issues (from reviews)<br/>Parking: Some customers note that parking can be confusing and limited during busy times.<br/><br/>Wait times: A few reviews mention long waits during peak hours, but the service remains attentive.<br/><br/>Practical Notes<br/>Reservation / wait: Walk-in friendly, but can get busy, especially during dinner.<br/><br/>Accessibility: Not mentioned.<br/><br/>Parking / transit: Street parking is available, but can be tricky.<br/><br/>Best use case: Ideal for groups looking for a casual dinner spot with great burgers.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Brave+The+Flames/@42.1921788,-74.1338275,1280m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m11!1m4!2m3!1sThai+Spice+Cafe+%E2%80%93+Well-liked+Thai+on+Raymond+Avenue!5m1!4e3!3m5!1s0x89ddad1f481249e1:0x7c36268c9a23e52f!8m2!3d42.1957858!4d-74.1367958!16s%2Fg%2F11vj5gb554?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMy4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
