  <Placemark>
    <name>Bridgewater Corners Bridge Bridgewater VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bridgewater Corners Bridge<br/><br/>📍 Route 100A, Bridgewater Corners, VT<br/><br/>A 111-foot, single-span steel Pratt through-truss bridge built in 1928 by the American Bridge Company following major flooding, carrying Route 100A over the Ottauquechee River just south of Route 4 and just east of the Long Trail Brewing Company. Despite the "Corners Bridge" name, it's steel construction, not a traditional wooden covered bridge. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1992.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Easy to pair with a stop (and a beer) at the neighboring Long Trail Brewing Company.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.5869%2C%20-72.6567]]></description>
