  <Placemark>
    <name>Bristol Falls Starksboro VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bristol Falls (Bartlett Falls)<br/><br/>📍 Lincoln Road, near Bristol, VT<br/><br/>Widely considered one of Vermont's most popular swimming holes. The New Haven River sheets over a bedrock shelf and plunges 14 feet into a deep pool ringed with ledges good for jumping; the falls are undercut enough that you can swim behind the curtain of water. About a quarter mile upstream is Circle Current, a quieter, less-visited swimming spot.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- From Bristol, drive east on Route 116/17 for 2.8 miles, then turn onto Lincoln Road — roadside parking appears about 0.2 miles along.<br/>- Popular and often crowded on hot summer days — arrive early.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.1310%2C%20-73.0330]]></description>
