  <Placemark>
    <name>Browns Head Lighthouse Vinalhaven ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Browns Head Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Vinalhaven Island, ME (Fox Islands Thoroughfare)<br/><br/>Established in 1832, with the current tower dating to 1857, guiding maritime traffic through the Fox Islands Thoroughfare between Vinalhaven and North Haven. Long a one-keeper family station — Stephen Baxter, born here in 1973, is believed to be the first (and likely last) baby born at a Coast Guard light station. Automated in 1987; transferred to the Friends of Browns Head Lighthouse in 2022.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Reach via the Rockland–Vinalhaven ferry; grounds are open but the dwelling and tower are closed to visitors.<br/>- Several miles from the ferry terminal — plan for a drive or bike ride once on the island.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
