  <Placemark>
    <name>Brunswick Farmers Market Brunswick ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Brunswick-Topsham Land Trust Farmers' Market<br/><br/>📍 277 Pleasant Hill Road, Brunswick, ME 04011<br/><br/>Run by the Brunswick-Topsham Land Trust on the conserved fields of Crystal Spring Farm, this is one of the larger and more polished markets on the Maine coast — over 40 vendors selling vegetables, fruit, dairy, meat, seafood, cut flowers, mushrooms, baked goods, and prepared foods, often with live music.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Saturdays, 8:30 AM–12:30 PM, first Saturday in May through the last Saturday in October<br/>- Large enough to make a full morning of it — bring cash for smaller vendors, though many take cards<br/>- On the way between Portland and midcoast Maine, so it pairs well with a stop in Bath<br/>- Not currently schedulable: the Portland base camp (Aug 3–5, Mon–Wed) has no Saturday in it, so `day` is intentionally left blank rather than forced onto a non-market day. Left as a researched candidate — revisit if the itinerary ever adds a Saturday near Portland/Brunswick.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Crystal+Spring+Farm+277+Pleasant+Hill+Road+Brunswick+ME]]></description>
