      <coordinates>-69.964,43.9148,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Bug Light Park South Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Bug Light Park<br/><br/>📍 Spring Point Drive, South Portland, ME (~10 min from downtown Portland)<br/><br/>Bug Light Park is a breezy open-air park at the tip of the Spring Point peninsula in South Portland, just across the harbor from Portland's Old Port. It's named for the Spring Point Ledge Lighthouse — a compact, cast-iron sparkplug lighthouse nicknamed "Bug Light" — that sits at the end of a 900-foot granite breakwater you can walk out onto.<br/><br/>The views here are exceptional: Portland Harbor and its working waterfront to the north, Portland Head Light visible to the south, and Casco Bay stretching out to the east. The walk from the parking area to the end of the breakwater and back is about 1.5–2 miles and completely flat.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The breakwater walk is the highlight — sturdy shoes recommended as the granite blocks are uneven<br/>- Bug Light is privately owned but the grounds and breakwater are public<br/>- The adjacent Southern Maine Community College waterfront adds more walking paths<br/>- Great spot to watch lobster boats, tankers, and ferries move through the harbor<br/>- Free parking in the lot off Spring Point Drive<br/>- Combine with Portland Head Light (~5 min drive) for a full Cape Elizabeth morning<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Bug+Light+Park/@43.6506,-70.2441,15z]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
