  <Placemark>
    <name>Burnt Coat Harbor Lighthouse Swans Island ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Burnt Coat Harbor Lighthouse (Hockamock Head)<br/><br/>📍 Swan's Island, ME<br/><br/>First lit August 15, 1872, this station uses two square brick range-light towers, the rear standing 75 feet above sea level. Keeper Frederick Alexander Allen's logbook — now in the National Archives — documents the station's early years, including heating lard oil through the brutal winter of 1874–75. Automated in 1975 and transferred to the Town of Swan's Island in 1994, with restoration beginning in 2006.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open in summer, Tuesday–Saturday, 11am–3pm.<br/>- Reach via the Swan's Island Ferry from Bass Harbor, then drive about 3.8 miles.<br/>- The keeper's house upstairs is a summer rental apartment.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
