  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Cabbage Island Clambakes Boothbay Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Cabbage Island Clambakes<br/><br/>📍 Ticket booth: Pier 6, Fisherman's Wharf Inn, 22 Commercial St, Boothbay Harbor, ME<br/><br/>Not a restaurant so much as a full excursion: board the Bennie Alice for a scenic narrated cruise of Boothbay Harbor, land on a 5.5-acre private island, and eat a traditional Downeast clambake cooked right there — fish chowder, two whole lobsters, a pound of steamer clams, corn on the cob, potato, onion, egg, and blueberry cake, with coffee/tea/water included. Round trip runs about 3.5 hours. Rated 4.9 on Tripadvisor, ranked around #12 of 46 Boothbay Harbor restaurants — reviewers consistently call it the best value excursion in the area.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Nothing to choose — the full clambake spread is the whole point, and it's included in the ticket price.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Book ahead; this sells out in peak season.<br/>- Arrive at the ticket booth (Pier 6, Fisherman's Wharf Inn) one hour before departure for check-in.<br/>- Cash or check only — they do not accept credit or debit cards, at the booth, on the boat, or on the island.<br/>- Price is tied to market lobster rates and can shift, so confirm current pricing before booking.<br/>- Budget the better part of an afternoon — this isn't a quick meal, it's a half-day activity.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.cabbageislandclambake.com/]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Restaurant</value></Data>
