  <Placemark>
    <name>Cabot Creamery Cabot VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Cabot Creamery<br/><br/>📍 Cabot VT<br/><br/>Vermont's most famous dairy cooperative, owned by 800 farm families since 1919, producing the cheddar that has won more American Cheese Society awards than any other. The visitor center in Cabot village offers free samples of the full aged-cheddar line, paid factory tours showing the production floor, and the best-price retail on Cabot cheese anywhere.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free samples are available without a tour — the 3-year extra sharp is the benchmark.<br/>- Factory tours run at 11am and 2pm daily in summer; book online.<br/>- The cooperative model — every pound sold benefits the 800 member farms — makes the cheese taste better.<br/>- 45 minutes from Stowe via Route 2; combine with a Montpelier visit.]]></description>
