  <Placemark>
    <name>Cadillac Summit Loop Trail Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Cadillac Summit Loop Trail<br/><br/>📍 Cadillac Mountain summit, Acadia National Park ME<br/><br/>A short paved path circling the bare granite summit of Cadillac Mountain — the highest point on the U.S. Atlantic coast — with 360° views over Frenchman Bay, the Porcupine Islands, and Bar Harbor. Requires driving up via the Cadillac Summit Road vehicle reservation (see that note for booking), but once at the top this specific loop is flat, paved, and wheelchair-accessible.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Only 0.5 miles round trip with ~40 ft of elevation gain — the easiest way to take in the summit views without a real hike<br/>- Very exposed to wind/weather at the top — bring a layer even on a warm day<br/>- Sunrise is the classic time to visit (first light on the U.S. East Coast much of the year) but also the most crowded/reservation-competitive]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Footpath</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>footprints</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>purple</value></Data>
