    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Cadillac Summit Road Bar Harbor ME (Visit 1)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-17T07:00:00<br/><br/>To drive up the Cadillac Summit Road, you will need to book a vehicle reservation in advance through Recreation.gov.<br/><br/>Here are the essential details you need to know before securing your slot:<br/><br/>📅 Booking Windows & Availability<br/><br/>Because spaces fill up incredibly fast, tickets are released in two separate tiers:<br/><br/>- 30% of tickets are released 90 days in advance on a rolling basis.<br/>- The remaining 70% are released at 10:00 AM ET exactly 2 days in advance. If you are looking for a last-minute slot for this week, setting an alarm for 10:00 AM two days before your desired drive is your best bet.<br/><br/>🚗 Ticket Options & Rules<br/><br/>- Cost: $6.00 per vehicle (non-refundable).<br/>- Ticket Types: You can choose a Sunrise ticket (entry window is typically 2 hours long) or a Daytime ticket (entry slots are every 30 minutes).<br/>- Length Limit: Vehicles must be under 21 feet long (including any hitch attachments or bike racks). Oversized vehicles or trailers are strictly prohibited.<br/>- Time Limits: While you must enter during your designated entry window, there is no departure time limit—you can stay at the summit as long as you'd like until the road closes at 9:00 PM.<br/><br/>⚠️ Important Reminders<br/><br/>1. Park Entrance Pass Required: The $6 vehicle reservation is _in addition_ to your standard Acadia National Park Entrance Pass (or America the Beautiful Senior/Annual pass). You must have both.<br/>2. No Connectivity at the Gate: Cellular service is highly unreliable on the mountain. You must print your reservation QR code or save it as a digital copy/screenshot on your phone before heading up. They cannot look up your reservation at the check station.<br/>3. No Re-entry: Your ticket is good for a single entry only.<br/><br/>This Visit<br/><br/>Confirmation #0864562614-1 — Sunrise, August 17, 2026, 7:00–7:30 AM entry window. Booked June 15, 2026.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.recreation.gov/timed-entry/400000]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-orange</styleUrl>
