  <Placemark>
    <name>Camden City Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Camden City Park (Laite Memorial Beach)<br/><br/>📍 Bay View Street, between Cedar and Chestnut Hill Streets, Camden, ME<br/><br/>The town's official name for this spot is Laite Memorial Beach — a small, low-key harbor beach easy to miss from the road (you'll mostly see swings and a few picnic tables). No fees, easy access to Camden Harbor's water, and a swimming platform anchored about 100 feet offshore in summer for anyone up for a brisk Atlantic swim. Restrooms, picnic tables, and grills on site.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open 6am–10pm daily.<br/>- Dogs allowed May 1–Oct 1, but only during set hours (6–10pm and 6–8am) and never on the beach itself May through September — check current signage before bringing one.<br/>- Water quality is tested weekly through the Maine Healthy Beaches program.<br/>- About a half-mile walk from downtown — an easy add-on rather than a special trip.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
