  <Placemark>
    <name>Camden Farmers Market Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Camden Farmers' Market<br/><br/>📍 116 Washington Street (Rt 105), Camden, ME 04843<br/><br/>One of the longest-running farmers' markets in Maine, operating continuously since 1974. Right in town, it's an easy walkable stop during the Camden base camp stretch — vegetables, fruit, meats, cheeses, tofu, mushrooms, maple syrup, baked goods, ice cream, wood-fired pizza, cut flowers, and handmade goods.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Saturdays 9 AM–12 PM, May through October<br/>- Also Wednesdays 3:30–6 PM, mid-June through September — a good second chance if Saturday doesn't work<br/>- Closest market to the Camden base camp itself — worth a recurring stop rather than a one-off<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Camden+Farmers+Market+116+Washington+Street+Camden+ME]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
