  <Placemark>
    <name>Camden Hills State Park (Mount Battie) Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Camden Hills State Park (Mount Battie)<br/><br/>📍 280 Belfast Road, Camden ME<br/><br/>The single most iconic view in Camden — Mount Battie's 800-foot summit overlooks Camden Harbor, Penobscot Bay, and the islands beyond (Cadillac Mountain is visible on a clear day). Tripadvisor Certificate of Excellence park, Mount Battie itself rated 5/5. Reachable either by a moderate 0.5-mile hiking trail or by driving the seasonal Mount Battie Auto Road straight to the summit parking lot.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The Auto Road (open ~May–October, 7am–sunset) means you don't have to hike at all — a good option if you'd rather skip the trail.<br/>- If hiking, the summit ledges are open and broad, not a narrow exposed scramble — much gentler than Beehive/Precipice in Acadia.<br/>- Also in the park: Mount Megunticook (highest peak in the range) and Maiden Cliff, a dramatic cliff-edge overlook — Maiden Cliff specifically has real drop-offs at the summit, worth weighing given vertigo sensitivity.<br/>- This is the view on your own Base Camp 3 cover photo — worth prioritizing early in the stay.<br/>- The summit viewpoint is also listed on Google Maps as "Curtis Lighthouse Overlook" — same spot, same 4.7 rating.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
