  <Placemark>
    <name>Campton Campground Waterville Valley NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Campton Campground<br/><br/>📍 Off NH-49, near Thornton, NH (White Mountain National Forest)<br/><br/>One of the first National Forest campgrounds drivers reach heading north on I-93 — 58 sites scattered among old-growth white pines, a short distance east of Exit 28. A convenient base for exploring Tripoli Road and Waterville Valley, with easy access to popular hikes like Welch-Dickey and the Osceolas, plus nearby 4000-footers Mt. Tecumseh and the Tripyramids.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Reserve ahead in peak summer/fall — it's a popular, easy-access campground right off the interstate.<br/>- Good jumping-off point if combining a River Heritage Trail drive with a White Mountains hiking day.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.8729%2C%20-71.6253]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-blue</styleUrl>
