  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Cannon Mountain Aerial Tramway Franconia NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Cannon Mountain Aerial Tramway<br/><br/>📍 Franconia NH<br/><br/>The oldest aerial tramway in North America, operating since 1938, carries passengers 2,022 vertical feet to the 4,080-foot summit of Cannon Mountain in 8 minutes. The summit observation deck delivers a panorama spanning Vermont's Green Mountains, the Presidential Range, and — on clear days — into Canada and the St. Lawrence. A summit trail adds another 200 feet to the true peak.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The tram runs daily in summer; tickets should be purchased online to avoid waits.<br/>- The summit can be 20°F cooler than the valley — bring a layer.<br/>- From the summit, the Rim Trail loop (1.5 miles) visits the true peak and several overlooks.<br/>- The Echo Lake beach and Artist Bluff hike are at the base of the tramway — easy to combine.]]></description>
