  <Placemark>
    <name>Cape Elizabeth West Lighthouse Cape Elizabeth ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Cape Elizabeth West Lighthouse (Two Lights, West Tower)<br/><br/>📍 Two Lights Road, Cape Elizabeth, ME<br/><br/>The inactive twin of the "Two Lights" pair, built in 1828 and rebuilt in cast iron in 1873. At least 98 vessels wrecked along this stretch of coast between 1780 and 1990 before the twin lights were established to guide ships into Portland Harbor. Privately owned with no public access — the active east tower nearby remains a Coast Guard aid to navigation.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Best public view is from The Lobster Shack Restaurant at the end of Two Lights Road.<br/>- Pair with the active Cape Elizabeth Lighthouse a short walk away.]]></description>
