  <Placemark>
    <name>Cape Neddick Nubble Lighthouse York Beach ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Cape Neddick (Nubble) Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Sohier Park, York Beach, ME<br/><br/>First lit July 1, 1879, this 41-foot conical cast-iron tower was manufactured in Portland and shipped out to Nubble Island aboard the USS Myrtle. Early keepers supplemented their pay by ferrying curious visitors out to the island for ten cents. An estimated half million people visit Sohier Park annually, and NASA included a digitized image of the lighthouse on Voyager II's Golden Record. Owned by the Town of York; automated in 1987.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds at Sohier Park are open to the public with an easy, short walk and great photo angles; the dwelling and tower are closed to visitors.<br/>- Scenic cruises out of Ogunquit pass by the lighthouse.<br/>- Lit with holiday lights every winter — a local tradition worth knowing about even outside trip dates.]]></description>
