  <Placemark>
    <name>Castle Tucker Wiscasset ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Castle Tucker<br/><br/>📍 2 Lee St, Wiscasset, ME 04578<br/><br/>An 1807 Georgian mansion perched above the Sheepscot River, operated as a historic house museum by Historic New England. Tells the story of the Tucker shipping family, who lived there from 1858 to 2004.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open June 1–Oct 15, Friday–Sunday, 11am–3pm only — plan around it<br/>- Pairs well with a walk through downtown Wiscasset<br/><br/>More info: https://www.historicnewengland.org/property/castle-tucker/]]></description>
