  <Placemark>
    <name>Catherine Mountain Franklin ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Catherine Mountain<br/><br/>📍 Donnell Pond Public Reserved Land, Franklin, ME<br/><br/>A 962-foot peak in Township 10 SD — the "Blackswoods" township the byway is named for — with local legend holding that it's named for a woman named Catherine whose ghost is said to haunt the hill. A moderate 2.8-mile hike (about 633 ft of gain, 1.5–2 hours) leads to summit views over Tunk Lake, Black Mountain, Schoodic Mountain, and Mount Desert Island in the distance.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A good moderate option if Tunk or Caribou Mountain feel too ambitious for the day.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.6164%2C%20-68.0859]]></description>
