  <Placemark>
    <name>Central Provisions Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Central Provisions<br/><br/>📍 414 Fore Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The name Central Provisions pays homage to the original purpose of its building. Daniel Fox, a merchant specializing in goods from the West Indies, constructed 414 Fore Street in 1828 for use as a provisions storehouse.<br/><br/>In the early 1800s, ships could sail directly up to the rear of the building and unload dry goods such as sugar, molasses, and spices. Today it is an award-winning restaurant that celebrates that maritime heritage.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Central+Provisions,+414+Fore+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
