  <Placemark>
    <name>Champlain Monument Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Champlain Monument<br/><br/>📍 Acadia National Park, ME<br/><br/>Commemorates French explorer Samuel de Champlain, who sailed past and named the island "Isle des Monts Deserts" (island of bare mountains) in 1604 — the source of both "Mount Desert Island" and Champlain Mountain's names.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A brief historical marker stop, easy to combine with other sights in the immediate area.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.2997%2C%20-68.2273]]></description>
