  <Placemark>
    <name>Chapman-Hall House Damariscotta ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Chapman-Hall House<br/><br/>📍 270 Main Street, Damariscotta, ME<br/><br/>One of the oldest surviving houses in the Damariscotta area, built in 1754 as a saltbox-style farmhouse. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places, it's preserved as a seasonal house museum with period furnishings and gardens on Main Street.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Note: some published addresses list "27 Main St" — that's actually River House's address nearby; the Chapman-Hall House itself is at 270 Main St.<br/>- Seasonal hours only (typically summer) — check ahead before visiting.]]></description>
