  <Placemark>
    <name>Charles Q Clapp Block Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Charles Q. Clapp Block<br/><br/>📍 Congress, Free & High Streets, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The Charles Q. Clapp Block is situated on a triangular site at the junction of Congress, Free, and High Streets — Portland's answer to New York City's Flatiron Building. It was designed by Charles Quincy Clapp in the Federal style and is one of the city's oldest commercial blocks.<br/><br/>Fun fact: Hay's Pharmacy occupied the ground floor for many decades, and today the building is more widely known as the "Hay Building."<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Charles+Q+Clapp+Block,+Congress+Free+High+Streets,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
