  <Placemark>
    <name>Chesterfield Gorge Natural Area Chesterfield NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Chesterfield Gorge Natural Area<br/><br/>📍 1823 Route 9, Chesterfield, NH<br/><br/>Only 13 acres but packed with visual drama — a gorge carved roughly 12,000 years ago as Ice Age glaciers retreated and released torrents of meltwater through the bedrock. Granite walls rise up to 70 feet along an easy, shaded 0.7–0.8-mile loop following Wild Brook, past smooth glacial potholes, ripple marks, and small cascades.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Best April through November; dogs welcome on leash.<br/>- A quick, easy stop right off Route 9 between Keene and Brattleboro, VT.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=42.9141%2C%20-72.4049]]></description>
