  <Placemark>
    <name>Civilian Conservation Corps Memorial Plaque Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Civilian Conservation Corps Memorial Plaque<br/><br/>📍 Acadia National Park, ME<br/><br/>Honors the Civilian Conservation Corps (CCC), whose crews — part of a Depression-era federal work relief program — built and maintained much of the trail and infrastructure network still used throughout Acadia today.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A brief historical marker rather than a destination in itself.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3745%2C%20-68.2600]]></description>
