  <Placemark>
    <name>Clinton House Poughkeepsie NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Clinton House<br/><br/>📍 549 Main St, Poughkeepsie, NY 12601<br/><br/>A Dutch Colonial/Georgian stone house, known formerly as the Clear/Everitt house and home to the Dutchess County Historical Society. Built in 1765, it burned and was rebuilt in 1783 by army masons. Tradition holds it to have been George Clinton's headquarters during the American Revolution.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Exhibits; research library by appointment. Call 845/471-1630 for visitor information.<br/>- Stop 29 of 33 on the Poughkeepsie & LaGrange Scenic Tour (Tour 5).]]></description>
