  <Placemark>
    <name>Coastal Maine Botanical Gardens Boothbay Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Coastal Maine Botanical Gardens<br/><br/>📍 105 Botanical Gardens Drive, Boothbay, ME<br/><br/>Over 300 acres of coastal gardens and natural spaces — one of the largest botanical gardens in New England, and consistently the top-rated attraction in the Boothbay region. Highlights include the Bibby and Harold Alfond Children's Garden, the Giles Rhododendron and Perennial Garden, a Native Butterfly House, and waterfront trails along the tidal Back River. The grounds also host rotating large-scale art installations, including Thomas Dambo's giant recycled-wood troll sculptures tucked into the woods.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Allow at least half a day — the grounds are genuinely extensive, and it's easy to lose several hours just in the Children's Garden and rhododendron garden alone.<br/>- Open daily 9am–5pm; buy tickets online in advance during peak summer to skip the gate line.<br/>- Free wheelchairs and $15–18 electric scooter rentals are available if walking the full 300 acres isn't realistic — there's also a 90-minute accessible cart tour led by docents, for up to five people.<br/>- Bring sunscreen, bug spray, comfortable shoes, and a refillable water bottle — stations are placed throughout the grounds.<br/>- No pets allowed (service animals excepted) — plan around this if traveling with a dog.<br/>- Combine with lunch at the on-site Kitchen Garden Cafe (see The Cafe) so you don't have to leave and re-enter.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
