  <Placemark>
    <name>Cobble Hill Trailhead Sugar Hill NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Cobble Hill Trailhead<br/><br/>📍 Near Landaff Center / Sugar Hill, NH<br/><br/>A 7-mile, moderate (1,167 ft elevation gain) trail through White Mountain National Forest between Cobble Hill and Moody Ledge, starting from the banks of the Wild Ammonoosuc River, with an alternate northern trailhead off Gale Chandler Road in Landaff Center.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Reviewers describe this specific trail as a logging-road/snowmobile-style route with no real views — if you want Sugar Hill's famous mountain panoramas, look at the area's other trails instead.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.1057%2C%20-71.8718]]></description>
