  <Placemark>
    <name>Colby Wildlife Preserve Edgecomb ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-10T14:00:00<br/><br/>Colby Wildlife Preserve<br/><br/>📍 McKay Road, East Edgecomb, ME<br/><br/>A 12-acre preserve on Salt Marsh Cove (Damariscotta River) — a short, easy loop (~0.5–0.7 mi total) through forest to a sheltered cove, suitable for any age. The shortest, easiest option of the day's hikes.<br/><br/>Getting There<br/>From Wiscasset village: Route 1 across the Davey Bridge, right onto Route 27 toward Boothbay, left onto McKay Road just past Edgecomb Potters.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free, open year-round.<br/>- Good "stretch your legs" stop near the end of the day, close to both Wiscasset and Glidden Point Oyster Farms.]]></description>
