  <Placemark>
    <name>Colonial Pemaquid State Historic Site ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-07T10:15:00<br/><br/>Colonial Pemaquid State Historic Site<br/><br/>📍 Colonial Pemaquid Rd, New Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A state historic site preserving the archaeological remains of a 17th- and 18th-century colonial settlement on the Pemaquid River, with a small on-site museum displaying artifacts found here (musket balls, coins, pottery, early hardware). The reconstructed Fort William Henry stands nearby — see Fort William Henry.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Rating in question: listed at 4.8, but independently I could only confirm Tripadvisor's figure (4.4 over 154 reviews) — Google itself tends to run noticeably higher than Tripadvisor, so 4.8 on Google is plausible, just not independently confirmed here.<br/>- Combine with Fort William Henry and Pemaquid Point Lighthouse for a full New Harbor colonial-history loop.]]></description>
