  <Placemark>
    <name>Compass Harbor Bar Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Compass Harbor<br/><br/>📍 Route 3, Bar Harbor ME (~1 mile south of downtown)<br/><br/>A quiet, uncrowded 0.8-mile out-and-back walk just a mile south of downtown Bar Harbor, leading to the ruins of "Old Farm," the former estate of George B. Dorr, the founder of Acadia National Park. Flat oceanfront path through woods to the shore, with stone foundations, steps, and remnants of a saltwater pool along the way.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Short and flat — a nice low-key walk if you want Acadia scenery without a real hike.<br/>- Easy to combine with a stroll into downtown Bar Harbor since it's so close.<br/>- Small, unmarked gravel parking lot off Route 3 — easy to miss, keep an eye out just north of Schooner Head Road.<br/>- Coordinates above are an approximation — worth confirming against Google Maps before you go.]]></description>
