  <Placemark>
    <name>Connecticut Lakes State Forest Pittsburg NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Connecticut Lakes State Forest<br/><br/>📍 Pittsburg, NH<br/><br/>A large state forest surrounding the Connecticut Lakes headwaters in New Hampshire's northernmost town — remote woods and a genuinely healthy moose population, the reason the byway running through it is named the Moose Path Trail.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Drive slowly, especially at dawn/dusk — moose sightings (and moose-vehicle collisions) are a real consideration on these roads.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=45.1862%2C%20-71.1876]]></description>
