  <Placemark>
    <name>Crabtree Ledge Lighthouse Hancock Point ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Crabtree Ledge Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Frenchman Bay, near Hancock Point, ME<br/><br/>A 54-foot iron caisson lighthouse first lit January 15, 1890, guarding the approach to Sullivan Harbor and its ferry routes. The station saw tragedy — assistant keeper Chester Brinkworth and his brother drowned in 1916, and assistant keeper Joseph Whitmore died in 1917. Discontinued in 1933, the abandoned structure finally collapsed into the bay during a winter storm in February 1950.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Nothing remains to visit — the lighthouse itself is gone. A bell buoy now marks the ledge.<br/>- Included here for completeness of the state list, not as a place to plan a stop.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
