  <Placemark>
    <name>Cranmore Mountain Resort North Conway NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Cranmore Mountain Resort<br/><br/>📍 North Conway, NH<br/><br/>Founded by local banker Harvey Dow Gibson, who decided his hometown needed a ski resort — Cranmore opened for the 1937-38 season with a single rope tow. Gibson later used his financial clout to bring Hannes Schneider, the "Father of Modern Skiing" and founder of the world's first ski school (1907), out of Nazi Germany to develop a ski school here, teaching his Arlberg technique to students from around the world. The Skimobile — a quirky lift of small cars on a wooden track, built for the 1938-39 season — carried skiers partway up the mountain until 1989. The Schneider family owned the resort until 1984; it's changed hands several times since and is now owned by the operators of Jiminy Peak in Massachusetts.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Right in North Conway village — easy to combine with Echo Lake, Cathedral Ledge, or a downtown stop.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0575%2C%20-71.1074]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
