  <Placemark>
    <name>Creek Meeting House Clinton NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Creek Meeting House<br/><br/>📍 Clinton, NY<br/><br/>In the late 1700s Quakers settled in the area and began construction of the building now occupied by the Upton Lake Grange. Completed in 1782, the fieldstone Creek Meeting House, home of the Clinton Historical Society, is identified as a Quaker site by separate entrances for women and men and by the adjacent burial ground, one of the oldest in the county.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Exhibits; call 845/266-5494 for visitor information.<br/>- Stop 16 of 26 on the Hyde Park, Clinton & Pleasant Valley Scenic Tour (Tour 3).]]></description>
