  <Placemark>
    <name>Crooked Farm Bristol ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Crooked Farm<br/><br/>📍 Old County Road, near Carpenter's Boatshop, off Route 130 at Bristol Library, Bristol, ME<br/><br/>Nearly 140 acres of forest, wetlands, and open fields (2002 community partnership) with Pemaquid River gravel spawning streambeds and moose/mink/otter habitat. ~2.5-2.6 mi loop, 144 ft gain.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Notably buggy in summer — bring repellent<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/crooked-farm/]]></description>
