  <Placemark>
    <name>Crum Elbow Meeting House Hyde Park NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Crum Elbow Meeting House<br/><br/>📍 Crum Elbow Rd, Hyde Park, NY 12538<br/><br/>A simple, 2-story white frame structure with separate doors for the sexes, dating back to the late 1700s when Friends settled the eastern hills of Hyde Park, then part of Clinton. A narrow porch with milled supports was added mid-19th century. The burial ground contains many early stones.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Stop 22 of 26 on the Hyde Park, Clinton & Pleasant Valley Scenic Tour (Tour 3).]]></description>
