  <Placemark>
    <name>Cuckolds Lighthouse Southport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Cuckolds Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 The Cuckolds, off Southport Island, near Boothbay Harbor, ME<br/><br/>Congress appropriated $25,000 in 1891 to build this fog-signal station on a pair of rocky, storm-battered islets, completed November 16, 1892. Keepers became known for daring rescues, including saving the crew of the schooner Aurora in 1896, which earned recognition from the Canadian government. Automated in 1974; the keeper's dwelling was demolished in the late 1970s after vandalism, but the site was later restored and briefly operated as an inn (2014–2019).<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Closed to the public, but viewable from shore via Route 27 south from Wiscasset to the Landing Road pier on Southport Island.<br/>- The original Fresnel lens is on display at the Maine Lighthouse Museum in Rockland.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
