  <Placemark>
    <name>Cumberland County Courthouse Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Cumberland County Courthouse<br/><br/>📍 205 Newbury Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The Cumberland County Superior Court at 205 Newbury Street was built in 1910 by local architect George Burnham, who was trained in Beaux Arts architectural style (also known as Classical Revival).<br/><br/>Along with three other buildings, the Cumberland County courthouse is one of the few buildings in Portland composed entirely of granite.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/205+Newbury+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
