    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Damariscotta Mills Fish Ladder &amp; Ice House Park Newcastle ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-10T10:45:00<br/><br/>Damariscotta Mills Fish Ladder & Ice House Park<br/><br/>📍 Newcastle, ME 04553 (Mills Rd / Route 215, ~1.5-1.6 mi north of Damariscotta)<br/><br/>A stone fish ladder built in 1807 by the towns of Nobleboro and Newcastle to give alewives access to the freshwater falls at Damariscotta Mills — restored starting 2007, with clear signage explaining the fish spawning process. Ice House Park next to it is the actual spot locals swim in summer, not a place most tourists find.<br/><br/>Getting There<br/>Two parking options: a lot just past Austin Road on Route 215, or the Fish House parking lot (path leads behind the building to the ladder).<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The famous alewife run itself is a May event, not relevant for an August visit — but the site, park, and swimming spot are worth seeing/using regardless of season.<br/>- Coordinates are an estimate — use the Google Maps link above for actual navigation, and check damariscottamills. for current directions/parking.<br/><br/>More info: https://damariscottamills.org/]]></description>
