    <description><![CDATA[Overview  <br/>Type: Sake brewery  <br/>  <br/>Best known for: Guided tours and tastings of premium Junmai Daiginjo sake.  <br/>  <br/>Location context: Not mentioned  <br/>  <br/>Price level: Not mentioned  <br/>  <br/>Visit timing: Not mentioned  <br/>  <br/>Typical Customers  <br/>Demographics: Not mentioned  <br/>  <br/>Group types: Couples, groups of friends, families  <br/>  <br/>Common occasions: Tastings, casual visits  <br/>  <br/>Vibe & Setting  <br/>Atmosphere: Spacious, casual  <br/>  <br/>Noise level: Not mentioned  <br/>  <br/>Decor & setting: Indoor seating, large parking area  <br/>  <br/>Service style: Friendly, with some new staff causing slight delays  <br/>  <br/>Recommended Dishes  <br/>Overall dish consensus  <br/>Reviewers have praised the offerings of Junmai Daiginjo sake, particularly enjoying the tastings. They reference the informative service provided during these tastings.  <br/>  <br/>How “top dishes” are determined  <br/>Top dishes are based on mentions in user reviews, focusing on those that highlight certain sake selections and tasting experiences.  <br/>  <br/>| Rank | Dish           | Why it stands out                               | How often it’s mentioned                     | Ideal for          |  <br/>|------|----------------|------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|--------------------|  <br/>| 1    | Junmai Daiginjo | Noted for its high quality and exquisite taste | Frequently praised in multiple reviews      | Special occasions  |  <br/>| 2    | Tasting flight  | Offers a variety of flavors and options      | Often recommended for newcomers to sake    | Sharing at the table |  <br/>| 3    | Not mentioned    | Not mentioned                                   | Not mentioned                              | Not mentioned      |  <br/><br/>Good alternates / backup choices  <br/>Not mentioned  <br/>  <br/>Highlights (non-dish positives from reviews)  <br/>Guided tours: Visitors enjoy the educational aspect of tours offered by the brewery.  <br/>  <br/>Beautiful setting: The brewery is noted for its pristine grounds, enhancing the experience.  <br/>  <br/>Knowledgeable staff: Many reviews commend the staff's detailed knowledge about sake.  <br/>  <br/>Common Issues (from reviews)  <br/>Service delays: Some customers experienced longer wait times due to new staff while ordering drinks.  <br/>  <br/>Miscommunication: There were reports of incorrect orders during busy times, such as receiving soap instead of sake.  <br/>  <br/>Practical Notes  <br/>Reservation / wait: Not mentioned  <br/>  <br/>Accessibility: Not mentioned  <br/>  <br/>Parking / transit: Ample parking available  <br/>  <br/>Best use case: Great for casual tastings and learning about sake.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Dassai+Blue+Sake+Brewery/@41.7616802,-73.9315144,827m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m14!1m7!3m6!1s0x89dd15c353234271:0x37cb3ae142a90957!2sDassai+Blue+Sake+Brewery!8m2!3d41.7616762!4d-73.9289395!16s%2Fg%2F11rx1gkwpv!3m5!1s0x89dd15c353234271:0x37cb3ae142a90957!8m2!3d41.7616762!4d-73.9289395!16s%2Fg%2F11rx1gkwpv?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMy4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
