  <Placemark>
    <name>David W Campbell House Cherryfield ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[David W. Campbell House<br/><br/>📍 Cherryfield, ME<br/><br/>Built in 1828 in the Federal and Italianate styles, notable for its cupola with Palladian windows — tied to the prominent Campbell family, into which the Archibald-Adams House's Elizabeth Archibald Adams remarried after her first husband's death. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Part of a walkable cluster of historic homes with the Archibald-Adams and William M. Nash houses.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.6006%2C%20-67.9219]]></description>
