  <Placemark>
    <name>De La Vergne Hill &amp; Silo Ridge Country Club Amenia NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[De La Vergne Hill & Silo Ridge Country Club<br/><br/>📍 5021 Route 44, Amenia, NY 12501<br/><br/>A mile-long "S" curve on the turnpike historically called the "Devil's Elbow," but the scenery is spectacular — at the turn there's a view of three states: New York, Connecticut, and Massachusetts. Silo Ridge Country Club, an 18-hole public golf course and restaurant, was developed in 1992 from cornfields and pastures around Squabble Hole, one of two 19th-century ore pits filled with water.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Call 845/373-9200 for the golf club.<br/>- Stop 9 of 17 on the Washington & Amenia Scenic Tour (Tour 4) — no matching town-level destination note exists yet for this stretch, so it's linked to the tour hub directly.]]></description>
