  <Placemark>
    <name>Deer Island Thorofare Mark Island Lighthouse Stonington ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Deer Island Thorofare (Mark Island) Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Mark Island, Deer Island Thorofare, near Stonington, ME<br/><br/>Congress appropriated funds in 1856 and the brick tower with attached seven-room dwelling went into service March 1, 1858, guiding traffic through this important inland passage between Deer Isle and Isle au Haut. A 1958 fire destroyed the keeper's dwelling; the station was automated soon after, with the historic Fresnel lens replaced by modern optics.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds open, tower closed — best viewed by boat.<br/>- Isle au Haut Boat Services out of Stonington offers views along its route.]]></description>
