  <Placemark>
    <name>Deer Leap Mountain Killington VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Deer Leap Mountain<br/><br/>📍 Sherburne Pass Trailhead, Killington, VT<br/><br/>A moderate 2.1-mile out-and-back starting at the Sherburne Pass Trailhead, crossing Route 4 toward the Inn at Long Trail before joining the Appalachian/Long Trail briefly to reach the Deer Leap Trail. The final quarter mile leads to a rock outcrop with dramatic views of the Coolidge Range and Sherburne Pass, looking back toward Pico and Killington.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Can be muddy and rocky, and gets crowded — best April through November.<br/>- A 4.5-mile loop option via the Appalachian Trail extends the hike if you want more.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.6701%2C%20-72.8362]]></description>
