  <Placemark>
    <name>Devils Slide Stark NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Devil's Slide<br/><br/>📍 Northside Road, Stark, NH<br/><br/>A 750-foot dark granite cliff that forms an imposing backdrop for the tiny village of Stark, best known from the classic photo pairing it with the Stark Covered Bridge in the foreground. From Route 110 in the village center, cross the covered bridge and turn onto Northside Road for the trailhead. A moderate 1.6-mile out-and-back (620 ft gain) climbs via a switchback along a ledge band, through a break in the rock, and around to a perch directly above the cliffs — a bird's-eye view over the village, bridge, and the lazy Upper Ammonoosuc River below.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Combine with the Stark Covered Bridge itself, right at the trailhead.<br/>- Short but genuinely steep in the middle section — sturdy shoes recommended.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.6053%2C%20-71.4147]]></description>
