  <Placemark>
    <name>Dia Beacon</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Dia:Beacon<br/><br/>📍 3 Beekman St, Beacon, NY 12508<br/><br/>A cavernous former Nabisco box-printing factory converted into one of the largest contemporary art museums in the country, run by the Dia Art Foundation. Vast, naturally-lit galleries hold large-scale, long-term installations by artists like Richard Serra, Louise Bourgeois, and Agnes Martin — built for pieces too big for a conventional museum.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Closed Tuesday–Thursday; open Monday and Friday–Sunday, 10am–5pm — confirm before building a day around it.<br/>- Plan at least 2–3 hours; the galleries are large and spread out, with real walking between them.<br/>- Easy pairing with Mount Gulian, about 10 minutes away.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.5002,-73.9827]]></description>
