  <Placemark>
    <name>Dice Head Lighthouse Castine ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Dice Head Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Castine, ME (Penobscot River)<br/><br/>First lit November 5, 1828, this 42-foot conical rubblestone tower guided vessels up the Penobscot River. In 1929, pilot William Wincapaw, guided home by its beam during a snowstorm, was inspired to start dropping gifts to isolated lighthouse keepers each Christmas — the origin of the "Flying Santa" tradition. Decommissioned in 1937, the light was restored and relit on January 31, 2008.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds open via a short pathway to a viewing area; the keeper's dwelling is a private rental, tower closed.<br/>- Easy stop while exploring Castine's historic waterfront.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
