  <Placemark>
    <name>Dogs Head Falls Johnson VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Dog's Head Falls<br/><br/>📍 Lamoille Valley Rail Trail, Johnson, VT<br/><br/>An 8-foot drop where the entire Lamoille River constricts and churns through a narrow gap carved into a sloping wall of schist — most dramatic at lower water levels. Named for a rock formation on the south bank just below the falls that resembles a dog's profile (a Saint Bernard, or maybe a stout Labrador, depending who you ask). Reached via an easy 2.4-mile out-and-back on the Lamoille Valley Rail Trail, following the historic "Bridge Road" rail line that once carried talc, limestone, and Christmas trees across the state.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- An easy, family-friendly walk (about 46 minutes round trip) — good for a quick break on a Green Mountain Byway drive.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.6226%2C%20-72.6773]]></description>
