  <Placemark>
    <name>Doubling Point Lighthouse Arrowsic ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Doubling Point Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Arrowsic Island, ~2 miles down the Kennebec River from Bath, ME<br/><br/>Placed in operation March 30, 1898, to aid navigation on the busy Kennebec River, and relocated 532 feet offshore onto a granite pier the following year. Ice floes damaged the granite foundation badly enough to require full removal and restoration in 1999–2000 before the light returned to service.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds open, dwelling and tower closed. Reach via Route 127 (Five Islands Road) to Whitmore's Landing Road, then Doubling Point Road, with limited parking.<br/>- The original Fresnel lens is on display at the Maine Lighthouse Museum in Rockland.<br/>- Pairs naturally with Doubling Point Range Lighthouse, a short walk away.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
