  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Doubling Point Range Lighthouse Arrowsic ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Doubling Point Range Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Arrowsic Island, near Bath, ME<br/><br/>Built in 1898 to guide ships over 600 feet long through a sharp double bend in the Kennebec River — two octagonal wooden towers with red roofs. Keeper Captain Harry L. Nye rescued four boys stranded on an ice floe in 1927 and earned efficiency flags in 1925 and 1930.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds open via Whitmore's Landing Road to Doubling Point Road, then a path to the lights — stay on the marked path.<br/>- Pairs naturally with Doubling Point Lighthouse a short walk away.<br/>- Maine Maritime Museum and Cap'n Fish's run cruises that pass both lights.]]></description>
