  <Placemark>
    <name>Downeast Windjammer Ferry Bar Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Downeast Windjammer Ferry<br/><br/>📍 Bar Harbor Terminal → Winter Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A scenic 45-minute ferry crossing from Bar Harbor to Winter Harbor that avoids road congestion around Ellsworth entirely. The ferry journey itself is part of the Schoodic Peninsula experience—arriving by water is more atmospheric than driving.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Departs from Bar Harbor waterfront<br/>- Check schedule in advance; ferries may be seasonal<br/>- 45-minute crossing provides scenic views of Frenchman Bay<br/>- Arrive at terminal 15-30 minutes before departure<br/>- Ferry dock is right at Winter Harbor, walking distance to amenities<br/>- Return ferry available for evening departure back to Bar Harbor<br/>- Saves significant drive time vs. routing through Ellsworth<br/>- A memorable and scenic way to start your Schoodic day]]></description>
