  <Placemark>
    <name>Duck Harbor Isle au Haut ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Duck Harbor<br/><br/>📍 Western shore of Isle au Haut, near the Duck Harbor Boat Landing<br/><br/>The most remote corner of Acadia National Park — a 5-site lean-to campground (fire ring, picnic table, 3-sided shelter per site), reached only by the Isle au Haut mailboat or a private boat. Open mid-May through mid-October; reservations typically fill within minutes of the April 1 opening. Isle au Haut offers rocky shoreline, wooded uplands, bogs, and a mile-long freshwater lake with far fewer visitors than Mount Desert Island.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Coordinates are approximate — worth confirming the exact boat landing/campground location before relying on it for navigation<br/>- Reservations required and highly competitive — plan months ahead if camping here is the goal<br/>- Composting toilets on site; hand pump for non-potable water 0.3 mi away, no potable water source<br/>- Even a day trip via mailboat (without camping) is a genuinely quiet, uncrowded way to see a different side of Acadia]]></description>
