  <Placemark>
    <name>Ducktrap River Preserve (CMLT Trail) Lincolnville ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Ducktrap River Preserve (CMLT Trail)<br/><br/>📍 Route 52, Lincolnville, ME — trailhead ~125 yds after Rt 52 crosses the Ducktrap River, 3.5 mi north of Lincolnville Center (coordinate approximate — no exact published GPS pin found, estimated from driving directions)<br/><br/>Coastal Mountains Land Trust's largest and most wild preserve, protecting the river's shoreline for wild Atlantic salmon habitat. The River Trail (1.7 mi one-way, easy, shares the first 1.4 mi with a snowmobile trail) reaches the river at an old, now-missing bridge location — crossable at low water only, cross at your own risk. The Backcountry Loop (1.8 mi round-trip, moderate) is accessed via an unbridged crossing. Conserved in stages from 1996 to present, alongside the multi-stakeholder Ducktrap Coalition's broader river-conservation work.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Coordinate is an estimate based on driving directions — verify locally before relying on it for navigation<br/>- Distinct from the existing "Ducktrap River Preserve" note (the coastal beach/river-mouth spot) — this is the same river, but well upstream, a different access point and a different experience (forest trail vs. beach)<br/>- No bridge at the river crossing — cross at your own risk, low water only<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org/preserves/ducktrap-river-preserve/]]></description>
