  <Placemark>
    <name>Ducktrap River Preserve Lincolnville ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Ducktrap River Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Lincolnville ME<br/><br/>A rocky beach and river-mouth area popular at low tide and sunset, with bald eagles known to nest nearby. Good for wading, shell collecting, and kayaking; a separate forested trail loop follows the Ducktrap River and Turner Falls.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Best around low tide and sunset, per most reviews.<br/>- Ducktrap Kayak & SUP operates guided trips from here if you want to get on the water.<br/>- Coordinates above are an approximation (Lincolnville town center) — worth confirming the exact access point against Google Maps before you go.<br/>- Not the same as Ducktrap River Preserve (CMLT Trail) — the actual Coastal Mountains Land Trust preserve is well upstream on Route 52, a forested salmon-habitat trail, distinct from this coastal beach spot]]></description>
