  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Eastern Promenade Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Eastern Promenade<br/><br/>📍 Eastern Promenade, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The Eastern Promenade is a 68-acre hilltop park running along Portland's eastern bluff above Casco Bay. It offers some of the best views in the city — on clear days you can see the Casco Bay islands, the open Atlantic, and the White Mountains of New Hampshire.<br/><br/>The park includes a paved multi-use trail (the East End Beach trail connects down to the water), a small sandy beach at the bottom, the site of Fort Allen, picnic areas, and a bandstand. It's a beloved local spot and one of Portland's great free pleasures.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Sunrise from the Promenade is exceptional — the east-facing bluff catches the first light over the bay<br/>- The paved trail is great for a morning walk or run with uninterrupted water views<br/>- East End Beach at the base is small but swimmable in summer<br/>- Connects to the Back Cove Trail Portland MEfor a longer loop around the peninsula<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Eastern+Promenade/@43.6647,-70.2382,17z]]></description>
