  <Placemark>
    <name>Eben's Head Trail Isle au Haut ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Eben's Head Trail<br/><br/>📍 Duck Harbor, Isle au Haut, ME (mailboat access from Stonington)<br/><br/>A 1.4-mile easy out-and-back trail on Isle au Haut, reviewed as "short and sweet" with "absolutely stunning views." Isle au Haut is Acadia's least-visited district by a wide margin — roughly 10,000 visitors a year compared to millions on Mount Desert Island — and it's only reachable by mailboat from Stonington, which is exactly why it stays this quiet. Only 23 AllTrails reviews total, itself a reflection of how few people make the trip.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Reached only by mailboat from Stonington — check the Isle au Haut Boat Services schedule before planning a visit<br/>- Trailhead is at Duck Harbor, on the island's more remote (Acadia NP-managed) southern end<br/>- Because the whole island sees so few visitors, this is worth treating as a half/full-day commitment, not a quick stop]]></description>
