  <Placemark>
    <name>Egg Rock Lighthouse Bar Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Egg Rock Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Egg Rock, Frenchman Bay, ~4 miles southeast of Bar Harbor, ME<br/><br/>Operational November 1, 1875, this twelve-foot square brick tower is built directly into the keeper's dwelling. A devastating gale in 1876 swept away outbuildings and flooded the station. Newspaper magnate Joseph Pulitzer, whose estate sat nearby, complained about the foghorn until it was upgraded and redirected away from shore in 1904.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds closed April 1–August 31 (nesting season for seabirds), lighthouse closed year-round — this covers most of the New England 2026 trip window.<br/>- Distant view from Acadia's Park Loop Road; closer views from Bar Harbor boat tours or a scenic flight.]]></description>
