  <Placemark>
    <name>Empire Chinese Kitchen Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Empire Chinese Kitchen<br/><br/>📍 575 Congress St, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Maine's first dedicated dim sum restaurant, established 2013. Reviewers consistently compare the Shanghai soup dumplings favorably to real Chinatown spots — a legitimate dim sum destination, not just a general Chinese restaurant with a few token items. Tripadvisor 4.5★ (466 reviews, #6 of 511 Portland restaurants); Yelp 735 reviews; Restaurant Guru 4.8★.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Shanghai soup dumplings — the standout, repeatedly singled out<br/>- Kung Pao chicken<br/>- Bacon fried rice<br/>- Garlic green beans<br/>- Gluten-free dumplings available<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Specializes in dim sum, Cantonese stir-fry, and gluten-free options<br/>- Right on Congress St in the Arts District — easy to combine with other downtown Portland stops<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Empire+Chinese+Kitchen/@43.6558,-70.2611,17z]]></description>
