  <Placemark>
    <name>Erickson Fields Preserve Rockport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Erickson Fields Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Route 90, Rockport, ME (0.5 mi from the Route 1/Route 90 light)<br/><br/>460 combined acres (with adjoining Beech Hill) of fields and forest, managed by Maine Coast Heritage Trust. The Beech Hill Connector Trail (built 2018-2021, a Coastal Mountains Land Trust/MCHT partnership) links Erickson Fields to Beech Hill Preserve — up to 1.8 mi one-way, gravel at Beech Hill, dirt and gravel at Erickson Fields.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- No parking on Beech Hill Rd — use the Erickson Fields trailhead on Rt 90 or the Beech Hill trailhead<br/>- Pairs naturally with the existing Beech Hill Preserve note — same connector trail links both<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
