  <Placemark>
    <name>Evangelical Baptist Church Laconia NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Evangelical Baptist Church<br/><br/>📍 Veterans Square, Laconia, NH<br/><br/>Built in 1836 by Congregationalists as the North Church, moved to its current location and sold to the First Christian Church (later Evangelical Baptist) in the 19th century, and extensively restyled in 1871. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1985. The Evangelical Baptist congregation relocated to Lakeport in 2013; the building was purchased in 2020 by Justin Spencer of Recycled Percussion and now operates as a theater/event venue.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A downtown landmark visible from Veterans Square — check current programming since it now functions as a performance venue, not a church.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.5292%2C%20-71.4722]]></description>
