  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Eventide Oyster Co Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Eventide Oyster Co.<br/><br/>📍 86 Middle Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Eventide Oyster Co. is one of Portland's crown jewels. Co-owners Mike Wiley and Andrew Taylor won the 2017 James Beard Foundation Award for Best Chef: Northeast, and the restaurant consistently ranks among the best in New England.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Raw oysters — the rotating selection is sourced from Maine's finest beds; the Wet Smack from Freeport is a favorite<br/>- Brown butter lobster roll — served warm in a steamed bao bun instead of the traditional split-top; a genuine revelation<br/>- New England clam chowder — clean and briny, not the heavy cream-laden tourist version<br/>- Chilled seafood platters for sharing<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Lunch is the best time to snag a seat without a long wait<br/>- The raw bar counter seats fill up fast — arrive at opening<br/>- Right next door to Duckfat and Mr. Tuna — Middle Street is a lunch destination in itself<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Eventide+Oyster+Co.,+86+Middle+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
