  <Placemark>
    <name>FDR Presidential Library &amp; Museum Hyde Park, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[FDR Presidential Library & Museum<br/><br/>📍 Hyde Park, NY<br/><br/>The first presidential library in the United States, housing FDR's papers and an outstanding museum covering his presidency, WWII, and Eleanor Roosevelt's life.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Allow 2+ hours — the museum is genuinely excellent<br/>- The WWII galleries are particularly well done<br/>- Combined ticket with Springwood and Val-Kill is the best approach<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/FDR+Presidential+Library+&+Museum+Hyde+Park,+NY]]></description>
