  <Placemark>
    <name>First Connecticut Lake Pittsburg NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[First Connecticut Lake<br/><br/>📍 Pittsburg, NH<br/><br/>The largest and lowest of the four Connecticut Lakes at 3,071 acres — the eighth-largest lake entirely within New Hampshire, sitting right at the headwaters of the Connecticut River. Known for landlocked salmon and lake trout; the fly-fishing-only stretch where the river enters the lake (Magalloway Bridge to Green's Point) is a spring and fall favorite. Three public boat launches provide access; ice fishing runs January through March, with average ice-out the first week of May.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Bring fly gear if targeting the salmon run near the inlet — check current fly-fishing-only regulations before dropping bait or lures there.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=45.1563%2C%20-71.1708]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
