  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>First Parish Church Congress St Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[First Parish Church (Congress St)<br/><br/>📍 425 Congress Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>First Parish Church at 425 Congress Street is considered one of Portland's finest examples of Federal Period architecture. Commissioned in 1824 to replace a wooden meeting house called Old Jerusalem, its granite structure allowed it to survive the Great Fire of 1866.<br/><br/>One of the building's most notable features is the Simon Willard clock tower — the last remaining functioning clock tower of its kind.<br/><br/>Fun fact: First Parish Church is the oldest place of worship in the city of Portland.<br/><br/>Note: Also featured on the Hidden Public Spaces walking tour — see First Parish Church Portland ME for garden and tour details.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/First+Parish+Church/@43.6586,-70.2582,17z]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
