      <coordinates>-70.2582109,43.6586135,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>First Parish Church Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[First Parish Church<br/><br/>First Parish Church at 425 Congress Street was built in 1825 to replace Old Jerusalem, the wooden predecessor on the same site. Inside this stunning granite building hangs a 600-pound cut-glass chandelier with a cannonball fused in the chain.<br/><br/>The church has partnered with Portland By The Foot to provide guided tours to the public. Even without a tour, the public is always welcome to enjoy the lovely gardens surrounding the church — a wonderful spot to pause and meditate.<br/><br/>Fun fact: The Maine Constitution was drafted in the original wooden church (Old Jerusalem) in 1820.<br/><br/>Highlights<br/>- 600-pound cut-glass chandelier with embedded cannonball<br/>- Peaceful surrounding gardens (always accessible)<br/>- Guided tours available via Portland By The Foot<br/>- Historic connection to the drafting of the Maine Constitution (1820)<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/First+Parish+Church/@43.6586,−70.2582,17z]]></description>
