    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>First Reformed Church Burial Ground Fishkill NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[First Reformed Church, Burial Ground<br/><br/>📍 Main St, Village of Fishkill, NY 12524<br/><br/>National Register listed. The church is the earliest house of worship in the county. The congregation, formed 1716, began building in 1725 with help from Catharyna Brett, whose body rests under the pulpit. During the Revolution the NY Provincial Congress met here as it formed a new government. The church became a Tory prison, where Enoch Crosby, the American secret agent who inspired Cooper's "The Spy," was imprisoned. At war's end ca. 1785, the devastated building was rebuilt and expanded — the steeple, dating from this era, is a village landmark.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Stop 27 of 38 on the Beacon & Fishkill Heritage Tour (Tour 7).]]></description>
