  <Placemark>
    <name>Fishkill Historic District Fishkill, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Fishkill Historic District<br/><br/>📍 Main St (NY-52), Fishkill, NY 12524<br/><br/>The historic core of Fishkill Village, roughly Main Street between Cary and Hopewell Streets — 108 buildings, mostly Greek Revival, dating from the late 18th to late 19th century. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1973. Once a key Revolutionary War crossroads tied to the nearby Fishkill Supply Depot, today it's a walkable strip of local shops and restaurants with its colonial-era character intact.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Pairs naturally with Van Wyck Homestead, just down Route 9 — do them together as one stop.<br/>- Best experienced as a short walk down Main Street rather than a single ticketed site.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.5334,-73.8990]]></description>
