  <Placemark>
    <name>Flume Bridge Franconia Notch NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Flume Gorge<br/><br/>📍 Flume Visitor Center, Franconia Notch State Park, NH<br/><br/>Discovered in 1808 by 93-year-old "Aunt" Jess Guernsey while fishing, this 800-foot granite gorge originally held a massive suspended boulder wedged between its walls — swept away by a violent 1883 rainstorm that also deepened the gorge and carved Avalanche Falls. Wooden boardwalks now wind through the chasm, crossing the Sentinel Pine Covered Bridge along the loop. A cornerstone of Franconia Notch State Park since its 1928 establishment.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Ticketed attraction with its own visitor center — budget 1.5-2 hours for the full 2-mile loop.<br/>- Can get crowded midday in summer/fall — early morning is best.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0977%2C%20-71.6786]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
