  <Placemark>
    <name>Flume Gorge Visitor Center Franconia NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[It’s really hard to narrow down the absolute best thing to do in Franconia Notch State Park, but if hard-pressed, I’d say that Flume Gorge is probably it. Not only is it great for everyone of all ages and abilities, it really lives up to the hype it receives online. This is such a fun 2-mile walk with not only the actual gorge to experience, but also covered bridges and overlooks with amazing mountain views.<br/><br/>Tip 1: Flume Gorge accepts reservations online that provide you with a 1-hour time slot window on the day you choose. Online tickets are discounted by $3 per person. Walk-in tickets are available at the ticket window, but since they only allow a certain number of people in at each time slot, there is a possibility you will have to wait, or come back another day. This generally only happens during peak season (fall) and on weekends. Click here to make your reservation online.<br/><br/>It’s really hard to narrow down the absolute best thing to do in Franconia Notch State Park, but if hard-pressed, I’d say that Flume Gorge is probably it. Not only is it great for everyone of all ages and abilities, it really lives up to the hype it receives online. This is such a fun 2-mile walk with not only the actual gorge to experience, but also covered bridges and overlooks with amazing mountain views.<br/><br/>Flume Covered Bridge<br/><br/>The next two things on this list are sites within Flume Gorge, but they definitely deserve their own mentions! The first is Flume Covered Bridge, and this is the iconic red covered bridge that most people post about when talking about Flume Gorge. It’s also the first site you’ll see during your walk through the trail.<br/><br/>It’s really hard to narrow down the absolute best thing to do in Franconia Notch State Park, but if hard-pressed, I’d say that Flume Gorge is probably it. Not only is it great for everyone of all ages and abilities, it really lives up to the hype it receives online. This is such a fun 2-mile walk with not only the actual gorge to experience, but also covered bridges and overlooks with amazing mountain views.<br/><br/>Tip 1: Flume Gorge accepts reservations online that provide you with a 1-hour time slot window on the day you choose. Online tickets are discounted by $3 per person. Walk-in tickets are available at the ticket window, but since they only allow a certain number of people in at each time slot, there is a possibility you will have to wait, or come back another day. This generally only happens during peak season (fall) and on weekends. Click here to make your reservation online.<br/><br/>So I would like to set up a system whereby you ingest all of this data, create all of these places, populate the front matter of each. with critical information like the project, the base camp, the type of page that you're looking at. I mean, is it a destination?<br/><br/>Is it a day camp? Is it a point of interest? Is it a daily agenda? Most pages will need coordinates, so I'll need for you to retrieve the coordinates.<br/><br/>Tip 1: Flume Gorge accepts reservations online that provide you with a 1-hour time slot window on the day you choose. Online tickets are discounted by $3 per person. Walk-in tickets are available at the ticket window, but since they only allow a certain number of people in at each time slot, there is a possibility you will have to wait, or come back another day. This generally only happens during peak season (fall) and on weekends. Click here to make your reservation online.]]></description>
