  <Placemark>
    <name>Fore River Sanctuary Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Fore River Sanctuary<br/><br/>📍 Rowe Avenue trailhead, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The Fore River Sanctuary is an 85-acre nature preserve managed by Portland Trails, just a few miles west of downtown. Its network of easy wooded paths winds through mature forest along the Fore River estuary — and at the heart of it sits Jewell Falls, Maine's only urban waterfall.<br/><br/>The falls are modest but genuinely lovely: a 26-foot cascade tucked into a shaded ravine, with a small footbridge and benches. The hike to the falls from the Rowe Avenue trailhead is under a mile each way and suitable for any fitness level.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The full trail network is about 3 miles; the out-and-back to Jewell Falls is ~1.5 miles and takes 30–40 minutes<br/>- Trailhead parking is on Rowe Avenue off Brighton Avenue — small lot, arrive early on weekends<br/>- Bring bug spray in summer — the wetland sections can be buggy<br/>- Dogs welcome on leash<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Fore+River+Sanctuary/@43.6487,-70.3156,15z]]></description>
