  <Placemark>
    <name>Fort George State Park Castine ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Fort George State Park<br/><br/>📍 124 Battle Avenue, Castine ME<br/><br/>The best-preserved British fortification from the War of 1812 in the United States — grass-covered earthwork ramparts enclosing a large parade ground, intact and accessible year-round. Free admission, Maine State Historic Site.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free, flat, and easy — a good quick stop rather than a full outing.<br/>- Combine with a walk through Castine's historic district (100+ documented historic structures) and the Maine Maritime Academy waterfront, both nearby.<br/>- Small parking lot off Wadsworth Cove Street.]]></description>
