  <Placemark>
    <name>Fort Popham Lighthouse Phippsburg ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Fort Popham Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Popham Beach, Phippsburg, ME (mouth of the Kennebec River)<br/><br/>Established October 1899 as a fixed red light to guide vessels through hazardous tidal currents at the Kennebec River's entrance, and upgraded in 1903 with a white pyramidal bell tower and 1,000-pound fog bell. Automation ended the staffed era in 1941, and the light was relocated onto adjacent Fort Popham in 1949 — a modern light still shines from a spindle atop the fort today.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The original lighthouse structure is gone; visit Fort Popham itself, a public park at Popham Beach.<br/>- Combine with a stop at Popham Beach State Park, one of Maine's best sand beaches.]]></description>
