  <Placemark>
    <name>Fort William Henry Pemaquid ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-07T10:15:00<br/><br/>Fort William Henry<br/><br/>📍 Colonial Pemaquid Rd, New Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A stone reconstruction (built 1907) of the original 1692 Fort William Henry — in its day the largest fort in New England — destroyed in the 1696 Siege of Pemaquid. Stands on the original foundation within Colonial Pemaquid State Historic Site.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Rating in question: listed at 4.8; the only independent figure I found was a thin Tripadvisor sample (4.0 over just 4 reviews) since most reviewers rate this as part of the broader Colonial Pemaquid site rather than separately — treat the number with real caution either way.<br/>- Climb the fort's tower for river and harbor views.]]></description>
