    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Frances B. Wood Gouldsboro ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Frances B. Wood<br/><br/>📍 Chicken Mill Road off Route 1 / Fletcher Wood Road, Gouldsboro, ME (shared lot with the National Wildlife Refuge)<br/><br/>438-acre upland watershed with natural streams and bogs supporting deer, beaver, and bobcat — noted warbler habitat, sitting above the Maine Coastal Islands National Wildlife Refuge on West Bay. 1.2-1.5 mi loop.]]></description>
