  <Placemark>
    <name>Frances Perkins Homestead Newcastle ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Frances Perkins Homestead<br/><br/>📍 478 River Road, Newcastle, ME<br/><br/>A National Historic Landmark and the family homestead of Frances Perkins, U.S. Secretary of Labor under FDR and the first woman to serve in a presidential Cabinet — a key architect of Social Security, unemployment insurance, and the 40-hour work week. Operated by the Frances Perkins Center on a working saltwater farm along the Damariscotta River.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Public access is limited — check the Frances Perkins Center's site for seasonal open-house days and guided tour schedules before planning a visit.<br/>- Combine with other Damariscotta/Newcastle stops — it's a short drive from downtown Damariscotta.<br/><br/>More info: https://francesperkinscenter.org/]]></description>
