  <Placemark>
    <name>Franklin Island Lighthouse Port Clyde ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Franklin Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Franklin Island, Muscongus Bay, ~5 miles east of Chamberlain/Port Clyde, ME<br/><br/>Maine's third lighthouse, first built in 1807; the current circular brick tower with a fourth-order Fresnel lens dates to 1855. Automated in 1933, and the island became a National Wildlife Refuge in 1973, now supporting nesting seabirds.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Closed to the public April 1–August 31 for seabird breeding season — covers virtually the whole trip window.<br/>- Best seen by private charter out of Port Clyde.]]></description>
