  <Placemark>
    <name>Frenchman Bay Community Forest Hancock ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Frenchman Bay Community Forest<br/><br/>📍 Route 182, ~1 mi from the Tideway Marketplace (750 US-1, Hancock, ME)<br/><br/>Frenchman Bay Conservancy's 1,400-acre portion of a ~4,500-acre forest within a larger ~25,000-acre undeveloped habitat block — likely the largest in Hancock County within a mile of the coast. Extensive trail network (6.23 mi full loop) for hiking, biking, and snowshoeing; wheelchair/stroller-accessible entry; connects to the Downeast Sunrise Trail.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Wheelchair/stroller-accessible entry point<br/>- Connects to the Downeast Sunrise Trail for a much longer route]]></description>
