  <Placemark>
    <name>George B Dorr Museum of Natural History Bar Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[George B. Dorr Museum of Natural History<br/><br/>📍 College of the Atlantic campus, Bar Harbor, ME<br/><br/>Named for George B. Dorr, the "father of Acadia National Park" — he spent over 40 years and much of his own inherited wealth acquiring and donating the land that became Sieur de Monts National Monument in 1916, then Acadia National Park in 1919. The museum, on the College of the Atlantic campus, has hands-on exhibits on Maine's terrestrial and marine wildlife, run largely by COA students.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Small and quick to visit — good rainy-day or between-hikes stop.<br/>- Pairs naturally with a walk around the COA campus and its waterfront.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3948%2C%20-68.2225]]></description>
