  <Placemark>
    <name>Gifford Woods State Park Killington VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Gifford Woods State Park<br/><br/>📍 Base of Pico Peak, Killington, VT<br/><br/>Established in 1931 with an initial 13-acre purchase, later expanded through further land buys and a donation from Walter K. Barrows. Protects one of Vermont's few remaining old-growth hardwood stands — grand sugar maples, beech, yellow birch, white ash, and hemlock. The 7-acre Gifford Woods Natural Area, designated in 1965 and named a National Natural Landmark in 1980, is kept undeveloped with no trails permitted to preserve it fully; an Old Growth Interpretive Trail with historical/ecological panels runs through the adjacent forest instead.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Good campground base for exploring both the Crossroad of Vermont and Killington-area trails.<br/>- The interpretive trail is short and easy — worth the stop even without camping here.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.6762%2C%20-72.8112]]></description>
