  <Placemark>
    <name>Glen Ellis Falls Pinkham Notch NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Glen Ellis Falls<br/><br/>📍 Pinkham Notch NH<br/><br/>A 65-foot waterfall where the Ellis River shoots through a narrow granite flume and plunges into a pool in a dramatic rocky gorge. One of the most visually powerful waterfalls in the White Mountains — the combination of the narrow slot, the vertical drop, and the surrounding boulders creates something genuinely spectacular. A 10-minute walk from the parking area on Route 16.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The trailhead is on Route 16, 0.6 miles south of the AMC Pinkham Notch Visitor Center.<br/>- An underpass beneath Route 16 accesses the falls — the path is paved and easy.<br/>- Best flow in spring and after heavy rain; still impressive in late summer.<br/>- Easily combined with Tuckerman Ravine or the Mount Washington Auto Road, both minutes away.]]></description>
