  <Placemark>
    <name>Glendarragh Lavender Farm Appleton ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Glendarragh Lavender Farm<br/><br/>📍 151 Searsmont Road, Appleton ME<br/><br/>Maine's first USDA-registered lavender farm — a dozen-plus lavender varieties across a 26-acre farm along the St. George River.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Only open late June through end of July, Mon-Sat 10am-3pm — a much narrower window than everything else on this list. Check the calendar before planning around it.<br/>- They also have a year-round storefront at 22 Main Street, Camden — a much easier fallback if the farm itself doesn't fit your dates.<br/>- Coordinates above are an approximation (Appleton town center) — worth confirming against Google Maps before you go.]]></description>
