  <Placemark>
    <name>Goat Island Lighthouse Cape Porpoise ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Goat Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Goat Island, Cape Porpoise, Kennebunkport, ME<br/><br/>Congress appropriated funds in 1831; the original tower was first lit in August 1833 and replaced by the current brick tower in 1859. It held onto its keeper the longest of any Maine light station, staffed until 1990. Transferred to the Kennebunkport Conservation Trust in 1998 under the Maine Lights Program.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A small dock is usable for 1–2 hours around high tide; resident volunteer keepers offer summer tower tours.<br/>- New England Eco Adventures runs guided boat tours with island landings.<br/>- Best views otherwise are from the water.]]></description>
