  <Placemark>
    <name>Goose Rocks Lighthouse Vinalhaven ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Goose Rocks Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Fox Islands Thoroughfare, between Vinalhaven and North Haven, ME<br/><br/>Completed November 14, 1890, this distinctive 37-foot "spark-plug" iron tower stands on a submerged ledge guarding a key shipping passage. Automated in 1963. In December 1940, substitute keeper Roy Manchester disappeared when his boat apparently exploded en route to the station.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned by Beacon Preservation, Inc. — requires permission, though paid overnight stays are available.<br/>- Isle au Haut Boat Services runs tours that pass the lighthouse; otherwise only reachable by water.]]></description>
