  <Placemark>
    <name>Gorge Path Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Gorge Path<br/><br/>📍 Off Park Loop Road, near the stone bridge over Kebo Brook, Acadia National Park ME<br/><br/>Climbs the narrow, shaded gorge between Cadillac Mountain and Dorr Mountain, staying close to a seasonal stream before the trail's signature feature: more than 1,000 stone steps built into the mountainside. Reaches the saddle between the two peaks, with ocean and island views available from either summit as an add-on.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Coordinates are approximate — trailhead is on Park Loop Road's one-way section, right after crossing the stone bridge over Kebo Brook; roadside parking only<br/>- Can be combined with a Cadillac Mountain or Dorr Mountain summit for full views<br/>- Old-growth forest and the bubbling stream make it a good pick on a hot day, more shaded than most Acadia trails]]></description>
