  <Placemark>
    <name>Granite State Scenic Railway Lincoln NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Granite State Scenic Railway (Hobo Railroad)<br/><br/>📍 64 Railroad Street, Lincoln, NH<br/><br/>A 60–80 minute, 15-mile round-trip vintage train ride along the Pemigewasset River on rail dating to the late 1800s, with views toward Franconia Notch and White Mountain National Forest, crossing numerous trestles. Runs late May through October, plus a Thanksgiving–December "Santa Express." Long operated under the "Hobo Railroad" name before rebranding as part of the Granite State Railway.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Reviews on this one are mixed (low aggregate rating) — worth checking recent reviews before committing, especially if traveling with kids expecting a bigger production.<br/>- Gift shop on site for train-themed souvenirs.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0405%2C%20-71.6792]]></description>
