  <Placemark>
    <name>Granite Store Sullivan ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Granite Store<br/><br/>📍 Sullivan, ME<br/><br/>A historic store building in Sullivan, listed on the National Register of Historic Places — a reminder of the granite-quarrying industry that once drove this stretch of the Down East coast, shipping stone from Sullivan and Sullivan Harbor to build cities up and down the Eastern Seaboard.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A quick roadside historical stop rather than an active retail store today.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.5204%2C%20-68.1988]]></description>
