  <Placemark>
    <name>Great Duck Island Lighthouse Southwest Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Great Duck Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Great Duck Island, ~8.5 miles southeast of Bass Harbor, ME<br/><br/>Placed in operation December 31, 1890 — a 42-foot cylindrical brick tower with a fifth-order lens flashing red. The fog signal here was one of the busiest in the state, sounding up to 1,542 hours a year. Assistant keeper Nathan Adam Reed raised sixteen children on the island and ran a one-room school in a converted barn.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Closed to visitors spring through mid-fall, which covers the trip window — plan on a boat tour or flight rather than a landing.<br/>- Lighthouse cruises from Bar Harbor or aerial flights from Bar Harbor airport offer views.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
