  <Placemark>
    <name>Green Mount Cemetery Montpelier VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Green Mount Cemetery<br/><br/>📍 250 State Street, Montpelier, VT<br/><br/>Established in 1854 on land partly funded by lawyer Calvin Keith, this 35-acre cemetery winds across 2.5 miles of terraced hillside roads. Notable for its sculptural craftsmanship — showcasing Vermont's granite and marble carving traditions, including the William Stowell tomb with hand-cut granite stairs and a life-size statue marking the 1900 grave of seven-year-old Margaret Pitkin. Several Vermont governors and war heroes are buried here, alongside a small 1865 Civil War soldiers' lot donated to the federal government.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A quiet, atmospheric walk rather than a formal attraction — good for those interested in funerary art or Vermont history.<br/>- Pairs naturally with the nearby Vermont State House.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.2577%2C%20-72.5966]]></description>
