  <Placemark>
    <name>Green Mountain Railroad White River Junction VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Green Mountain Railroad (White River Junction)<br/><br/>📍 106 Railroad Row, White River Junction, VT<br/><br/>The Green Mountain Railroad runs three Vermont excursion routes; the White River Flyer departed Union Depot here for Norwich and the Montshire Museum of Science, tracing the Connecticut River with White Mountain foothill views and passing a causeway wildlife sanctuary. A historic 1892 steam engine, "Old 494," is displayed in the adjacent Depot Park.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Recent listings mark the White River Junction operation as closed — verify current status before planning around it; the Green Mountain Railroad's other routes (Burlington–Charlotte, Bellows Falls–Chester) may still be running.<br/>- Depot Park and "Old 494" are worth a quick look even if the excursion train isn't operating.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.6487%2C%20-72.3179]]></description>
