  <Placemark>
    <name>GreenSpark Sustainability Park Waterbury Center VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[GreenSpark Sustainability Park<br/><br/>📍 95 Gregg Hill Rd, Waterbury Center, VT<br/><br/>Opened in 2017 by owner Alex Chernomazov as the country's first interactive sustainability park — the whole site runs entirely off the electric grid on its own solar power. Exhibits let visitors explore renewable energy and green building hands-on, plus a "sustainable garage" showcasing vehicles powered by electricity, wind, and biomass.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Closed on rainy days — check weather and call ahead.<br/>- Guided tours run at 12pm, 2pm, and 4pm.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3896%2C%20-72.7206]]></description>
