  <Placemark>
    <name>Grindle Point Lighthouse Islesboro ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Grindle Point Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Islesboro Island, ME (ferry landing, ~6 miles from Lincolnville)<br/><br/>Appropriated in 1849 and rebuilt in 1875, this brick lighthouse guided ships into Gilkey Harbor during the 19th century, when Islesboro was home to many ship captains. Decommissioned in 1933, sold to the Town of Islesboro for $1,200 in 1934, and reactivated in 1987. The keeper's quarters now house the Sailors' Memorial Museum.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Right next to the ferry landing — no car needed to visit.<br/>- Tower reopened to the public June 29, 2025 after a six-year structural-repair closure.<br/>- Museum open Friday–Sunday, July 1 through Labor Day — squarely within the trip window.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
