  <Placemark>
    <name>Grindstone Neck Golf Course Winter Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Grindstone Neck Golf Course<br/><br/>📍 106 Grindstone Ave, Winter Harbor, ME<br/><br/>Founded in 1891 as part of a Gilded Age summer colony built by a group of Philadelphia and New York families — the Neck once had a 250-room inn, two churches, a casino, and a saltwater pool alongside the course. Alex Findlay redesigned the original holes in the early 1900s. The community faded after the Depression and WWII, then revived starting in the 1980s. Every hole on the nine-hole course has a water view of Winter Harbor or Frenchman Bay's pink granite coastline.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A scenic round even for non-serious golfers, given the water views from every hole.<br/>- Semi-private — check current public access/tee-time policy before planning around it.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3900%2C%20-68.0960]]></description>
