  <Placemark>
    <name>Halfway Rock Lighthouse Casco Bay ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Halfway Rock Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Halfway Rock, ~11 miles east of Portland, ME (Casco Bay)<br/><br/>First lit August 15, 1871, after decades of petitions following shipwrecks in the area. The 76-foot conical granite tower was automated in 1975. It survived a devastating 1962 nor'easter and was privately purchased in 2014 for $283,000, undergoing extensive restoration since.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned; grounds and tower closed to the public.<br/>- View by boat or air — Rocky Coast Cruises out of Portland offers trips that pass it.]]></description>
