  <Placemark>
    <name>Hamilton House South Berwick ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hamilton House<br/><br/>📍 40 Vaughan's Lane, South Berwick, ME<br/><br/>A grand 1785 Georgian mansion set on a bluff over the Salmon Falls River, with 50 acres of grounds — a National Historic Landmark recognized for its maritime trade history and a notable revival garden. Owned and operated by Historic New England as a historic house museum.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open June 1–October 15, Friday–Sunday, 11am–4pm; the grounds themselves are open year-round.<br/>- Admission is free for Historic New England members, $8 for non-members, with senior and group discounts.<br/>- Combine with Hamilton House's near neighbor, the Sarah Orne Jewett House, also in South Berwick and also Historic New England-operated.<br/>- A genuinely quiet, uncrowded stop compared to the more visited coastal Maine landmarks — worth it for the river-bluff setting alone.]]></description>
