  <Placemark>
    <name>Hamlet of Staatsburg NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hamlet of Staatsburg<br/><br/>📍 Old Post Rd, Staatsburg, NY 12580<br/><br/>Thought to be the earliest settlement in Hyde Park, this hamlet along Old Post Rd. was developed around commerce generated by farms and estates. The narrow lane, lined by trees and stone walls, passes the former Union Free School, wooden barns with unique trefoil and quadrifoil windows, Victorian-era houses, and a former stage stop. St. Margaret's Episcopal Church, a mid-19th-century English Gothic adaptation noted for its French medieval stained glass windows (a gift of Ogden Mills), sits nearby — its original home, a small Carpenter Gothic structure, now houses the Hamlet Library.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Stop 9 of 26 on the Hyde Park, Clinton & Pleasant Valley Scenic Tour (Tour 3).]]></description>
