  <Placemark>
    <name>Harbor Ice Cream New Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-07T11:45:00<br/><br/>Harbor Ice Cream<br/><br/>📍 Route 130, New Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A local institution on "the Hill" in New Harbor for over 30 years, serving Gifford's Maine ice cream (plus vanilla/chocolate soft serve, cold brew, and baked goods) just minutes from Pemaquid Point Lighthouse. Picnic tables outside.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Gifford's ice cream — Maine-themed flavors like Moose Tracks and Deer Tracks<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Rating in question: listed at 4.8, but Tripadvisor independently shows 4.3 — a real but not huge gap, plausibly explained by Google running higher than Tripadvisor as it often does.<br/>- Coordinates are an approximate New Harbor village-center match — the exact Route 130 address didn't resolve via geocoding.<br/>- Good stop after Pemaquid Point Lighthouse.]]></description>
