  <Placemark>
    <name>Harts Village Millbrook NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Harts Village<br/><br/>📍 Harts Village Rd, Millbrook, NY<br/><br/>Named for the Hart family, this hamlet was the town's economic center until the mid-19th century, powered by water from numerous falls in the deep gorge along Mill Brook. Hart's grist mill (1755, enlarged 1790) was the first, followed by fulling, dye cutting, saw, cotton and flour mills. Phillip Hart's carefully restored Georgian frame home (National Register, private) sits set back from the road.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Note the Town Park along the route.<br/>- Allyn's Restaurant and Cafe, originally a Methodist church, offers food and tourist information nearby — call 845/677-5888.<br/>- Stop 4 of 17 on the Washington & Amenia Scenic Tour (Tour 4).<br/>- No single street address for this hamlet — coordinates left blank.]]></description>
