  <Placemark>
    <name>Hatchet Mountain Preserve Hope ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hatchet Mountain Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Hatchet Mountain Road (ME-235), Hope ME<br/><br/>A 1.4-mile out-and-back trail rising above Hope Village, with a well-built 0.75-mile switchback trail to viewpoints over Hobbs Pond, Bald and Ragged Mountains, and Camden Hills State Park toward Penobscot Bay. Moderately challenging, about an hour round trip.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Trailhead and parking are on ME-235, 0.6 miles from Hope Center.<br/>- A good option if you want a real hike with a view but shorter/quieter than the Camden Hills trails.<br/>- This is the destination note's own namesake attraction — previously had no Place note at all despite being the reason for the destination's name.]]></description>
