  <Placemark>
    <name>Hatchtown Preserve Bristol ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hatchtown Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Boyd Pond Lane, off Sproul Hill Road, Bristol, ME (coordinate approximate — road-level geocode, not the exact parking/kiosk spot down the lane)<br/><br/>35-acre preserve along the Pemaquid River's west side, looping around an 'almost-island.' Gently graded, with a canoe/kayak pull-out. Spring wildflowers (blue bead lily, trout lily, goldenseal). ~0.6 mi, 22 ft gain.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Coordinate is approximate<br/>- Good canoe/kayak put-in if paddling the Pemaquid River<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/hatchtown-preserve/]]></description>
