  <Placemark>
    <name>Head of Tide Preserve Belfast ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Head of Tide Preserve<br/><br/>📍 89 Doak Rd, Belfast, ME<br/><br/>Protects part of the Passagassawakeag River shoreline plus old fields and forest, abutting the Stover Preserve within the Passagassawakeag Greenway. The River Loop travels the high riverbank; the Shed of Tides, a tool-storage and small-event space, anchors the Land Trust's Waldo County work. Conserved 2009 with Land for Maine's Future support.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- River Loop (1.1 mi, moderate) and Woods Loop (1.0 mi, easy, old road) — pick based on time/energy<br/>- Pairs naturally with Stover Preserve, right next door<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
