  <Placemark>
    <name>Hedgehog Mountain Albany NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hedgehog Mountain<br/><br/>📍 UNH Trail, near Passaconaway Campground, Albany, NH<br/><br/>A 2,532-foot peak named for the University of New Hampshire Forestry Camp once located nearby. The 4.7-mile UNH Trail loop climbs about 1,500 feet in its first 1.5 miles, then rewards with views from Hedgehog's ledges, the summit, and Allen's Ledge — looking south and east toward Mount Passaconaway and the Sandwich Wilderness.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Best May through October; a steep climb early on, so pace accordingly.<br/>- Trailhead parking is the Downes Brook Trail lot off the Kancamagus near Passaconaway Campground.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.9731%2C%20-71.3628]]></description>
