  <Placemark>
    <name>Hendricks Head Lighthouse Southport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hendricks Head Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Southport Island, near West Southport, ME<br/><br/>Erected in 1829 by Joseph Berry to guide vessels up the Sheepscot River toward Wiscasset's shipbuilding center. Best known for the contested legend of a baby rescued from the sea around 1870 during keeper Jaruel Marr's tenure. Rebuilt with a brick tower in 1875, with a fog bell tower added in 1891.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned; grounds, dwelling, and tower closed to the public.<br/>- View from West Southport Beach off Route 27, or from Maine Maritime Museum / Cap'n Fish's boat cruises.]]></description>
