  <Placemark>
    <name>Henrys Public House Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Henry's Public House<br/><br/>📍 375 Fore Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The three-story brick building at 375 Fore Street features lancet windows — long, narrow windows with pointed arches at the top — a hallmark of Gothic Revival architecture.<br/><br/>Before housing Henry's Public House (an Old Port pub and restaurant), the building was home to the Portland Seamen's Friend Society, an organization that provided food, entertainment, lodging, spiritual needs, and general advocacy for sailors.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/375+Fore+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
