  <Placemark>
    <name>Heron Neck Lighthouse Vinalhaven ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Heron Neck Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Green Island, ~2 miles southwest of Vinalhaven, ME<br/><br/>First exhibited February 6, 1854, this cylindrical brick tower sits atop a sand-colored granite cliff guiding mariners into Carver's Harbor. For over three years, keeper Levi Farnham's Newfoundland dog Nemo was trained to bark at ship whistles in fog — an unofficial "fog-bark" with no government budget behind it. After a 1989 fire, the Island Institute's stewardship here helped launch the statewide Maine Lights Program.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned; grounds and tower closed.<br/>- Isle au Haut Boat Services runs excursions that pass the lighthouse by water.]]></description>
