  <Placemark>
    <name>High Falls D&amp;H Canal Locks High Falls, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[High Falls D&H Canal Locks<br/><br/>📍 High Falls, NY<br/><br/>Remarkable 19th-century Delaware & Hudson Canal locks preserved in situ — a rare intact example of early American industrial infrastructure with short walking paths along the original canal.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free to visit; interpretive walk takes 30–45 minutes<br/>- Stone masonry from the 1820s is surprisingly impressive up close<br/>- Combine with the Depuy Canal House just steps away for lunch or dinner<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/High+Falls+D&H+Canal+Locks+High+Falls,+NY]]></description>
