  <Placemark>
    <name>Hodson and Rheault Preserve Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hodson and Rheault Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Molyneaux Rd, Camden, ME (off Washington St/Route 105, ~2.5 mi out, then 0.6 mi on Molyneaux Rd)<br/><br/>A hemlock grove and historic mill site along Sucker Brook. The easy 0.75 mi Hodson Loop passes mature hardwoods and apple trees; the difficult 1.2 mi Rheault Trail climbs the forested Rheault easement to the summit of Howe Hill, a managed organic blueberry barren — no dogs or hunting permitted, please stay on trail through the working farm.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- No dogs or hunting permitted<br/>- Stay on the marked trail through the Rheault easement — it's a working blueberry farm<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
