  <Placemark>
    <name>Huguenot Street New Paltz, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Huguenot Street<br/><br/>📍 New Paltz, NY<br/><br/>America's oldest street with original stone houses dating to the 1690s — seven preserved structures offer guided tours that bring colonial Huguenot history vividly to life.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Guided tours depart from the visitor center on Broadhead Avenue; allow 90 minutes<br/>- One of the most genuinely historic walking streets in America<br/>- Far less crowded than it deserves to be — usually uncrowded even on weekends<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Huguenot+Street+New+Paltz,+NY]]></description>
