  <Placemark>
    <name>Hulls Cove Visitor Center Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hulls Cove Visitor Center<br/><br/>📍 Route 3, near the north entrance to Park Loop Road, Acadia National Park, ME<br/><br/>Acadia's primary visitor center, right at the start of Park Loop Road. Staffed by rangers who can help plan a route, check current trail/road conditions, and answer questions; shows a short park orientation film. The place to buy an entrance pass in person if you didn't get one online ahead of time.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A natural first stop if starting the Park Loop Road drive from the Bar Harbor side.<br/>- Gets busy midday in peak season — early morning is easiest for a quick in-and-out.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.4090%2C%20-68.2473]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
