  <Placemark>
    <name>Hunters Beach Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hunters Beach<br/><br/>📍 Off Park Loop Road, near Seal Harbor, Acadia National Park, ME<br/><br/>A short, pleasant forested walk leads to a secluded cove covered in ocean-tumbled cobblestones, with a small brook running through the rocks into the sea. As the surf comes and goes, the cobbles shift and clink together — a distinctive, almost musical soundscape. Quieter and far less crowded than Sand Beach.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Not a swimming beach — cold water and a rocky (not sandy) shore; come for the sound and scenery.<br/>- Watch your footing on wet cobbles, which shift underfoot.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.2959%2C%20-68.2189]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Beach</value></Data>
