  <Placemark>
    <name>Huston Landing Damariscotta ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Huston Landing<br/><br/>📍 Bristol Road (Route 129), 1.6 mi south of Business Route 1, Damariscotta, ME<br/><br/>10-acre preserve (2006 gift) with a tombolo (sandy isthmus to an island), a glacial erratic marking a trail junction, 500+ ft of Damariscotta River frontage, and a horseshoe-crab spawning shoreline. ~0.4 mi round trip, 118 ft gain.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Good sunset viewing spot — westerly river views<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/huston-landing/]]></description>
