  <Placemark>
    <name>Hyde Park Village Center NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Hyde Park Village Center<br/><br/>📍 Harvey St to Market St, Hyde Park, NY 12538<br/><br/>Delightful 19th-century houses are found in a 4-block area. The Hyde Park Elementary School (1940, built during the Roosevelt administration), the James Roosevelt Memorial Library (1927, a gift from Sara Delano Roosevelt to honor her husband), the Town Hall (1968), and the Hyde Park Post Office (1940, a WPA structure and personal project of FDR) mark the original business center. The Reformed Dutch Church (1826) serves the congregation formed 1790.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Victorian commercial buildings line the original business center.<br/>- Stop 4 of 26 on the Hyde Park, Clinton & Pleasant Valley Scenic Tour (Tour 3).]]></description>
