  <Placemark>
    <name>Ice Caves Trail Cragsmoor NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Ice Caves Trail<br/><br/>📍 Sam's Point Preserve, Cragsmoor, NY<br/><br/>The main loop trail at Sam's Point Preserve, leading through the Ellenville Fault Ice Caves — a series of deep fissures and passageways in the conglomerate bedrock, cool enough that ice can linger well into summer. Often combined into a loop with Lake Maratanza, the highest lake on the ridge.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Bring a flashlight and a layer — the caves stay cold even on hot days.<br/>- Some passages involve ladders and tight squeezes; not ideal for claustrophobia.<br/>- Pairs naturally with a Lake Maratanza loop from the same Sam's Point trailhead.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.6923%2C%20-74.3735]]></description>
