  <Placemark>
    <name>Indian Island Lighthouse Rockport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Indian Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Rockport Harbor, Rockport, ME<br/><br/>Congress appropriated funds in 1849 for a lighthouse at the entrance to Rockport Harbor. Discontinued in 1859 due to proximity to other lights, then restored in 1875 as lime shipping revived the harbor's traffic. Operated until 1933, then sold at auction in 1934 for $1,025 to a Chicago buyer — it's remained in the same family since, and appeared in the 2001 film In the Bedroom.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned, no public access.<br/>- Best viewed from the water via Camden Harbor Cruises, or from shore near Rockport.]]></description>
