  <Placemark>
    <name>Isle au Haut Ferry Stonington ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Isle au Haut Ferry<br/><br/>📍 Stonington ME<br/><br/>The Isle au Haut Boat Services mail boat departs Stonington daily for the 45-minute crossing to Isle au Haut — a remote island where roughly a third of the land is a wild and almost entirely undeveloped section of Acadia National Park. The NPS limits day visitors to 48 people per day; advance reservations required May through October.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Reserve NPS day-use permits well in advance at recreation. — they sell out weeks ahead.<br/>- The ferry drops at Town Landing; the NPS section is a 4-mile walk or bike ride south at Duck Harbor.<br/>- Bring everything you need — the island has almost no services for day visitors.<br/>- The remoteness and quiet are the point: this is what the rest of Acadia looked like before the crowds.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
