    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Isle au Haut Lighthouse Isle au Haut ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Isle au Haut Lighthouse (Robinson Point)<br/><br/>📍 Robinson Point, Isle au Haut, ME<br/><br/>Completed December 30, 1907, this 40-foot granite and brick tower with a fifth-order Fresnel lens guided fishing boats into the harbor during fierce northeast snowstorms. Only two head keepers ever served here before automation in 1933. The Town of Isle au Haut took ownership in 1998 and led a major restoration in 2021.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Reach via the Isle au Haut ferry from Stonington, then walk to the point; grounds open, dwelling and tower closed.<br/>- Isle au Haut Boat Services runs scheduled trips that include a view of the lighthouse.]]></description>
