  <Placemark>
    <name>JB Brown Memorial Block Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[J.B. Brown Memorial Block<br/><br/>📍 Congress Street & Casco Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The J.B. Brown Memorial Block at Congress and Casco Streets is one of the few commercial buildings in Portland designed in the Queen Anne style. This style — which favors fine details, asymmetry, and broken rooflines — was more commonly applied to residential buildings, making this block a rare commercial example.<br/><br/>Fun fact: Many of Portland's historic buildings display two dates — the older is when originally constructed, and the newer is when reconstructed after the Great Fire of 1866.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/JB+Brown+Memorial+Block,+Congress+St+and+Casco+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
