  <Placemark>
    <name>Jackson Corners &amp; Gaddes Store Red Hook NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Jackson Corners & Gaddes Store<br/><br/>📍 CR 56 at CR 50, Red Hook, NY<br/><br/>Jackson Corners was an important stop on the Nobletown stage road to northern New England before the end of the 18th century. Gaddes Store (1773) was one of many inns along the route, spaced roughly ten miles apart so horses could be changed and passengers allowed to stretch. A few hundred feet into Columbia County leads to the Taconic Parkway.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Also en route: the Roeliff Jansen Kill and bridge, marking the northernmost border when Dutchess County was formed in 1683.<br/>- Stop 19 of 33 on the Rhinebeck, Red Hook & Milan Scenic Tour (Tour 1).]]></description>
