  <Placemark>
    <name>James Baird State Park LaGrange NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[James Baird State Park<br/><br/>📍 Freedom Plains, LaGrange, NY<br/><br/>James Baird, construction engineer who built the Lincoln Memorial in Washington, D.C., gave the lands to the State for a park in 1939. Beautiful grounds open year round; picnic areas, shelters, trails, restaurant (seasonal). Fees for golf course.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Call 845/452-1489 for visitor information.<br/>- Stop 25 of 33 on the Poughkeepsie & LaGrange Scenic Tour (Tour 5).]]></description>
