  <Placemark>
    <name>Jean S. Picker Memorial Garden Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Jean S. Picker Memorial Garden & Children's Garden<br/><br/>📍 Camden Public Library grounds, Camden, ME<br/><br/>A smaller, quieter garden space on the Camden Public Library grounds, adjoining a Children's Garden — part of the same library complex as the better-known Amphitheatre & Fawn's Garden (the Fletcher Steele-designed horseshoe theater), but a distinct, smaller corner of it. Worth noting: independent research on this specific garden by name is thin online — most sources reference the library's "Jean Picker Room" (an indoor space) rather than a standalone outdoor garden, so treat the exact scope here as approximate until seen in person.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free access, same grounds as the Amphitheatre — easy to combine both in one stop.<br/>- If it turns out to be the same space as the Amphitheatre/Fawn's Garden rather than a distinct corner, that's fine — either way it's worth the short walk from Main Street.<br/>- Good for a quiet few minutes away from the harbor crowds.]]></description>
