  <Placemark>
    <name>Jeffersonville Bridge Cambridge VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Jeffersonville Bridge<br/><br/>📍 Cambridge Junction Road, off Route 15, Cambridge, VT<br/><br/>Also known as the Cambridge Junction Bridge or Poland Covered Bridge, this 152.5-foot, one-lane Burr arch truss span over the Lamoille River was built in 1887 by George Washington Holmes, giving communities west of the river access to the Cambridge Junction railroad station. Combines an arch-bridge design with King Post-style trusswork. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1974; underwent a two-stage restoration in 2001 that stabilized and raised the structure three feet.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A classic Vermont covered-bridge photo stop, off the main Route 15 corridor.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.6492%2C%20-72.8308]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
