  <Placemark>
    <name>Jericho Mountain State Park Berlin NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Jericho Mountain State Park<br/><br/>📍 Berlin, NH<br/><br/>Acquired by the state in 2005 and redesigned around motorized recreation, this is New Hampshire's only major state-owned ATV riding area — 50 to 60 miles of trail for ATVs, UTVs, trail bikes, and snowmobiles, plus the first public-land 4x4 Jeep and truck trail in the Northeast, an official Jeep off-roading Badge of Honor route. Riders can connect straight into 1,000+ miles of Coös County OHRV trails, reaching Gorham, Errol, Pittsburg, and even Maine and Vermont without trailering. The campground has 20 sites (including cabins and Adirondack shelters) with a modern shower/laundry building, plus a day-use beach and boat launch.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Bring your own OHV — this is a trail network, not a rental operation on site (check locally for nearby rental options if needed).<br/>- The 4x4 trail is a genuine technical off-road route, not a casual scenic drive — know your vehicle's capability first.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.4670%2C%20-71.2228]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
