  <Placemark>
    <name>John and Peg Sproul Preserve Bristol ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[John and Peg Sproul Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Old County Road, ~1.5 mi from Bristol Library, Bristol, ME (coordinate approximate)<br/><br/>50-acre preserve (2008 gift) bordering both Ross Pond (gentle loop, beaver dams) and Boyd Pond (steeper loop, small sandy beach) — moss/fern-covered ledges and prime porcupine habitat. ~0.7-0.9 mi total across two loops.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Coordinate is approximate<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/john-and-peg-sproul-preserve/]]></description>
