  <Placemark>
    <name>Johnson Railroad Depot Site Johnson VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Johnson Railroad Depot (Site)<br/><br/>📍 Railroad Street, Johnson, VT<br/><br/>Built in 1887, this Victorian railroad depot was once the gateway carrying Johnson's industrial products to national markets via the St. Johnsbury and Lamoille County Railroad. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1980 — but the depot building has since been demolished, and a modern building now occupies the site. The old rail corridor is today the Lamoille Valley Rail Trail, which passes right through the heart of Johnson.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Nothing historic remains standing here — treat this as a site marker for the rail trail's history rather than a visitable structure.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.6311%2C%20-72.6875]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
