  <Placemark>
    <name>Jolie Rogers Raw Bar Wiscasset ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Jolie Rogers Raw Bar<br/><br/>📍 8 Railroad Ave, Wiscasset, ME<br/><br/>An oyster bar right on the Sheepscot River, opened by longtime friends Ryan Jolie and Andy Rogers — Rogers is one of the country's best oyster shuckers, with a competitive shucking background. Sleek, minimalist, hidden-gem feel tucked on a side street with river views. Menu changes seasonally; beyond oysters, expect tuna tartare, scallop ceviche, and other small plates. Also sells oysters and their signature sauces retail. Rated 5/5 on Restaurant Guru across dozens of reviews — widely considered one of the top oyster bars in Maine.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Fresh oysters — the entire reason to go, and the reviews back it up<br/>- Tuna tartare<br/>- Scallop ceviche<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Small, easy-to-miss location on a side street off the main drag — worth seeking out deliberately, it's not a walk-by discovery.<br/>- Good pairing with Red's Eats or Panacea if you want lobster roll/chowder plus a proper raw bar course on the same Wiscasset stop.<br/>- Also sells oysters/sauces to take home if you want to bring some back to the base camp kitchen.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.jolierogersrawbar.com/]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
