  <Placemark>
    <name>Jordan Cliffs Trail Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Jordan Cliffs Trail<br/><br/>📍 Trailhead near Jordan Pond North Lot, Acadia National Park, ME<br/><br/>A cliffside trail near Jordan Pond, completely overshadowed by the adjacent and far more famous Jordan Pond Path and the Bubbles. One write-up calls it "incredibly underrated" — same neighborhood as Acadia's most popular spot, a fraction of the foot traffic.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Involves iron rungs/ladders on exposed cliff sections — not a casual flat walk despite being near Jordan Pond<br/>- Access via the Jordan Pond North Lot / Spring Trail]]></description>
