  <Placemark>
    <name>Jordan Pond Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Jordan Pond<br/><br/>📍 Acadia National Park ME<br/><br/>One of the most photographed spots in Acadia — a glacially-carved pond with the classic reflection view of the twin granite domes known as the Bubbles. The Jordan Pond House, a historic tea house on the south shore, has served popovers and tea on the lawn since the 1890s. The 3.3-mile Jordan Pond Path circles the shoreline, with a boardwalk section through the boulder field at the north end.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Jordan Pond House popovers with butter and jam are the classic order — expect a wait in peak season, especially for lawn seating.<br/>- The full loop trail (3.3 mi) is flat and easy except for the north-end boulder field, which has a boardwalk but requires some care underfoot.<br/>- Parking fills early; this is one of the busiest stops on Park Loop Road.<br/>- The Bubbles Divide trail connects from the north end if you want a short add-on hike with a summit view.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Scenic</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>waves</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>green</value></Data>
