      <coordinates>-68.253658,44.320484,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Jordan Pond House Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[View website<br/><br/>Jordan Pond House<br/><br/>📍 2928 Park Loop Rd, Seal Harbor, ME (Jordan Pond's south shore, Acadia National Park)<br/><br/>A restaurant and gift shop with roots to 1893, when first proprietor Nellie McIntire began baking popovers for visitors. Sits on a hill overlooking a lawn along Jordan Pond, with the Bubbles visible across the water — the classic Acadia photo backdrop. Most tables are held for walk-ins rather than reservations.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Popovers with butter and jam — the signature order, served with afternoon tea<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open ~11am–5pm; most tables are walk-in, expect ~40 minute waits in peak season<br/>- One of the busiest stops on Park Loop Road — the parking lot fills early<br/>- Reviews are mixed (3.9/5) — the tradition and setting are the draw more than the food/value, worth going in with that expectation<br/><br/>More info: https://jordanpondhouse.com/]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-red</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Restaurant</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>utensils</value></Data>
