  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Jordan's Restaurant - Breakfast - Lobster Rolls - Burgers - Pancakes - Sandwiches 1 Bar Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Open in Google Maps<br/><br/>What It Is & What It's Best Known For<br/><br/>Jordan's Restaurant is a casual breakfast and lunch diner on Cottage Street in Bar Harbor, Maine. It is unpretentious and long known for its wild Maine blueberry pancakes. The menu includes lobster rolls, omelets (Maine delight, lobster cheese, western), quiche, waffles, home fries, bacon, and clam chowder. The restaurant celebrates its 50th anniversary in 2026.<br/><br/>Typical Customers<br/><br/>The restaurant attracts tourists (especially those visiting Cadillac Mountain for sunrise), families with children, locals who view it as "the heart of this town," and travelers seeking affordable, no-frills breakfast experiences.<br/><br/>Overall Vibe<br/><br/>Casual and bustling with a "small-town feel" and "old school vibe." The atmosphere is informal and fast-paced—customers are told to "sit wherever you like." The energy is lively with staff "hustling and enjoying their work." Decidedly budget-friendly and unpretentious, described as "no frills, no foam art, just real food."<br/><br/>Strongest Positives (from reviews)<br/><br/>1. Wild Maine blueberry pancakes are exceptional – Mentioned in 393 reviews, guests consistently praise them as "delicious" and "exceptional." The wild Maine blueberries are "tiny but so flavorful." Blueberry muffins and waffles are similarly praised as "loaded with blueberries."<br/>    <br/>2. Outstanding value and affordability – Reviewers call it "the best and probably cheapest breakfast" in town. At $10–20 per person, the generous portions deliver excellent value. One reviewer noted it as "the best and probably cheapest breakfast we had while in town."<br/>    <br/>3. Genuinely friendly staff and welcoming local character – Staff are described as "very kind," "super friendly," and helpful with local tips. The owner and crew are viewed as a "family" that treats both locals and visitors with warmth. One local called it "definitely this gem" and "the heart of this town."<br/>    <br/>4. Excellent omelets and diverse menu beyond blueberries – Omelets (Maine delight, lobster cheese, lobster mushroom) are consistently praised as "delicious." Quiche, lobster rolls, home fries, bacon, and clam chowder receive positive mentions for quality and portion size.<br/>    <br/><br/>Most Common Issues or Downsides (from reviews)<br/><br/>1. High-volume service creates pressure and inconsistency – One reviewer with a young child reported "bad" service and felt "pressured to be quick and get out as soon as possible." Another noted the place is "so busy that we felt pressured to be quick." The owner acknowledged poor service "is not the norm," but the volume operation can affect the dining pace.<br/>    <br/>2. Some menu items fall short – Haddock chowder was described as "way too watery and quite disappointing." One reviewer found blueberry pancakes "way overhyped" and "ok" rather than exceptional, noting they "are not sweet."<br/>    <br/>3. Popularity creates crowds and waits – The restaurant is extremely busy during peak times, which contributes to the rushed atmosphere despite the casual seating policy.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Jordan's+Restaurant+-+Breakfast+-+Lobster+Rolls+-+Burgers+-+Pancakes+-+Sandwiches/@44.3887812,-68.2110299,595m/data=!3m2!1e3!5s0x4caebf79398c221d:0x760efaa8d0294f9f!4m21!1m7!3m6!1s0x4caebf005b379c81:0xc72ad7b501a68b23!2sDinner!8m2!3d44.3886633!4d-68.2140236!16s%2Fg%2F11vxy0p6s6!3m12!1s0x4caebf7c6dc34add:0xa44453f85df41378!5m4!1s2026-09-21!2i4!4m1!1i2!8m2!3d44.3888274!4d-68.2100349!9m1!1b1!16s%2Fg%2F1tdpr7xc?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-red</styleUrl>
