  <Placemark>
    <name>Kaaterskill Falls Haines Falls, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kaaterskill Falls<br/><br/>📍 Haines Falls, NY<br/><br/>New York's tallest waterfall at 260 feet in two stages — one of the most photographed natural landmarks in the state and a defining image of the Hudson River School painters.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Laurel House Road trail: 1.4 miles round trip, moderate; parking on Route 23A fills by 9 AM weekends<br/>- Late September shows early fall color; peak foliage typically early October<br/>- The upper falls ledge is accessible; the lower pool requires a short scramble<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Kaaterskill+Falls+Haines+Falls,+NY]]></description>
