  <Placemark>
    <name>Kancamagus Highway Rocky Gorge Scenic Area Albany NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Rocky Gorge Scenic Area<br/><br/>📍 Kancamagus Highway, 8 miles west of Conway, NH<br/><br/>A narrow, glacier-carved gorge on the Swift River where water rushes through even during droughts. A paved, wide, accessible walkway leads to an overlook of a 15-foot waterfall and rapids, with a footbridge crossing the gorge for a closer view. The 0.7-mile Lovequist Loop continues around Falls Pond beyond the falls and connects to the Nanamocomuck Ski Trail in winter.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Heavily visited — expect crowds, especially weekends. A parking pass (self-pay station) is required.<br/>- Restrooms and a picnic area on site; benches along the accessible path.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0017%2C%20-71.2773]]></description>
