  <Placemark>
    <name>Kensico Dam Plaza Valhalla, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kensico Dam Plaza<br/><br/>📍 Valhalla, NY<br/><br/>A wide public plaza and park at the foot of the Kensico Dam, a massive early-1900s granite structure that impounds the reservoir supplying part of New York City's water. The plaza itself is popular for walking, picnics, and events.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Large open lawn hosts concerts and festivals in summer — check for events before visiting if you want a quiet stop.<br/>- Marks the southern end of this Taconic Byway list, close to Cranberry Lake Preserve.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.072009,-73.768234]]></description>
