    <name>Keyes Woods Preserve Bristol ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Keyes Woods Preserve<br/><br/>📍 185 Poor Farm Road, Bristol, ME<br/><br/>70-acre property (2018) with historic rock walls and foundations, and 1,900+ ft of Pemaquid River shoreline — the stream confluence is a real waterfowl hotspot. ~2.2 mi + 0.3 mi loops, 101 ft gain.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- No dogs permitted, to protect wildlife<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/keyes-woods-preserve/]]></description>
