  <Placemark>
    <name>Kimball Castle Gilford NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Kimball Castle<br/><br/>📍 Gilford, NH (hillside above Lake Winnipesaukee)<br/><br/>Railroad magnate Benjamin Ames Kimball began building this Rhine-castle-inspired summer estate in 1894 and used it until his death in 1920. After leaving the Kimball family in 1960 it fell into decades of disrepair and vandalism, though it remained listed on the National Register of Historic Places (1982). A fire on August 27, 2025 destroyed the castle — it's now considered a total loss, with demolition likely.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- As of this trip, there's no structure left to see — check current status before planning a stop, since the site may be inaccessible or fenced off pending demolition.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.5801%2C%20-71.3795]]></description>
