  <Placemark>
    <name>Ladies Delight Lighthouse Lake Cobbosseecontee ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Ladies Delight Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Lake Cobbosseecontee, ~2 miles west of Augusta, ME<br/><br/>Built in 1908 by the Cobbosseecontee Yacht Club, this 16-foot stone lighthouse marks a small islet where steamboat passengers once made comfort stops — local legend says that's the origin of the name. Restored since 2001, including structural corrections and a new lantern room. Maintained by the Cobbosseecontee Lake Association.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Inland, well off the coastal route — the only lake lighthouse on Maine's list, not a coastal one.<br/>- Needs a boat to see well; rentals available from Lakeside Lodge and Marina.]]></description>
