  <Placemark>
    <name>Lake Winnipesaukee Meredith NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Lake Winnipesaukee<br/><br/>📍 Central New Hampshire<br/><br/>New Hampshire's largest lake, stretching about 21 miles and covering 72 square miles, dotted with 253 islands. The whole 111-mile Lakes Region Tour byway essentially circles this lake and its bays, passing through Wolfeboro, Alton, Laconia, Meredith, and other shoreline towns.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The M/S Mount Washington cruise ship (departing Weirs Beach) is the classic way to see the whole lake at once.<br/>- Views vary dramatically by town — Wolfeboro and Meredith have walkable downtown waterfronts, while Alton and Center Harbor are quieter.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.6349%2C%20-71.4017]]></description>
