  <Placemark>
    <name>Lewis Art Gallery Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Lewis Art Gallery<br/><br/>Located inside the Portland Public Library at 5 Monument Square, the Lewis Art Gallery is a hidden gem. The gallery is on the bottom floor, open to the public, and features a new exhibit each month.<br/><br/>Beyond the gallery, the library itself boasts art on every floor — take a slow, meandering tour through the building to see how many pieces you can spot.<br/><br/>The library is also a great place to:<br/>- Browse a wide collection of books, music, and more<br/>- Use free internet access<br/>- Attend events throughout the week<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free admission to both the gallery and the library<br/>- Check the library's events calendar for gallery opening receptions<br/>- New exhibit installed each month — worth visiting on multiple trips if staying nearby<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Portland+Public+Library/@43.658,−70.2595,17z]]></description>
