  <Placemark>
    <name>Liberty Springs Trailhead Franconia Notch NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Liberty Springs Trailhead<br/><br/>📍 Just north of the Flume Visitor Center, Franconia Notch State Park, NH<br/><br/>A hard 8.6-mile round trip (part of the Appalachian Trail) climbing 2,933 feet to 4,459-foot Mount Liberty — a steep, continuous rock-staircase climb for nearly two miles after the initial approach. The summit offers 360-degree views of the Kinsman Range, Cannon Cliffs, Franconia Notch, and the Pemigewasset Wilderness. The Liberty Spring Tentsite, about 1.5 miles up, is a popular overnight stop with platforms and reliable water.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A serious 5+ hour hike — this is not a casual Notch stop.<br/>- Access via the bike path from the Flume Visitor Center parking, not directly off the highway.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.1100%2C%20-71.6808]]></description>
