  <Placemark>
    <name>Life is Good 428 Fore Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Life is Good (E. Klaman Bottle Building)<br/><br/>📍 428 Fore Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>In 1924, Nathan Wood & Son called 428 Fore Street home — their business included a wide array of "remedies" or botanic medicines. According to property tax assessment records from that year, the building was valued at $5,251.<br/><br/>Today it is known as the E. Klaman Bottle Building, named after the bottle recycler that occupied the storefront in the second half of the 20th century. The building now houses a Life is Good retail store.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/428+Fore+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
