  <Placemark>
    <name>Lincoln Woods Trail Lincoln NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Lincoln Woods Trail<br/><br/>📍 Kancamagus Highway, ~4-5 miles east of Lincoln, NH<br/><br/>An easy, family-friendly walk with under 300 feet of elevation gain, following the grade of the old East Branch and Lincoln Railroad (built 1894) alongside the East Branch of the Pemigewasset River. This trailhead is the main gateway into the Pemigewasset Wilderness — the second-largest Forest Service wilderness area east of the Mississippi and the largest in the Northeast — with junctions branching to numerous peaks and trails beyond.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Check current conditions before visiting — a stretch of trail (Route 112 junction to the Osseo trail junction) is scheduled for restoration closure June 15–November 2026; parking and the suspension bridge/East Side Trail should still be accessible.<br/>- A good easy option if you want a taste of the Pemigewasset Wilderness without a serious hike.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0639%2C%20-71.5877]]></description>
