  <Placemark>
    <name>Little Hunter's Beach Acadia ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Little Hunter's Beach<br/><br/>📍 Acadia National Park Loop, southeastern edge, Mount Desert Island, ME<br/><br/>While tourists flock to Sand Beach, locals head to this hidden, cobblestone-covered cove nestled along the southeastern edge of the island. It's quiet, framed by spruce trees, and rarely crowded.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Located off the main Loop Road; requires a bit of searching to find<br/>- Cobblestone beach is unique and photogenic<br/>- Bring water shoes; the stones can be rough<br/>- Early morning or late afternoon is best for avoiding crowds<br/>- Part of Acadia National Park, so no entry fee required]]></description>
