  <Placemark>
    <name>Little Long Pond &amp; Rockefeller Boathouse Seal Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Little Long Pond & Rockefeller Boathouse<br/><br/>📍 Main Gate, Route 3 at Bracy Cove, Seal Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A former Rockefeller family estate pond, now part of the Mount Desert Land & Garden Preserve, reached via carriage road from the Main Gate on Route 3 at Bracy Cove. No bicycles are allowed on this stretch of carriage road — only foot and horse traffic — which is a big part of why it stays so quiet compared to the Rockefeller carriage roads inside Acadia proper.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- No bikes allowed on this section of carriage road — foot/horse only<br/>- Pairs well with a Day Mountain Trail or Seal Harbor Beach stop nearby<br/>- Coordinate given is the pond itself; parking is at the Main Gate on Route 3]]></description>
