  <Placemark>
    <name>Little Moose Island Tide Walk Schoodic ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Little Moose Island Tide Walk<br/><br/>📍 Blueberry Hill area, Schoodic Peninsula, ME<br/><br/>A unique tide-dependent excursion walking out from Blueberry Hill toward Little Moose Island at low tide. This is an unusual exploratory walk that most visitors never attempt—timing is critical and adds an element of adventure to the Schoodic experience.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- CRITICAL: Time this around low tide only. Check tide charts before planning.<br/>- Depart Blueberry Hill parking area at or near low tide window<br/>- Plan for muddy/rocky terrain; sturdy waterproof boots essential<br/>- Return well before incoming tide—this is not a place to get trapped<br/>- Unique wildlife and geologic exploration opportunity<br/>- Brings a genuine sense of discovery and local knowledge<br/>- Very few tourists ever experience this; highly unique to Schoodic<br/>- Check weather before attempting; rough conditions dangerous at tide transitions]]></description>
