  <Placemark>
    <name>Little River Lighthouse Cutler ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Little River Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Little River Island, Cutler, ME<br/><br/>Congress appropriated funds in 1847 for a conical stone tower to reduce shipwrecks in this fog-prone stretch of coast; an iron tower replaced it in 1876. Automated in 1975 and left to deteriorate until the American Lighthouse Foundation restored the lantern room in 2001, then took ownership in 2002 — the first lighthouse transfer of its kind in New England.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds open June–October when the floating dock is in place; overnight stays available in the restored keeper's house through Friends of Little River Lighthouse.<br/>- Occasional summer open houses include transportation to the island and tower access.<br/>- Bold Coast Charters runs sightseeing trips that pass the light.]]></description>
