  <Placemark>
    <name>Littlefield Preserve Belfast ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Littlefield Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Walter Ash Recreation Area, Swan Lake Ave (Route 141), Belfast, ME<br/><br/>Two waterfront parcels protecting Upper Mason Pond's wetland habitat and scenic views. A landing spot and picnic table make it good for wildlife-watching or a paddle — the Goose River can be paddled all the way from Swanville into the pond. Water access only. Donated 2016 by Carroll and Evelyn Littlefield.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- No trail — water access only, from the Walter Ash Recreation Area (City of Belfast) parking lot<br/>- Paddle route connects from Swanville via the Goose River<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
