  <Placemark>
    <name>Littleton Diner Littleton NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Overview<br/>Type: Diner  <br/>Best known for: Friendly service, classic diner fare  <br/>Location context: Littleton, cozy small-town setting  <br/>Price level: $10–20 per person  <br/>Visit timing: Commonly busy with a quick-moving line on weekends  <br/><br/>Typical Customers<br/>Demographics: Mostly locals  <br/>Group types: Families, couples, friends  <br/>Common occasions: Casual dining, brunch, quick bites  <br/><br/>Vibe & Setting<br/>Atmosphere: Casual, nostalgic  <br/>Noise level: Moderate  <br/>Decor & setting: Indoor seating, diner-style decor  <br/>Service style: Attentive and friendly  <br/><br/>Recommended Dishes<br/>Overall dish consensus  <br/>Reviewers highlight the clam chowder, fish and chips, and homemade hash as must-try items due to their quality and flavor.  <br/><br/>How “top dishes” are determined  <br/>Top dishes are identified based on mentions in user reviews, popular dishes noted in the menu, and items that receive strong praise or appear frequently in photos.  <br/><br/>| Rank | Dish                  | Why it stands out                                       | How often it’s mentioned         | Ideal for                |<br/>|------|----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|-------------------------|<br/>| 1    | Clam Chowder         | Hot and delicious, a comforting classic.              | Mentioned in numerous reviews     | Sharing at the table    |<br/>| 2    | Fish and Chips       | Steaming hot, well-prepared, a diner staple.          | Repeatedly called out as a favorite | Hearty main            |<br/>| 3    | Homemade Hash        | Flavorful with quality ingredients, a breakfast hit.  | Appears in many photos           | Comfort food            |<br/><br/>Good alternates / backup choices  <br/>- Corned Beef Hash and Eggs: Known for being satisfying and hearty.  <br/>- Fried Scallops and Shrimp: While some found it bland, others appreciated it.  <br/><br/>Highlights (non‑dish positives from reviews)<br/>Service: Attentive and fast, contributing to a pleasant dining experience.  <br/>Atmosphere: Nostalgic feel, reminiscent of classic diners, making it a cozy spot.  <br/><br/>Common Issues (from reviews)<br/>Long Waits: Especially on weekends, there can be a line, though it moves quickly.  <br/>Portion Sizes: Some dishes criticized for being small relative to the price.  <br/><br/>Practical Notes<br/>Reservation / wait: Walk-in friendly but expect wait times on weekends.  <br/>Accessibility: Not mentioned  <br/>Parking / transit: Not mentioned  <br/>Best use case: Great for casual brunch with friends, local dining experience.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Littleton+Diner/@44.3069463,-71.7757809,194m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m14!1m7!3m6!1s0x4cb46f2d8d8d7741:0x655c417a30beacd!2sChang+Thai+Cafe!8m2!3d44.3066109!4d-71.7731008!16s%2Fg%2F1tg34trv!3m5!1s0x4cb46f2d7146ab9f:0xc7dbcaf59dedb30b!8m2!3d44.3071708!4d-71.7757229!16s%2Fg%2F1264nnvt5?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMy4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
