  <Placemark>
    <name>Lobster Landing Clinton CT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Lobster Landing<br/><br/>📍 152 Commerce St, Clinton, CT<br/><br/>A rustic, weathered shack on the dock at Clinton Harbor, established in 1995 — the menu is deliberately tiny (lobster rolls, hot dogs, chowder, or sausage & peppers) and built entirely around one thing: a hot buttered lobster roll widely considered among the best in Connecticut. Seating is inside or outside among the boats and waterway. BYOB. Rated 4.5 on Google across 1,569 reviews, ranked #1 of 30 Clinton restaurants on Tripadvisor.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Hot buttered lobster roll — the entire reason to go; there isn't much else on the menu<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- BYOB — bring your own drinks and sides if you want them.<br/>- The menu is genuinely limited (four items) — know that going in rather than expecting variety.<br/>- Right on the Chatham → Hudson Valley transfer route — a natural stop for that drive.<br/>- Reviews are mixed on service speed at peak times; go a little outside the lunch rush if possible.]]></description>
