  <Placemark>
    <name>Locust Grove Estate Poughkeepsie, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Locust Grove Estate<br/><br/>📍 Poughkeepsie, NY<br/><br/>Samuel Morse's 1830s Italianate villa on 200 acres of carriage roads, river overlooks, and formal gardens — where the inventor of the telegraph spent his later years.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds free to walk; mansion tours ticketed<br/>- The carriage roads make for an excellent 2–3 mile walk with Hudson River views<br/>- Combine with the Walkway Over the Hudson — both in south Poughkeepsie<br/>- Also stop 12 of 33 on the Poughkeepsie & LaGrange Scenic Tour (Tour 5)<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Locust+Grove+Estate+Poughkeepsie,+NY]]></description>
