  <Placemark>
    <name>Longfellow House Garden Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Longfellow House Garden<br/><br/>The garden behind the Henry Wadsworth Longfellow House at 489 Congress Street is a favorite of local residents and downtown employees. A brick pathway leads from Congress Street toward the Maine Historical Society library and into the multi-tiered garden — complete with benches, a fountain, and many flowering plants.<br/><br/>Though the garden is only open seasonally, you can always:<br/>- Take in the history of the Longfellow home from the street<br/>- Visit the Maine Historical Society gift store<br/>- Explore the MHS museum next door<br/><br/>Highlights<br/>- Peaceful, multi-tiered historic garden<br/>- Fountain and flowering plantings<br/>- Adjacent to Maine Historical Society library and museum<br/>- Brick pathway connecting Congress Street to the garden<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Check seasonal hours before visiting — garden access is limited outside of summer<br/>- The MHS museum is worth a visit for Portland history<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Wadsworth-Longfellow+House/@43.6568,−70.2603,17z]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
