  <Placemark>
    <name>Longfellow School Rutland VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Longfellow School<br/><br/>📍 6 Church Street, Rutland, VT<br/><br/>Also known as Church Street School, built in 1890 as Rutland's first purpose-built graded school, in the Colonial Revival style — it became a model for schools built afterward in the city. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1976.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A historic building landmark rather than a visitor site — appreciate from the street.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.6087%2C%20-72.9776]]></description>
