  <Placemark>
    <name>Loon Mountain Lincoln NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Loon Mountain<br/><br/>📍 60 Loon Mountain Rd, Lincoln, NH<br/><br/>Founded by former NH Governor and Eisenhower Chief of Staff Sherman Adams in 1958, Loon Mountain opened in December 1966 with 12 trails and a gondola. The current Doppelmayr gondola (1988) still uses some of the original tower bases; it runs in summer and fall for scenic rides to the summit, where trails lead to glacial caves and White Mountains views, alongside winter skiing. Now owned and operated by Boyne Resorts.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Summer/fall gondola rides are a good non-hiking way to get a high-elevation White Mountains view if visiting outside ski season.<br/>- Pairs naturally with Clark's Trading Post and the Granite State Scenic Railway, both minutes away in Lincoln.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0360%2C%20-71.6214]]></description>
