  <Placemark>
    <name>Lubec Channel Lighthouse Lubec ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Lubec Channel Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Lubec Channel, between South Lubec Beach and Campobello Island, Lubec, ME<br/><br/>First exhibited December 31, 1890, to mark the newly dredged channel — one of only three remaining "spark plug"/"wedding cake" style caisson lights on the Maine coast. Head Keeper Loring Myers (1895–1923) invented a non-sinkable lifeboat and made multiple rescues. Automated in 1939; major structural repairs corrected a serious lean in 1992.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned, tower closed — best seen by boat or plane, or distantly from Boot Cove Road.<br/>- The 1,200-pound fog bell is on display at the Lubec Historical Society.<br/>- Easy pairing with West Quoddy Head Light while in Lubec.]]></description>
