  <Placemark>
    <name>Machias Seal Island Lighthouse Cutler ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Machias Seal Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Machias Seal Island, ~12 miles off Cutler, ME (also claimed by Canada)<br/><br/>Both the U.S. and Canada have claimed sovereignty over this island. The original wooden octagonal towers date to 1832; a third-order Fresnel lens was added in 1869 and a powerful steam fog whistle — the strongest then on the Bay of Fundy — in 1873. The current reinforced concrete tower, built in 1915, is still active. The island hosts the largest Atlantic puffin nesting colony south of the Gulf of St. Lawrence.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Visited via puffin tours from Bold Coast Charters (Cutler) or Sea Watch Tours (Grand Manan, Canada); landing is weather-dependent.<br/>- Bar Harbor Whale Watch also runs lighthouse excursions past the island.<br/>- Book puffin tours well ahead — they sell out during nesting season, which overlaps the trip window.]]></description>
