  <Placemark>
    <name>Mackworth Island Falmouth ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mackworth Island<br/><br/>📍 Andrews Avenue causeway, Falmouth, ME (~10 min from downtown Portland)<br/><br/>Mackworth Island is a small state-owned island in Casco Bay connected to Falmouth by a short causeway. The perimeter trail — a 1.5-mile loop — hugs the rocky shoreline almost the entire way, offering 360° views of the bay, the Portland skyline, the Calendar Islands, and the open Atlantic.<br/><br/>The walk is virtually flat, takes about 40 minutes at a leisurely pace, and is consistently rated among the best short walks in Maine. The island also features a fairy house village in the woods near the center — a whimsical tradition maintained by local children.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A Maine state park vehicle pass ($8 non-resident day use) is required at the gate; cash or card accepted<br/>- Arrive before 9 AM on summer weekends — the small parking area fills up fast<br/>- The causeway itself offers good views of Portland Harbor before you even reach the island<br/>- Combine with a Portland Head Light visit (~15 min south) for a full morning outdoors<br/>- Dogs welcome on leash<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Mackworth+Island/@43.7008,-70.2321,15z]]></description>
