  <Placemark>
    <name>Mad River Glen Waitsfield VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mad River Glen<br/><br/>📍 62 Mad River Glen Resort Road, Fayston, VT (near Waitsfield)<br/><br/>Skier-owned since 1995 — the first, and still the only, cooperatively-owned ski area in the United States. That ownership structure shapes the whole experience: low skier density, natural snow prioritized over snowmaking, and a deliberately non-commercial, old-school feel ("Ski it if you can" is the unofficial motto). Its Single Chair, in continuous operation since 1948, is one of only two single-person chairlifts still running in the country (the other is in Cordova, Alaska). Over 80% of the 1,700+ shareholders voted to restore it rather than replace it, raising $1.8 million; the refurbished lift reopened December 15, 2007.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Known for genuinely challenging, natural terrain — not the resort to pick if you want groomed cruisers and snowmaking guarantees.<br/>- Right by Appalachian Gap, so easy to combine both stops on a Route 17 drive.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.1958%2C%20-72.8913]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
