  <Placemark>
    <name>Madame Brett Homestead Beacon NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Madame Brett Homestead<br/><br/>📍 Van Nydeck Ave, Beacon, NY 12508<br/><br/>National Register listed. The oldest house in the county (1709) is a unique frame Dutch vernacular farmhouse. The home of Catharyna and Roger Brett, pioneers in Southern Dutchess, it reflects family fortunes through 7 generations. Cared for by the Melzingah Chapter of the D.A.R. since 1954, it is operated as a house museum with collections of furnishings, clothing and documents. The Tellers, prominent Dutch settlers, married into the Brett family in 1790.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Tours available. Call 845/831-6533 for visitor information.<br/>- Stop 22 of 38 on the Beacon & Fishkill Heritage Tour (Tour 7).]]></description>
