  <Placemark>
    <name>Maiden Cliff Trail Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Maiden Cliff Trail<br/><br/>📍 Trailhead on ME-52, ~2.8 mi from US-1/ME-52 junction, Camden, ME<br/><br/>~1.9 mi round trip, moderate (a short uphill section, well under 3mi). One of the most famous short hikes in Maine — climbs to an 800-foot sheer granite cliff marked by a giant white cross, with staggering panoramic views over Lake Megunticook and the surrounding mountains.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Paved trailhead lot, no restrooms.<br/>- Right in Camden itself — no need to drive far from base camp.]]></description>
