  <Placemark>
    <name>Maine Lobster Festival Rockland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Maine Lobster Festival<br/><br/>📍 Rockland ME<br/><br/>New England's largest seafood festival, held on the Rockland waterfront in late July/early August. Whole live lobsters cooked in the world's largest lobster cooker, served with drawn butter and corn in a waterfront tent. Local schooners in the harbor, Maine-made craft vendors, live music, and the annual Sea Goddess parade. Dates to 1947.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Check exact dates — typically the last week of July into the first weekend of August.<br/>- Buy tickets in advance; the lobster dinner tent sells out by early afternoon on peak days.<br/>- The waterfront location is walkable from the Farnsworth Art Museum.<br/>- Pair with the Breakwater Lighthouse walk, 10 minutes away.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
