  <Placemark>
    <name>Maine State House Augusta ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Maine State House<br/><br/>📍 State Street, Augusta, ME<br/><br/>Maine's working capitol building, constructed from granite quarried nearby in Hallowell. The free self-guided tour (about an hour) takes you through the historic Hall of Flags and up to a rooftop veranda with views over the Kennebec River.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free admission and self-guided tour<br/>- About one hour to explore thoroughly<br/>- Historic granite construction<br/>- Rooftop veranda offers river views<br/>- Combine with nearby Viles Arboretum and Hallowell antiques]]></description>
