  <Placemark>
    <name>Mariners Church Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mariner's Church<br/><br/>📍 366–376 Fore Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The Mariner's Church at 366–376 Fore Street was constructed in 1828 and designed by Asa Clapp. It sustained extensive damage during the Great Fire of 1866, along with many buildings along Fore Street.<br/><br/>In 1969, the building was saved from demolition when the entire block was purchased by C.H. Robinson. The Mariner's Church provided food, entertainment, lodging, spiritual needs, and general advocacy for sailors — serving the Portland Seamen's Friend Society.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/366+Fore+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
