  <Placemark>
    <name>Marsh Meadow Preserve Knox ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Marsh Meadow Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Waldo Ave/Route 137, Knox, ME (10.4 mi from downtown Belfast)<br/><br/>Coastal Mountains Land Trust's first preserve in the town of Knox — a remarkable wetland at the headwaters of Marsh Stream, which flows from Frye Mountain to the lower Penobscot River. The trail follows a dry woods road, skirts a beaver-dammed pond, then climbs the steep eastern slope for wetland and Frye Mountain views (best fall or winter). Conserved 2021.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Park only in the designated lot, not along the driveway<br/>- 0.7 mi one-way, moderate, 260 ft gain<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
