  <Placemark>
    <name>Marshall Point Lighthouse Gardens Port Clyde ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Marshall Point Lighthouse Grounds<br/><br/>📍 Port Clyde, ME<br/><br/>Free, open sunrise to sunset year-round. Wheelchair- and stroller-friendly grounds framed by informal coastal plantings and wildflowers around the keeper's quarters. Genuinely uncrowded compared to Pemaquid or Portland Head lighthouses—the grounds have a natural garden feel with native coastal plants.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free admission and parking<br/>- Open sunrise to sunset year-round<br/>- Wheelchair and stroller accessible<br/>- Informal coastal plantings<br/>- Wildflower gardens<br/>- Uncrowded compared to famous Maine lighthouses<br/>- Good photo opportunity with lighthouse backdrop]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
