  <Placemark>
    <name>Marshall Point Lighthouse Port Clyde ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Marshall Point Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Port Clyde ME<br/><br/>The 1857 lighthouse at the tip of the St. George Peninsula, connected to the keeper's house by a distinctive white wooden walkway over the rocks. Featured in Forrest Gump as the endpoint of Forrest's cross-country run. The museum inside the keeper's house tells the story of the light's role in guiding boats through the Muscle Ridge Channel. Already in Port Clyde for the Monhegan Island ferry.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The lighthouse and grounds are free and always open.<br/>- The museum in the keeper's house (small donation) is worth 20 minutes.<br/>- Excellent photography at sunrise — the light faces east over the water.<br/>- Combine with the Monhegan ferry departure from Port Clyde, half a mile away.]]></description>
