  <Placemark>
    <name>McLellan-Poor Preserve Northport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[McLellan-Poor Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Route 1 at the Belfast/Northport town line (100 yds south), or via the Herrick Rd entrance off Perkins Rd<br/><br/>100 acres almost entirely forested in hemlock, mixed conifer, old-field pine, and red maple along the southern shore of Little River Lower Reservoir, crossed by many small streams and ravines. Land donated since 2007 by Hugh McLellan Russell, Elisabeth Wolfe, and Michael Cunning; original gift facilitated through Maine Coast Heritage Trust.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Two entrances: Route 1 (100 yds south of the Belfast/Northport line) and Herrick Rd (off Perkins Rd, near the Northport boundary)<br/>- Peggity's Path (1.4 mi round-trip) and the Reservoir Trail and Loop (0.9 mi) are both easy, dirt footpaths<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
