  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>McLoons Lobster Shack South Thomaston ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[McLoons Lobster Shack<br/><br/>📍 315 Island Rd, Spruce Head, South Thomaston, ME<br/><br/>A small, red-shingled lobster shack right on a working wharf on Spruce Head Island, a few miles south of Rockland — picnic tables sit close enough to watch lobster boats unloading their catch while you eat. Rated 4.7 on Tripadvisor (#1 of 5 restaurants in South Thomaston), 4.6 on Restaurant Guru across nearly 4,000 reviews, and 4.8 on Sirved — consistently among the most-praised lobster rolls in the Midcoast.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Lobster roll — generously filled, repeatedly called the best reviewers have ever had<br/>- Blueberry bread pudding — a genuine standout dessert, best served warmed<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Expect a line at peak lunch hours — it's a small operation and popular.<br/>- Lobster rolls run $15+; this isn't the cheapest option, but reviewers consistently say it's worth it.<br/>- The working-wharf setting is part of the appeal — arrive ready to watch the boats, not just eat.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.mcloonslobster.com/]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Restaurant</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>utensils</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>purple</value></Data>
    </ExtendedData>
    <Point>
      <coordinates>-69.1184019,43.9953979,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>McSeagull's Restaurant Boothbay Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[McSeagull's Restaurant<br/><br/>📍 14 Wharf St, Boothbay Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A pub-style harborfront institution built right over the water next to Boothbay Harbor's famous footbridge, with both indoor dining and a wraparound outdoor deck that's one of the best harbor-view seats in town. Ranked among the top 20 of 50+ Boothbay Harbor restaurants across hundreds of reviews, with a Tripadvisor Certificate of Excellence. The menu leans pub-casual — lobster dishes, fresh seafood, burgers, pizza, nachos — rather than fine dining, which is exactly the appeal after a day on the water.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Lobster roll — a generous portion of whole lobster meat, the dish most reviewers single out<br/>- Award-winning clam chowder — repeatedly called out as some of the best in New England; pair with the lobster bisque if you can't choose<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Busy in peak season — expect a wait at lunch and prime dinner hours; outdoor deck seating goes first.<br/>- Price range runs roughly $12–$40, wide enough to work for a casual lunch or a full seafood dinner.<br/>- Ask for a table on the deck side facing the footbridge — the view is the draw as much as the food.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-red</styleUrl>
