  <Placemark>
    <name>Meadow Brook Preserve Swanville ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Meadow Brook Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Oak Hill Rd, Swanville, ME (2.6 mi from downtown Belfast via High St/City Point Rd)<br/><br/>Central to a 2,408-acre undeveloped habitat block, with a 2.1 mi trail crossing from a new Oak Hill Rd lot to Swan Lake Ave through mature forest, wetland, riparian, and early-successional habitats, with unique views into the wetlands around Hurds Pond. Two rock-dam crossings over Meadow Brook require careful stone-stepping.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Roadside parking only on Swan Lake Ave — no formal lot there (park across from the Swanville transfer station)<br/>- Watch footing at the two rock-dam brook crossings mid-trail<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
