  <Placemark>
    <name>Mechanics Hall Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mechanics' Hall<br/><br/>📍 519 Congress Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>In 1815, the Maine Charitable Mechanic Association was formed to support Maine's creative community — blacksmiths, coopers, artists, innovators, and creators. Between 1857 and 1859, they built Mechanics' Hall at 519 Congress Street as a communal gathering space with a lending library at its center.<br/><br/>Today, Mechanics' Hall celebrates that rich history through literary arts programs, music, performance, and more while working to restore the landmark building as a vibrant cultural resource.<br/><br/>Inside you'll find:<br/>- A grand ballroom<br/>- A member-supported library<br/>- A historic classroom<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/519+Congress+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
