  <Placemark>
    <name>Megunticook Lake CMLT Preserves Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Megunticook Lake (CMLT Preserves)<br/><br/>📍 Bog Bridge Boat Launch, Washington St/Route 105, Camden, ME (coordinate approximate — no precise pin found for this launch, verify locally)<br/><br/>Coastal Mountains Land Trust holds four preserves on Megunticook Lake — Fernald's Neck (see the existing note), plus McPheters, Echo Island, and Richard's Wildlife (Pine and Little Pine Islands), all water-access only with no trails. Paddles range 0.75-3.5 mi one-way from either the Bog Bridge or Route 52 boat launches. Echo, Pine, and Little Pine Islands close seasonally for loon nesting, April 1-July 15.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Two public launches: Bog Bridge (Washington St/Rt 105) and Route 52 (Mountain St/Rt 52, just past Beaucaire Ave)<br/>- Islands closed to landing April 1-July 15 for loon nesting<br/>- Land's End, a Town of Camden property, has picnic-table launch sites along the shore too<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
