  <Placemark>
    <name>Mesier Park Wappingers Falls, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mesier Park<br/><br/>📍 2 Spring St, Wappingers Falls, NY 12590<br/><br/>A shaded village green on a hill above Wappinger Creek, centered on the Mesier Homestead — a wood-frame house built in two phases, starting around 1741-42 and expanded in the 1750s. Peter Mesier bought the property in 1777, and the family sold it to the village in 1891 for public use. The park is a contributing feature of the Wappingers Falls Historic District, listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1984.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The Homestead itself is run by the Wappingers Historical Society and opens for public tours one Sunday a month (typically 1, 2, and 3pm) — check their calendar before planning around it.<br/>- A quick, easy stop to pair with Fishkill Historic District or Van Wyck Homestead on the way through — all a short drive apart along Route 9.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.5968,-73.9148]]></description>
