  <Placemark>
    <name>Mill Brook Preserve Searsport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mill Brook Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Goodell St, Searsport, ME (walk 0.3 mi in from the municipal lot — no parking currently at the preserve itself)<br/><br/>A 44 ft hemlock-decked bridge spans Mill Brook in a steep, forested valley — walking distance from Searsport's schools, used as an outdoor-education 'Learning Landscape.' Great for fishing. Conserved 2021, thanks to Linda and Jim Babb.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- No parking at the preserve — park in the public lot on Goodell St and walk 0.3 mi (look for the grassy road entrance next to a red fire hydrant)<br/>- Trail currently dead-ends at 0.3 mi<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
