  <Placemark>
    <name>Mill Village Historic District Waterbury VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mill Village Historic District<br/><br/>📍 Stowe Street, Waterbury, VT<br/><br/>A compact 19th-century industrial village along Stowe Street, once powered by the waters of Graves (also called Thatcher's) Brook, where a cluster of mills and small industrial operations thrived well into the 20th century. Most of the surviving residential buildings date from 1860 to 1890. Now a quiet residential pocket of Waterbury. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1979.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A quiet residential walk, not a commercial attraction — appreciate it as a stroll through 19th-century mill-town architecture.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3431%2C%20-72.7478]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Historical</value></Data>
