      <coordinates>-72.7478,44.3431,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Millbrook Village NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Millbrook Village<br/><br/>📍 Franklin Ave, Millbrook, NY 12545<br/><br/>Flourished as a result of local businessmen such as George H. Brown, owner of the United States Condensing Co. (est. 1864), who brought in the Newburgh, Dutchess & Columbia RR in 1869. Tree-lined Franklin Ave. invites strollers to galleries, antique shops, bookstores, restaurants and attractions such as the Tribute Gardens, a gift of Mrs. Oakleigh Thorne dedicated to WWI and WWII veterans. The Thorne Building, now a branch of Dutchess Community College, was intended as a school and cultural center.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Park in lots or along streets and walk Franklin Ave.<br/>- Stop 5 of 17 on the Washington & Amenia Scenic Tour (Tour 4) — this is the tour's namesake village, the hub of local government, business and culture.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
