  <Placemark>
    <name>Minnewaska State Park Preserve New Paltz, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Minnewaska State Park Preserve<br/><br/>📍 New Paltz, NY<br/><br/>A spectacular 22,000-acre ridge-top park with crystal-clear sky lakes, miles of carriage roads through pine barrens, and the Sam's Point Ice Cave Trail.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Lake Minnewaska itself is swimmable — crystal clear ridge-top lake at 1,650 feet<br/>- Sam's Point Area (separate entrance) features unique ice caves and the best ridge views<br/>- September is excellent before peak foliage crowds arrive<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Minnewaska+State+Park+Preserve+New+Paltz,+NY]]></description>
