  <Placemark>
    <name>Mirror Lake Tuftonboro NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mirror Lake<br/><br/>📍 Mirror Lake village, Tuftonboro, NH<br/><br/>An unincorporated village on the shore of Mirror Lake in southern Tuftonboro, along NH Route 109 connecting Wolfeboro to Melvin Village and Moultonborough. Known for its summer camps and cabin colonies; the small Mirror Lake Community Church holds summer-only services in the village center. Union Wharf, just north on 19 Mile Bay, has a small summer store, boat gas, and a public beach.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A quiet lakeside pass-through on the drive between Wolfeboro and Moultonborough rather than a destination in itself.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.6241%2C%20-71.2637]]></description>
