  <Placemark>
    <name>Moffat House Berlin NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Moffett House Museum<br/><br/>📍 119 High St, Berlin, NH<br/><br/>The former home and medical office of Dr. and Mrs. Irving Moffett, now run by the Berlin and Coös County Historical Society (opened as a museum in 1997). The main floor displays sports memorabilia and photo albums; upstairs holds three rooms of genealogy records and local town histories; downstairs, Dr. Moffett's original office and exam rooms are preserved with period medical equipment. The collection also includes military uniforms spanning WWI through Desert Storm and Coös County's largest collection of souvenir china.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free admission; open Tuesday–Saturday, 12–4pm.<br/>- A good stop for anyone with North Country family genealogy to research.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.4739%2C%20-71.1798]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
