  <Placemark>
    <name>Mohonk Mountain House New Paltz, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mohonk Mountain House<br/><br/>📍 New Paltz, NY<br/><br/>A turreted seven-story resort stretching nearly an eighth of a mile along Lake Mohonk. The Sky Top tower, completed in 1923, offers views of six states on clear days. Distinct from (but adjacent to and historically connected with) the nonprofit Mohonk Preserve.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Located off Mountain Rest Road, linking High Falls to the north and New Paltz to the south<br/>- 35 miles of cross-country ski trails; 18,000 sq ft ice rink built in 2001<br/>- Carriage roads built at the turn of the century are wonderfully preserved for hiking and biking<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.7691%2C%20-74.1566]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-blue</styleUrl>
