  <Placemark>
    <name>Mohonk Preserve New Paltz, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mohonk Preserve<br/><br/>📍 New Paltz, NY<br/><br/>An 8,000-acre Shawangunk Ridge nature preserve with world-class rock climbing, miles of carriage roads, sky lakes, and some of the finest ridge hiking in the Northeast.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Day-use fee $15–20 for non-members; purchase online or at the trailhead<br/>- The Trapps carriage road is the best intro — flat, scenic, stunning cliffside views<br/>- September is prime climbing season — the Gunks attract serious climbers worldwide<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Mohonk+Preserve+New+Paltz,+NY]]></description>
