  <Placemark>
    <name>Moose Peak Lighthouse Mistake Island ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Moose Peak Lighthouse (Mistake Island)<br/><br/>📍 Mistake Island, ~5 miles southeast of Jonesport, ME<br/><br/>Built by Jeremy Berry and lit October 9, 1826, marking the entrance to Main Channel Way. First keeper Alexander Milliken, a War of 1812 privateer, served 23 years. In 1931 the station logged 1,562 fog hours — recognized as the foggiest spot in the country that year. Automated in 1972; sold into private hands in 2012 and again in 2019.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds open; landing on Nature Conservancy-controlled Mistake Island is allowed if visitors stay on the boardwalk to the lighthouse. Tower closed.<br/>- Reach via local boat operators out of Jonesport.]]></description>
