  <Placemark>
    <name>Moss Glen Falls Granville VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Moss Glen Falls (Granville)<br/><br/>📍 Route 100, Granville Gulf, Granville, VT<br/><br/>Formed where Deer Hollow Brook squeezes through a narrow bedrock notch and fans out into a remarkably symmetrical 68-foot veil — arguably the most photographed waterfall in Vermont, and easily one of the most accessible. Right along Route 100 within the Granville Gulf State Reservation; a large roadside parking area leads across a small bridge to a short (0.1-mile), easy walkway ending at a wooden viewing deck.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Not the same waterfall as "Moss Glen Falls" in Stowe, VT — this vault has a separate note for that one; don't confuse the two when planning.<br/>- Extremely popular — expect company, especially during foliage season.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0181%2C%20-72.8503]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
