  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Cabot Stark NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mount Cabot<br/><br/>📍 Pilot Range, near Stark, NH (Bunnell Notch / Kilkenny Ridge Trails)<br/><br/>The highest peak in the Pilot Range at 4,170 feet — the northernmost of New Hampshire's 48 four-thousand-footers, and one of the more remote ones on the list. Its summit ridge was too high and rugged to log, which made it a natural spot for a fire lookout: the Forest Service built a cabin and steel tower near the top in 1924, standing until the tower was removed in the 1960s. The summit clearing itself has only obstructed views today, but Bunnell Rock, passed along the way, gives a genuine vista south and east.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Main routes are the Bunnell Notch Trail and Kilkenny Ridge Trail — a serious, remote hike, not a casual outing.<br/>- Don't expect a summit view; the payoff is Bunnell Rock and the sense of remoteness, not a 360-degree panorama.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.5061%2C%20-71.4145]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
