  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Gulian Historic Site Beacon, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mount Gulian Historic Site<br/><br/>📍 145 Sterling St, Beacon, NY 12508<br/><br/>A reconstructed 18th-century Dutch-style manor overlooking the Hudson, built on the site of the original Verplanck family homestead. During the Revolutionary War it served as headquarters for Baron von Steuben, and it's traditionally regarded as the birthplace of the Society of the Cincinnati, founded there in 1783 by Continental Army officers.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Small, quiet site — pairs naturally with Dia:Beacon, about 10 minutes away, for a history-then-art half day.<br/>- Grounds include gardens and river views worth a slow walk beyond the house tour itself.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.4986,-73.9805]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
