  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Kancamagus NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mount Kancamagus<br/><br/>📍 White Mountain National Forest, near Kancamagus Pass<br/><br/>The peak that gives the Kancamagus Highway its name (itself named for a 17th-century sachem of the Pennacook confederacy), near the byway's high point at Kancamagus Pass.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- No maintained public trail to the summit — appreciate it as the highway's namesake landmark rather than a hiking objective.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0117%2C%20-71.4787]]></description>
