  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Lafayette Franconia Notch NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mount Lafayette<br/><br/>📍 Franconia Ridge, Franconia Notch State Park, NH<br/><br/>The 5,260-foot high point of the Franconia Range, and centerpiece of the Franconia Ridge Loop — widely considered one of the best (and most heavily hiked) trails in the White Mountains, with over a mile of exposed, above-treeline ridge walking connecting Lafayette, Mount Lincoln, and Little Haystack.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A serious full-day hike (~8-9 miles, ~3,900 ft gain) — start early to beat both crowds and afternoon weather, since the ridge is fully exposed.<br/>- Trailhead parking at Lafayette Place fills fast on nice days; arrive very early or expect to wait.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.1607%2C%20-71.6444]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
