  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Osceola Waterville Valley NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mount Osceola<br/><br/>📍 Tripoli Road, Waterville Valley, NH<br/><br/>A heavily used, moderate 5.9-mile out-and-back with a steady 2,050-foot climb over 3.2 miles from the Tripoli Road trailhead — rocky and rough at the start, then short, steeper switchbacks near the top. The 4,340-foot summit is the site of an old fire tower; the ambitious can continue along the ridge to East Osceola (4,156 ft).<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Tripoli Road is unpaved and typically closed November through late May (snow) — check before driving up.<br/>- Day-use parking fee ($5/vehicle) at the trailhead.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0014%2C%20-71.5359]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
