      <coordinates>-71.5359,44.0014,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Percival Preserve Northport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mount Percival Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Upper Bluff Rd, Northport, ME (entrance across from the mailbox marked 220 Upper Bluff Rd)<br/><br/>A gradual climb to a 410 ft summit with the foundation of an early-1900s rusticator's tower and cistern — expansive Penobscot Bay/Camden Hills views existed then, though the grown-in forest mostly blocks them now. Donated by the Hildreth family, transferred from Maine Coast Heritage Trust in 2003.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Roadside parking only — no dedicated lot<br/>- Short trail (0.3 mi one-way) but real history at the summit ruins<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
