    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Tuck Preserve Stockton Springs ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mount Tuck Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Meadow Rd, Stockton Springs, ME (4.1 mi north on Route 1, then 0.6 mi on Meadow Rd — do not block the road, it's actively used by abutting landowners)<br/><br/>A long, rewarding ramble through mixed-age forest — 0.7 mi across abutting property on a dirt road/meadow, then a moderate 0.8 mi climb to the forested summit of Mount Tuck, plus a 0.3 mi extension to a scenic overlook on the east side with views toward the Penobscot Narrows Bridge. Conserved through five property purchases, 2019-2022.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- 1.7 mi one-way total, moderate, 425 ft gain<br/>- Park on the side of Meadow Rd or in the dirt pull-off by the kiosk — don't block the road<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
