      <coordinates>-68.82202,44.5487,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Washington Bretton Woods NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mount Washington<br/><br/>📍 Presidential Range, NH<br/><br/>The highest peak in the Northeastern United States at 6,288 feet, and home to some of the world's most extreme recorded weather — including a 231 mph wind gust in 1934, a world record that stood for decades. Summit access is via the Cog Railway (from Bretton Woods), the Mount Washington Auto Road (from Pinkham Notch), or on foot via several demanding trails.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Weather can turn dangerous fast even in summer — check the Mount Washington Observatory forecast before any hike, and dress for winter conditions regardless of the valley temperature.<br/>- The Cog Railway and Auto Road are the practical options if you don't want to hike; both need advance booking in peak season.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.2705%2C%20-71.3033]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Attraction</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>mountain</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>green</value></Data>
    </ExtendedData>
    <Point>
      <coordinates>-71.3033,44.2705,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Washington Cog Railway Bretton Woods NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Mount Washington Cog Railway<br/><br/>📍 Marshfield Base Station, Bretton Woods, NH<br/><br/>The world's first mountain-climbing (rack-and-pinion) railway, operating since 1869 — engineer Sylvester Marsh's invention. A 3-hour round trip climbs almost 3,600 feet along a western spur of the mountain to the 6,288-foot summit, the highest point in the Northeast. Wood-fired through 1910, then coal, then the first biodiesel locomotive was introduced in 2008; some trips still run vintage steam.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Base station is 6 miles off Route 302, near Bretton Woods Ski Resort and the Omni Mount Washington Hotel — book ahead, trips sell out in peak season.<br/>- Weather at the summit can be dramatically colder and windier than the base — bring layers regardless of season.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.2734%2C%20-71.4472]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
