  <Placemark>
    <name>Murray Preserve Lincolnville ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Murray Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Howe Point Rd, Lincolnville, ME (off Route 1, 1.1 mi north of Lincolnville Beach)<br/><br/>A 7-acre former hay/blueberry field, mowed annually for habitat and a scenic view from Route 1 to Penobscot Bay. Accessed by walking south along the state-owned cobble beach at Ducktrap Harbor — no trail, beach access only. Donated 2007 by the Murray family.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Beach access only — park at the small lot at the end of Howe Point Rd and walk south along the shore<br/>- Metal Preserve medallions mark the boundary, visible from the beach<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
