  <Placemark>
    <name>Narraguagus Lighthouse Milbridge ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Narraguagus (Pond Island) Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Pond Island, near Milbridge, ME (Narraguagus Bay)<br/><br/>Congress funded this lighthouse in 1851 to guide vessels into Narraguagus Bay near the shipbuilding town of Milbridge; construction finished in April 1853. Keeper Charles E. Tracy rescued four Canadian sailors from the wrecked schooner Valdare in 1929. A lighted bell buoy replaced the light when it was decommissioned in 1933.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned by the Dameron family; grounds, dwelling, and tower closed.<br/>- Best viewed by boat or plane through Robertson Sea Tours or Bar Harbor Whale Watch.]]></description>
