  <Placemark>
    <name>Nash Island Lighthouse South Addison ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Nash Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Big Nash Island, ~3.75 miles northeast of South Addison, ME<br/><br/>Marking the entrances to Pleasant Bay and Moosabec Reach, the original 1838 rubblestone tower was rebuilt in brick in 1873. Keeper John Purington raised nine children here from 1916–1935, including daughter Jenny, who captained her own lobster boat for over 70 years and kept the island's sheep-grazing tradition alive until 2004. Automated in 1947, discontinued in 1982.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Owned by Friends of Nash Island Light; part of Petit Manan National Wildlife Refuge, closed April–August for seabird nesting — covers the whole trip window.<br/>- Best accessed by boat via Robertson Sea Tours or Bar Harbor Whale Watch.]]></description>
