  <Placemark>
    <name>Newman Preserve Northport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Newman Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Beech Hill Rd, Northport, ME (3.8 mi from Route 1)<br/><br/>A downhill trail through four distinct forest types, ending at a picnic spot on Pitcher Pond — the only shorefront access to the Breslin-Richenaker Tract. Donated 1999 by the Newman family, with a 2015 addition from the Breslin estate providing the pond-access trail section.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- 1.1 mi, moderate, 280 ft elevation loss on the way in (so a climb back out)<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
