  <Placemark>
    <name>Nine Partners School &amp; Meeting House Millbrook NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Nine Partners School & Meeting House<br/><br/>📍 Church St, Millbrook, NY (National Register)<br/><br/>Established 1780 (cemetery along Church St.), was the site of the Orthodox and Hicksite Quaker "Separation" (1828). This area, called Mechanic, was settled ca. 1750 by Quakers who organized the Meeting. East of the Meeting House was Nine Partners School, the first Quaker co-ed boarding school in America, est. 1796, an ancestor of Oakwood School in Poughkeepsie. The Millbrook Golf and Tennis Club (private) is the site of Willets Academy, where distinguished Quaker educators Jacob and Deborah Willets taught.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Marked with a National Register historical marker.<br/>- Stop 14 of 17 on the Washington & Amenia Scenic Tour (Tour 4).<br/>- No single street address — coordinates left blank.]]></description>
