  <Placemark>
    <name>North Moat Mountain North Conway NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[North Moat Mountain<br/><br/>📍 Diana's Baths trailhead, West Side Road, North Conway, NH<br/><br/>A demanding hike (8.3 miles, ~2,600 ft gain) to a bare, rocky 3,196-foot summit with 360-degree views and — come July — wild blueberry bushes covering the ledges. The trail passes Diana's Baths, a popular swimming spot with cascades on Lucy Brook, right near the trailhead.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A full 5-8 hour day for the full loop — start early.<br/>- Diana's Baths itself (a short walk from the parking area) is worth visiting even if not doing the full mountain.<br/>- $3/day parking fee at the trailhead.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0431%2C%20-71.2153]]></description>
