  <Placemark>
    <name>Ocean Path Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Ocean Path<br/><br/>📍 Between Sand Beach and Otter Point, Acadia National Park ME<br/><br/>A relatively flat, mostly gravel/concrete coastal walk following the eastern shoreline of Mount Desert Island — the classic Acadia landmarks (Sand Beach, Thunder Hole, Monument Cove, Otter Cliff) all sit directly along it, making it one of the most efficient ways to see the park's signature coastline in a single walk.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- One-way distance is 2.2 mi (4.4 mi round trip) — Sand Beach and the Otter Point/Otter Cliff parking areas are both trailheads, so a one-way walk with a car shuttle or the Island Explorer shuttle is an option<br/>- Two short staircases climb around a rocky section about 1.4 miles in<br/>- Extremely popular — go early morning for fewer crowds, especially near Thunder Hole]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
