  <Placemark>
    <name>Oceanarium and Education Center Trenton ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Oceanarium and Education Center<br/><br/>📍 Thomas Bay, Trenton, ME (just before the MDI bridge)<br/><br/>A hands-on marine education center on Thomas Bay, with touch tanks, a lobster hatchery display explaining Maine's lobster fishery, and a salt marsh boardwalk walk — geared toward kids and a good stop right before or after crossing onto Mount Desert Island.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Reviews are mixed — a modest, low-key attraction rather than a major draw; good for young kids specifically, less so for others.<br/>- Convenient timing: right on Route 3 at the gateway to MDI, easy to fit in without a detour.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.4201%2C%20-68.3498]]></description>
