  <Placemark>
    <name>Old Orchard Beach ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Old Orchard Beach<br/><br/>📍 Old Orchard Beach, ME<br/><br/>Part Coney Island, part classic New England — a 7-mile sand beach with a boardwalk, an active pier lined with arcades and rides, and a carnival-set-up feel that's leaned into for decades. Fodor's Travel named it one of the 10 best boardwalks in America; Reader's Digest ranked it a top-5 beach boardwalk nationally in 2021.<br/><br/>Why go: Classic boardwalk/pier/arcade energy — nationally ranked as one of the best beach boardwalks in the country, visually distinctive for photos.<br/><br/>Who it's for: Families with kids, anyone wanting a nostalgic carnival-beach-town day; less appealing if you want quiet/upscale.<br/><br/>Likes: The pier itself, Pier Fries (since 1932), the lively/fun atmosphere.<br/><br/>Dislikes: Loud, crowded, touristy — mixed reviews mostly come down to expectations (it's not a peaceful beach day).<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Pier Fries (since 1932) and Bill's Pizza (since 1949) are the boardwalk food landmarks — both worth the wait<br/>- Expect real crowds on summer weekends; visit on a weekday or in shoulder season (late spring/early fall) for a calmer experience<br/>- About 20-25 min south of downtown Portland — an easy half-day add-on<br/>- Visually distinctive for photos even if the specific rides/pier don't mean much locally — the boardwalk-and-carnival look reads well to an outside audience<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Old+Orchard+Beach+Pier/@43.515463,-70.373156,15z]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
