  <Placemark>
    <name>Old Rhinebeck Aerodrome NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Old Rhinebeck Aerodrome<br/><br/>📍 9 Norton Rd, Red Hook, NY 12571<br/><br/>This site is home to World War I and pioneer Lindbergh-era aircraft (1900-1937). Displays, air shows and barnstorming rides in an open cockpit biplane.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Stop 29 of 33 on the Rhinebeck, Red Hook & Milan Scenic Tour (Tour 1).<br/>- Rating is TripAdvisor's figure (279 reviews) — ranked #1 in its category in Red Hook; technically under the 4.7 threshold but marked purple as a genuinely unique living-history attraction (actual flying WWI/vintage aircraft, not just static displays).]]></description>
