  <Placemark>
    <name>Omni Mount Washington Resort Bretton Woods NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Omni Mount Washington Resort<br/><br/>📍 Bretton Woods NH<br/><br/>A Spanish Renaissance palace of white stucco and red-tile roofing set against the Presidential Range, built in 1902 for 2,000 workers over 22 months. In July 1944, 730 delegates from 44 Allied nations gathered here to establish the Bretton Woods monetary system — pegging global currencies to gold and creating the IMF and World Bank. The veranda faces Mount Washington directly. Worth a meal, a drink, or simply a walk through the grand public rooms.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Non-guests can visit the public areas, veranda, and grounds freely.<br/>- The dining room and Cave bar are open to the public — reservations recommended for dinner.<br/>- The Presidential Range view from the veranda is one of the great hotel views in America.<br/>- The Bretton Woods ski area and Mount Washington Cog Railway are both on the property.]]></description>
