  <Placemark>
    <name>Opus 40 Saugerties, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Opus 40<br/><br/>📍 Saugerties, NY<br/><br/>A monumental 6-acre bluestone sculpture environment hand-built by artist Harvey Fite over 37 years — one of the most extraordinary outdoor artworks in the United States.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open seasonally May–October; check opus40. for exact dates<br/>- Allow 90 minutes minimum to fully explore the structure<br/>- The on-site museum tells the remarkable story of Fite's 37-year solo construction<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Opus+40+Saugerties,+NY]]></description>
