  <Placemark>
    <name>Orford Street Historic District Orford NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Orford Street Historic District<br/><br/>📍 Route 10 (Orford Street), Orford, NH<br/><br/>A half-mile Federal-period streetscape along Route 10, 38 buildings deep, described since the 18th century as "the most charming country village." Its centerpiece is the Ridge — seven fine houses built between 1773 and 1839 by Orford's professional and business class, showing the influence of Boston architect Asher Benjamin (associate of Charles Bulfinch), who likely designed the John B. Wheeler house, southernmost in the row. The first Ridge house was built for Orford's first minister, later becoming home to Samuel Morey — an inventor with over 20 patents, including an early paddlewheel steamboat and one of the first internal combustion engines. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1977.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A tree-lined common and promenade make this an easy, scenic walk — no ticketed attraction, just a drive or stroll down Route 10.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.9053%2C%20-72.1373]]></description>
