  <Placemark>
    <name>Owl &amp; Turtle Bookshop Cafe Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Owl & Turtle Bookshop Cafe<br/><br/>📍 33 Bay View St, Camden, ME<br/><br/>A Camden institution since 1970 — an independent, carefully-curated bookstore that added a full café under new ownership, pouring hand-brewed coffee, espresso, and chai alongside locally-baked pastries. It's also the retail home of Coffee On The Porch, a Camden-based micro-roaster that doesn't have its own walk-in shop — this is where to actually taste their beans in person. Rated 4.7 on Restaurant Guru (424 reviews), 4.8 by the local Chamber of Commerce (177 reviews), and 4.6 on Tripadvisor (#12 of 40 Camden restaurants) — consistent across all three.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Hand-poured coffee or espresso, specifically featuring Coffee On The Porch's Camden-roasted beans<br/>- Biscotti or muffins — repeatedly praised alongside the coffee<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Worth stopping in even just to browse — it's a real, carefully-curated bookstore, not a coffee shop with books as decor.<br/>- A good rainy-day or slow-morning pick, right in the middle of downtown.<br/>- Friendly, unhurried service per reviews — not a grab-and-go spot.]]></description>
