  <Placemark>
    <name>Page Pond and Forest Trailhead Meredith NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Page Pond and Forest Trailhead<br/><br/>📍 Quarry Road, Meredith, NH (main trailhead)<br/><br/>A community-conserved forest with a network of hiking trails around Page Pond, managed with support from the Meredith Conservation Commission. The main trailhead is via Quarry Road (2 miles north of Meredith on Route 25, then 0.4 miles on Quarry Road) with a large unpaved lot and a $3 parking fee; a second trailhead is on Barnard Ridge Road, and informal access exists from Blueberry Hill Road.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Bring cash for the Quarry Road lot's parking fee.<br/>- Good option for a shorter, low-key hike compared to the region's bigger peaks (Red Hill, Mount Major).<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.6761%2C%20-71.4699]]></description>
