  <Placemark>
    <name>Panacea Wiscasset ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Panacea<br/><br/>📍 100 Main St, Wiscasset, ME<br/><br/>Opened February 2025 in the former Yonder sandwich shop space, directly across from Red's Eats — an ocean-inspired chowder house and soupery from Chauncey Erskine, formerly of Maine Booch in Damariscotta. Built around community as much as comfort food: nautical charts, sea captain figurines, and regular game nights fill out the room. Rated 5.0 on Tripadvisor from early reviews.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Maine clam chowder — reviewers call it the best they've had anywhere in the state<br/>- Knotty Buoy grilled cheese — cheddar, green apple, seaweed, and maple-miso spread<br/>- Lobster grilled cheese<br/>- Vegan chowder option, if that matters for your group<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Small, casual spot — good for a quick, satisfying lunch rather than a sit-down dinner.<br/>- Right across the street from Red's Eats, so easy to pair with (or use as the less-crowded alternative to) Wiscasset's famous lobster roll line.<br/>- Portions are described as reasonable and reasonably priced — not a splurge stop.<br/><br/>More info: https://panaceamaine.com/]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
