  <Placemark>
    <name>Paolo's Brunswick ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Paolo's<br/><br/>📍 Fort Andross Mill building, Brunswick, ME (exact suite unconfirmed — large multi-tenant complex, double-check when booking)<br/><br/>Opened summer 2026 by Jeremy and Marina Kratzer (who also run Dutchman's wood-fired bagels, co-located at the same site), named for Jeremy's late grandfather Paul Macher. Brings true New Jersey-style Italian-American cooking — not the more common New England Italian — with a wood-fired oven doing double duty on pizza and mains.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Neapolitan-style 12" pizzas — margherita, carbonara, and a thin Roman-style Jersey clam pizza<br/>- House-made pasta — bucatini featured<br/>- Chicken Parmesan — vodka sauce or house marinara<br/>- Dry-aged bone-in NY strip steak<br/>- Charred broccolini with whipped ricotta; tiramisu, lemon pie, chocolate mousse, affogato martini<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Very new and currently open Thursday-Sunday only, 5-9pm dinner, drinks/snacks from 4pm<br/>- No online reservation platform found — call ahead given limited days and newness<br/>- Confirm the exact suite within the Fort Andross complex before going<br/><br/>More info: https://paolos.me/]]></description>
