  <Placemark>
    <name>Parking - Round Pond Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-07T12:15:00<br/><br/>Parking — Round Pond Harbor<br/><br/>📍 Near the town landing, Round Pond, ME<br/><br/>Round Pond has no large formal lot — it's a small working harbor village, and street parking along the harbor near the lobster docks and general store is the norm. Everything (Round Pond Lobster Co-op, Muscongus Bay Lobster, King Ro Market, Granite Hall Store, Round Pond Coffee, The Anchor Restaurant) is within a couple minutes' walk from here.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Rarely a real problem — Round Pond stays quiet even in peak season compared to Pemaquid Point or Boothbay Harbor.<br/>- Don't block driveways or the working lobster co-op's loading areas.]]></description>
