  <Placemark>
    <name>Paugus Bay Laconia NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Paugus Bay<br/><br/>📍 Laconia / Gilford, NH<br/><br/>A southern arm of Lake Winnipesaukee, separated from the main lake by the narrow channel at Weirs Beach. Ringed by marinas, lakefront restaurants, and camps, it's one of the busiest stretches of water in the Lakes Region during summer.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Weirs Beach, right where Paugus Bay meets the main lake, is the region's classic boardwalk-and-arcade summer scene.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.5761%2C%20-71.4592]]></description>
