  <Placemark>
    <name>Peach's Restaurant Conway NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Overview<br/>Type: Breakfast and brunch restaurant<br/><br/>Best known for: Lobster Benedict, Coconut French Toast<br/><br/>Location context: North Conway<br/><br/>Price level: $10–20 per person<br/><br/>Visit timing: Busy during brunch hours<br/><br/>Typical Customers<br/>Demographics: Locals and tourists<br/><br/>Group types: Couples, families, friends<br/><br/>Common occasions: Brunch, casual breakfast<br/><br/>Vibe & Setting<br/>Atmosphere: Casual, friendly<br/><br/>Noise level: Moderate<br/><br/>Decor & setting: Indoor seating, cozy atmosphere<br/><br/>Service style: Attentive and fast<br/><br/>Recommended Dishes<br/>Overall dish consensus: Reviewers frequently mention the Lobster Benedict and Coconut French Toast as must-try dishes for their delicious flavors and unique offerings.<br/><br/>How “top dishes” are determined: Top dishes are selected based on their frequency in reviews, mentions in photos, and overall praise from diners on the Google Maps page.<br/><br/>Top dishes to order<br/>| Rank | Dish                 | Why it stands out              | How often it’s mentioned        | Ideal for                 |<br/>|------|----------------------|-------------------------------|--------------------------------|--------------------------|<br/>| 1    | Lobster Benedict      | Rich flavors and generous portions. | Often mentioned as a favorite  | Hearty main              |<br/>| 2    | Coconut French Toast  | Sweet and comforting; a crowd-pleaser. | Appears in numerous reviews    | Lighter option           |<br/>| 3    | Irish Benedict        | Tasty and filling; unique twist on traditional eggs Benedict. | Repeatedly called out for quality | Sharing at the table     |<br/><br/>Good alternates / backup choices<br/>- Smoked salmon Benedict: Noted for good flavor and portion size.<br/>- Breakfast burrito: Described as okay, more like a wrap rather than a burrito.<br/>- Pancakes: Generally praised for being yummy.<br/><br/>Highlights (non‑dish positives from reviews)<br/>Service: Attentive and quick, enhancing the dining experience.<br/><br/>Atmosphere: Cozy and welcoming, making it a great spot for breakfast gatherings.<br/><br/>Common Issues (from reviews)<br/>Menu variety: Some found the options unique but limited for specific preferences.<br/><br/>Response time: A few guests experienced longer waits during peak hours.<br/><br/>Practical Notes<br/>Reservation / wait: Walk-in friendly; no reservations needed mentioned.<br/><br/>Accessibility: Not mentioned<br/><br/>Parking / transit: Not mentioned<br/><br/>Best use case: Best for casual brunch with family or friends.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Peach's+Restaurant/@44.04981,-71.1295725,2018m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m6!3m5!1s0x4cb3a1008d62615b:0xfd2c9c5c96359b70!8m2!3d44.0485698!4d-71.124915!16s%2Fg%2F1td09k21?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMy4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
