  <Placemark>
    <name>Peaks Island Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Peaks Island<br/><br/>📍 Portland ME<br/><br/>A 20-minute Casco Bay Lines ferry ride from the Old Port delivers you to a car-free island with 3 miles of flat road looping past rocky beaches, WWII-era artillery batteries, and Portland skyline views. Bike rentals are at the ferry dock. The 5th Maine Regiment Museum and the Umbrella Cover Museum (the world's only) are unexpected delights.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Take any Casco Bay Lines ferry from the Old Port terminal — ferries run frequently in summer.<br/>- Rent bikes at Brad's Bike Shop, right at the dock.<br/>- The back shore loop past Brackett Avenue offers the best cliff and ocean views.<br/>- The island has no cars — this is a genuine escape even from a busy Portland day.]]></description>
