  <Placemark>
    <name>Pemaquid Beach Park Bristol ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-07T09:15:00<br/><br/>Pemaquid Beach Park<br/><br/>📍 New Harbor, Bristol, ME<br/><br/>A genuinely rare find on the Maine coast — a soft, white-sand crescent beach with gentle surf, run by the Bristol Parks and Recreation Department. Amenities include restrooms/changing rooms, outdoor showers, picnic tables, an ADA boardwalk to the sand, beach-gear rentals (chairs, boogie boards, umbrellas), and a seasonal restaurant on site (Mimi's on the Beach).<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Rating in question: no hard numeric figure independently confirmed — but every review surfaced was strongly positive ("rare white sand beach," "gem of a beach"), ranked #2 of 7 things to do in Bristol on Tripadvisor.<br/>- Parking fills up on warm summer days — arrive early.<br/>- Combine with Pemaquid Point Lighthouse and Colonial Pemaquid, both a short drive away.]]></description>
