  <Placemark>
    <name>Pemaquid Pond Preserve Bremen ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Pemaquid Pond Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Turner Road, ~0.6 mi past the Pemaquid/McCurdy Pond causeway, Bremen, ME<br/><br/>196-acre preserve leading to Pemaquid Pond's shore, with flat rocks for picnicking; a native vegetation buffer protects the pond's water quality. A new orange loop trail was added in 2025. ~0.7-1.5 mi out and back, 75 ft gain.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Flat rocks at the shore are good for a picnic stop<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/pemaquid-pond-preserve/]]></description>
