  <Placemark>
    <name>Penny Lake Boothbay ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Penny Lake<br/><br/>📍 Off Route 27/96, Boothbay Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A 29-acre Boothbay Region Land Trust preserve (plus a 25-acre easement) that's unusually close to downtown — just off the Route 27/96 junction, right by the Chamber of Commerce and Flagship Inn. The main loop is an easy 0.5 miles between the trailhead kiosk and a wooden bridge with bench seating, passing through an apple orchard and woodland around a freshwater wetland. Watch for migratory and nesting birds, turtles, beaver, deer, and occasionally moose.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Parking: from the Route 27/96 traffic light, go north 0.1 mile, turn left between the Chamber of Commerce and the Flagship Inn, and continue past the Carousel Music Theater to the BRLT lot.<br/>- Genuinely convenient for a short walk without driving out of town — closer to the harbor than any other BRLT preserve.<br/>- Popular with locals for running, dog-walking, and general exercise, not just sightseeing — expect some foot traffic even though it's not a tourist spot.<br/>- All trails are easy, flat walking — a good option if you want nature without committing to a real hike.]]></description>
