  <Placemark>
    <name>Penobscot Shore Preserve Prospect ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Penobscot Shore Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Bowden Point Rd, Prospect, ME (off Route 174, before the Penobscot Narrows Bridge)<br/><br/>1,800 ft of forested Penobscot River shoreline — the Land Trust's first preserve in Prospect. Old foundations line the shore, with views across the river to the former Bucksport mill site. Transferred from Great Pond Mountain Conservation Trust in 2017, originally donated by Elizabeth Wemett in honor of Mary Lord.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- 1.0 mi round-trip, moderate, 250 ft gain<br/>- Park along the road — no formal lot<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
