  <Placemark>
    <name>Perkins Island Lighthouse Bath ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Perkins Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Perkins Island, Kennebec River, ~2.5 miles north of Popham Beach, ME<br/><br/>Built in 1897–98 following the Lighthouse Board's 1892 recommendation to improve navigation on the busy Kennebec River — a wooden octagonal tower upgraded to a fifth-order Fresnel lens in 1902. Keeper Jacob W. Haley served nearly 30 years and took part in multiple rescues, as did successor Eugene W. Osgood. Automated in 1959.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds open, dwelling and tower closed.<br/>- Best seen by boat via Maine Maritime Museum cruises (Bath) or Cap'n Fish's (Boothbay Harbor); limited land view from Parker Neck Road.]]></description>
