  <Placemark>
    <name>Peter Trout's Tavern and Inn Southwest Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Peter Trouts is a laid-back tavern known for its seafood offerings, including fish sandwiches and Nashville hot chicken sandwiches. It attracts a diverse crowd, likely consisting of families and groups looking for casual dining experiences. The ambiance is casual and lively, with a focus on good food, drinks, and music. Customers consistently praise the large portion sizes, tasty cheese topping on the buttered toasted bread, and the overall vibe and cleanliness of the establishment. However, some reviewers noted that the music selection might not appeal to everyone, and there were instances of emptiness during off-peak hours.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Peter+Trout's+Tavern+and+Inn/@44.2786623,-68.3368706,3098m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m6!3m5!1s0x4caebdb888f99ed1:0xbe5d378879f3b949!8m2!3d44.2688916!4d-68.3113483!16s%2Fg%2F11fm4w7xw2?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
