  <Placemark>
    <name>Peters Kill At Minnewaska State Park Gardiner NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Peter's Kill At Minnewaska State Park<br/><br/>📍 Minnewaska State Park Preserve, off Route 44/55, Gardiner, NY<br/><br/>A distinct section of the 23,000-acre Minnewaska State Park Preserve, entered separately off Route 44/55 with its own 120-space parking lot. It's the only area of the park where technical rock climbing and bouldering are permitted (April–December, weather permitting, with a daily climbing permit and acknowledgement-of-risk form). Mixed hardwood forest, pitch pine barrens, wetlands, and the Peter's Kill stream and waterfalls surround the High Peter's Kill escarpment.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Buy the daily climbing permit at the entrance if planning to climb; hiking and picnicking don't require one.<br/>- Picnic tables are a short walk from the parking lot, first-come first-served — no grilling permitted.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.7387%2C%20-74.2183]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
