  <Placemark>
    <name>Petey's Summertime Seafood Rye NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Petey's Summertime Seafood<br/><br/>📍 1323 Ocean Blvd, Rye, NH<br/><br/>A beachfront seafood restaurant right on Route 1A in Rye, on New Hampshire's short stretch of coastline between Massachusetts and Maine. Sells lobster, lobster rolls, fried clams, steamer clams, and the full range of New England seafood standards, with a real bar attached. Repeatedly recognized in state and local magazines. Rated 4.5 on Google across over 3,000 ratings (Restaurant Guru runs higher at 4.8, Tripadvisor lower at 4.2 — Google is the figure used here as the more broadly representative source).<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Fried oysters<br/>- Steamed lobster<br/>- Steamed mussels<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Right on the coastal drive between Massachusetts and Maine — a natural stop on the Boston–Portland leg of the trip.<br/>- Full bar and sit-down service, more of a restaurant than a pure walk-up shack.<br/>- Fast service even when busy, per reviews — a reliable choice rather than a gamble.<br/><br/>More info: https://peteys.com/]]></description>
