  <Placemark>
    <name>Petit Manan Lighthouse Milbridge ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Petit Manan Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Petit Manan Island, ~2.5 miles southeast of Petit Manan Point, near Milbridge, ME<br/><br/>The original 1817 rubblestone tower deteriorated badly and was replaced in 1855 by a 119-foot granite tower with a second-order Fresnel lens from Paris — one of Maine's tallest lighthouses, built to warn ships off dangerous offshore ledges in one of the nation's foggiest locations. Automated in 1972.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Island closed April 1–August 31 for seabird nesting — covers the trip window; boat tours still offer water views.<br/>- Owned by U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service (Maine Coastal Islands National Wildlife Refuge). Original Fresnel lens on display at the Maine Lighthouse Museum in Rockland.]]></description>
