  <Placemark>
    <name>Piper Stream Preserve Northport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Piper Stream Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Prescott Hill Rd, Northport, ME (off Route 52, 3.8 mi from Belfast)<br/><br/>A small, quiet preserve with mixed forest and a charming stream and wetlands. Piper Stream feeds the Little River and is an important wildlife corridor to the large Herricks Bog in central Northport. Donated 2021 by Susan Conard and David Randall.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Easy, nearly flat 0.3 mi one-way — a genuine quick stop<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
