  <Placemark>
    <name>Pisgah State Park Chesterfield NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Pisgah State Park<br/><br/>📍 Winchester / Chesterfield / Hinsdale, NH<br/><br/>New Hampshire's largest state park at 13,300 acres — 8,320 in Winchester, 4,660 in the north in Chesterfield, and 690 in the west in Hinsdale. Encompasses a complete watershed north of the Ashuelot River, seven ponds, four highland ridges, extensive wetlands, and a rare 20-acre parcel of old-growth forest. Nearly 62 miles of multi-use trail support hiking, fishing, and horseback riding.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Undeveloped and lightly visited compared to NH's more famous parks — good for solitude, but come prepared (limited facilities).<br/>- Main access points are off Old Chesterfield Road in Winchester and Route 63 in Chesterfield.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=42.8600%2C%20-72.4200]]></description>
