  <Placemark>
    <name>Plummer Point Preserve South Bristol ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Plummer Point Preserve<br/><br/>📍 1695 State Route 129, South Bristol, ME<br/><br/>85-acre coastal spruce forest preserve (71 ac 1991 + 14 ac 2022) with views of the Damariscotta River and Seal Cove, a disused rock quarry, and seals often visible on ledges at low tide. ~1.9-2.0 mi trail network.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Low tide is the time to look for seals on the ledges<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/plummer-point-preserve/]]></description>
