  <Placemark>
    <name>Polly's Pancake Parlor Sugar Hill NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Polly's Pancake Parlor<br/><br/>📍 Sugar Hill NH<br/><br/>A 90-year-old hilltop farm institution in Sugar Hill, serving buckwheat, cornmeal, oat, and whole wheat pancakes with homemade syrups — maple, blueberry, and pure — alongside homemade granola, country ham, and eggs from the farm's own hens. The dining room faces south across a meadow to the Franconia Range. One of the most beloved breakfast destinations in New England.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Buckwheat pancakes with pure maple syrup<br/>- Country ham and eggs<br/>- Homemade granola<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open May through October; breakfast and lunch only — arrives by 9am to avoid the wait.<br/>- The view from the dining room alone is worth the detour up Sugar Hill.<br/>- No reservations; expect a short wait on summer weekends.<br/>- Combine with the Sugar Hill Scenic Vista overlook, 1 mile up the road.]]></description>
