  <Placemark>
    <name>Pomelia Brunswick ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Pomelia<br/><br/>📍 16 Station Ave, Brunswick, ME (Brunswick Station complex)<br/><br/>From chef-owner Tony Bickford (previously of Wiscasset's Little Village Bistro) — genuinely distinctive modern Sicilian cooking, not standard red-sauce Italian, with roughly 70% of the menu meatless. Praised by the Portland Press Herald for making the most of Sicilian classics.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Arancini — saffron risotto balls, crunchy exterior, creamy interior<br/>- Marsala porcini pasta with pistachio<br/>- Panellichi — chickpea fritters on brioche slider buns<br/>- La Brontese focaccia pizza — pistachio, caciocavallo<br/>- Ragu di salsiccia — orecchiette, house-made sausage<br/>- Cannoli for dessert<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Reservations via OpenTable or (207) 203-6593; groups of 6+ call or email mangia@pomelia.<br/>- Open Tue-Sat 11am-2pm and 4-8:30/9pm (closed Sun; hours vary slightly by source, confirm before going)<br/>- Good pre-show option for Maine State Music Theatre<br/>- Full bar/wine, gluten-free and vegan-friendly<br/><br/>More info: https://pomelia.restaurant/]]></description>
