  <Placemark>
    <name>Pond Island Lighthouse Popham Beach ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Pond Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Pond Island, Kennebec River entrance, near Popham Beach, ME<br/><br/>Congress appropriated funds in 1821 to mark the Kennebec River's mouth. The original conical stone tower deteriorated and was replaced in 1855 by the current twenty-foot brick tower with a fifth-order Fresnel lens. The automated station's island now supports a successfully restored tern colony, ongoing since 1996.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Managed by U.S. Fish & Wildlife Service; grounds open September–March only, tower always closed.<br/>- Reasonable views from Popham Beach State Park; boat cruises via Maine Maritime Museum (Bath) or Cap'n Fish's (Boothbay Harbor).]]></description>
