    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Popham Beach State Park Phippsburg ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Popham Beach State Park<br/><br/>📍 10 Perkins Farm Ln, Phippsburg, ME<br/><br/>Consistently ranked one of the best beaches in Maine and New England — wide, clean sand, relatively uncrowded compared to southern Maine beaches, with views of offshore islands and lighthouses. At low tide you can walk out to Fox Island. Flush toilets and showers on-site.<br/><br/>Why go: Repeatedly ranked one of the best beaches in Maine — wide clean sand, an island you can walk to at low tide, real lighthouse/island views.<br/><br/>Who it's for: Beach days with kids, swimmers, anyone wanting classic Maine coastline without southern Maine's crowds.<br/><br/>Likes: Cleanliness, space, scenery, a calmer crowd compared to York/Ogunquit.<br/><br/>Dislikes: Entrance fee; parking scarce on peak summer days.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Gets crowded and parking fills up on summer weekends — arrive early<br/>- There's a state park entrance fee (a season pass may be worth it if visiting more than once)<br/>- Pair with Fort Popham, right next door at the same beach<br/>- Good spot for surf fishing as well as swimming/walking<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Popham+Beach+State+Park/@43.738436,-69.798309,15z]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Beach</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>waves</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>purple</value></Data>
