  <Placemark>
    <name>Porcupine Islands Bar Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Porcupine Islands<br/><br/>📍 Offshore from Bar Harbor, ME (coordinate is the Bar Harbor Town Pier, the typical kayak/tour launch point)<br/><br/>The chain of islands (Bald, Sheep, Burnt, Long, and Rum Key Porcupine) visible right from Bar Harbor's waterfront. Despite being constantly in view from town, they're visited far less frequently than the rest of the park — actually reaching them requires a sea-kayak tour.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Book a sea-kayak tour out of the Bar Harbor Town Pier to actually visit — no casual walk-up access<br/>- Great subject for photos from the Shore Path even without a boat trip]]></description>
