  <Placemark>
    <name>Porter Preserve Boothbay ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Porter Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Kimballtown Road, Barters Island, Boothbay, ME<br/><br/>A 23-acre Boothbay Region Land Trust preserve out on Barters Island, described by BRLT itself as one of the most beloved in the region. An easy 1.1-mile path winds through heavily wooded old-growth spruce, oak, and pine, with several benches positioned for scenic Sheepscot River estuary views — seals are commonly spotted from shore at low tide. The preserve also includes a small beach, Roberts Wharf (a real working lobstering waterfront, not just scenery), and a Memorial Grove with rustic seating.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Getting there is part of the experience: from Route 27 at Boothbay Center, take Corey Lane (0.3 mi), right on Barters Island Road (2.2 mi, crossing two bridges), left on Kimballtown Road (0.5 mi), then left onto the dirt Porter Preserve Street (0.1 mi).<br/>- Primary parking is in a small lot past the cemetery; overflow parking is near the stacked lobster traps at the end of Kimballtown Road.<br/>- Dogs must stay leashed throughout.<br/>- Time it near low tide for the best chance of spotting seals from the overlook benches.<br/>- Combine with a stop at Roberts Wharf to see the island's actual working lobster fleet, not just a trail.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
