  <Placemark>
    <name>Portland Breakwater Lighthouse South Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Portland Breakwater Lighthouse ("Bug Light")<br/><br/>📍 Bug Light Park, Pickett Street, South Portland, ME<br/><br/>Built in 1855 in wood after an 1831 storm damaged Portland Harbor's entrance, then rebuilt as the current ornate 26-foot cast-iron tower in 1875, its design based on a fourth-century Greek monument. Deactivated in 1942 and relit in 2002 as a private navigation aid.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds open at Bug Light Park, easy walk, great photo spot; tower closed.<br/>- The original Fresnel lens is at the nearby South Portland Coast Guard Station.]]></description>
