  <Placemark>
    <name>Portland City Hall Congress St Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Portland City Hall<br/><br/>📍 389 Congress Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Architecturally inspired by New York City's City Hall, Portland City Hall at 389 Congress Street is one of the city's most striking landmarks. The "U"-shaped building fills almost the entire block bounded by Congress, Chestnut, and Myrtle Streets and Cumberland Avenue.<br/><br/>The building features porticos, columns, large wings, and a majestic 200-foot tower. Inside you'll find city offices and — in the right rear wing — Merrill Auditorium, which seats 1,900 and is the home venue of the Portland Symphony Orchestra and the Kotzschmar Organ.<br/><br/>Fun fact: City Hall is built with granite from North Jay, Maine.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Portland+City+Hall/@43.6592,-70.2574,17z]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Attraction</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>star</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>green</value></Data>
    </ExtendedData>
    <Point>
      <coordinates>-70.2573592,43.6592404,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Portland City Hall Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Portland City Hall<br/><br/>Portland City Hall at 389 Congress Street is listed on the National Register of Historic Places. Cherry trees flank the entrance and the steps make a great photo spot — look up close at the City seal with the motto "Resurgam" (I shall rise again), highlighting Portland's resilience after the Great Fire of 1866.<br/><br/>During business hours, head inside to the Clocktower Café in the basement for a bite to eat, or wander through the building to admire the art collections throughout.<br/><br/>Highlights<br/>- Cherry trees and City seal at the main entrance<br/>- National Register of Historic Places<br/>- Clocktower Café (basement) — open during business hours<br/>- Public art throughout the interior<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Visit during weekday business hours to access the interior<br/>- Steps are a popular spot for photos with the City seal<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Portland+City+Hall/@43.659,−70.2574,17z]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Historical</value></Data>
