    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Portland Freedom Trail Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Portland Freedom Trail<br/><br/>The Portland Freedom Trail is part of the broader Maine Freedom Trails network. A series of granite posts with brass plaques mark the trail through downtown Portland, commemorating the people and places connected to the Underground Railroad.<br/><br/>A PDF self-guided tour is available from the Maine Historical Society at mainehistory.org.<br/><br/>Start on Commercial Street and follow the markers through the Old Port and downtown neighborhoods.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Pick up a trail map at the Maine Historical Society or download the PDF from mainehistory.<br/>- Allow 1–2 hours to walk the full trail with stops<br/>- Trail is free and self-paced<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Portland+Freedom+Trail,+Commercial+Street,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Historical</value></Data>
