    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Portland Regency Hotel Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Portland Regency Hotel<br/><br/>📍 20 Milk Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The Portland Regency Hotel at 20 Milk Street was originally built as the State of Maine Armory for Maine's National Guard in 1895. It was converted to a hotel in 1984 and in 1990 was invited by the National Trust for Historic Preservation to become a distinguished member of the Historic Hotels of America.<br/><br/>Fun fact: At the turn of the 20th century, the armory's drill hall was a popular civic auditorium and hosted the Maine Music Festival.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Portland+Regency+Hotel,+20+Milk+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
