  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Post Office Park Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Post Office Park<br/><br/>Just a short walk up from Commercial Street through the Old Port, Post Office Park sits on Middle Street between Market Street and Exchange Street.<br/><br/>Once the location of the original Post Office, the park is now home to:<br/>- A rock sculpture honoring Casco Bay's Islands<br/>- Red mailboxes — a gift from Portland's sister city Shinagawa, Japan<br/>- A small brick stage for performances<br/><br/>Directly across the street is Tommy's Park, another wonderful public space to sit and relax.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Easy to miss — it's tucked between the Old Port's busier streets<br/>- Great spot for a quiet break while exploring the Old Port<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Post+Office+Park,+Middle+Street,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
