  <Placemark>
    <name>Poughkeepsie Railroad Station NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Poughkeepsie Railroad Station<br/><br/>📍 41 Main St, Poughkeepsie, NY 12601<br/><br/>Erected in 1918 and modeled after NYC's Grand Central Station, it had fallen into disrepair and disuse in the 1960s. Carefully restored, it provides a thriving mode of transportation for Metro-North RR and Amtrak.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- National Register listed.<br/>- Stop 7 of 33 on the Poughkeepsie & LaGrange Scenic Tour (Tour 5).]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
