  <Placemark>
    <name>Power House Covered Bridge Johnson VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Power House Covered Bridge<br/><br/>📍 Off Route 100C, Johnson, VT<br/><br/>Also known as the School Street Covered Bridge, this 1872 Queen post truss bridge crosses the Gihon River (a Lamoille River tributary), named for a now-obsolete hydroelectric generating station that once stood just upstream. A heavy snow load collapsed the roof and side walls into the river in 2000; Blow & Cote rebuilt it, reopening June 29, 2002. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1974.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A short, easy stop just off the main road through Johnson village.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.6353%2C%20-72.6817]]></description>
