  <Placemark>
    <name>Printers Exchange Block Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Printers Exchange Block<br/><br/>📍 103–107 Exchange Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The Printers Exchange Block at 103–107 Exchange Street was developed between 1866 and 1867 in the immediate aftermath of the Great Fire. Architect Charles Quincy Clapp designed the building with Italian details — deep hip roofs and arched windows.<br/><br/>Originally, a twin building sat across the block to visually frame the Exchange Street area. The block reflects Portland's remarkable speed of reconstruction after the devastating fire of 1866.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/103+Exchange+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
