  <Placemark>
    <name>Prospect Harbor Lighthouse Gouldsboro ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Prospect Harbor Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Prospect Harbor, Gouldsboro, ME<br/><br/>Established April 2, 1849 as a granite conical tower, discontinued in 1859 for lack of traffic, then reestablished in 1870 with an alternating red-and-white flash. The wooden conical tower seen today dates to 1891.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Sits on a Navy installation — grounds, dwelling, and tower closed to the public.<br/>- View from the entrance gate on Lighthouse Road, or across the harbor along Route 186.<br/>- Easy add-on to a Schoodic Peninsula loop from Bar Harbor.]]></description>
