  <Placemark>
    <name>Pumpkin Island Lighthouse Little Deer Isle ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Pumpkin Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Pumpkin Island, near Little Deer Isle, ME (Eggemoggin Reach)<br/><br/>Built in 1854–55 to guide vessels through the commercially important Eggemoggin Reach, this round brick tower held one of the first Fresnel lenses used in Maine. It operated for nearly 78 years before decommissioning in 1933 and passing into private hands.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned, no public access — visible from the Deer Isle bridge area and passing boats.]]></description>
