  <Placemark>
    <name>Rachel Carson Salt Pond Preserve. New Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-07T10:45:00<br/><br/>Rachel Carson Salt Pond Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Off Route 32, New Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A Nature Conservancy-maintained tidal salt pond where pioneering marine biologist Rachel Carson conducted the research behind The Edge of the Sea. An easy 1.1-mile trail winds past tide pools stocked with lobster, shrimp, starfish, crabs, and hermit crabs.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Rating most in question of this batch: listed at 4.8, but Tripadvisor ranks it only #6 of 9 things to do in New Harbor with "mixed but generally positive" reviews — the biggest gap between claimed and independently-found signal in this whole set. Worth a fresh check before building an itinerary around it.<br/>- Check low tide before visiting — tide pools are the whole point.<br/>- Parking is very limited and there are no restrooms on site.]]></description>
