  <Placemark>
    <name>Ragged Mountain Preserve Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Ragged Mountain Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Thorndike Brook Trailhead: 223 Hope St, Hope, ME (smoothest access); also Camden Snow Bowl (20 Barnestown Rd, Camden) and a Route 17 lot maintained by Georges River Land Trust<br/><br/>A 2,645-acre conservation and recreation complex on a 1,300 ft mountain, with 30+ miles of combined trail — the 6.5 mi Round the Mountain Trail (hiking/biking, machine-built gravel), 11.5 mi of foot-only hiking trails (partly the Georges Highland Path, run by partner Georges River Land Trust), and 15+ mi of mountain-biking trails split between the Camden Snow Bowl (steeper, technical) and Goose River (flatter, more moderate) networks.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Thorndike Brook Trailhead has the smoothest surface and most gradual ascent — best for a first visit<br/>- Snow Bowl access is better for mountain biking; Goose River trailhead is off Rollins Rd (do not park on the road)<br/>- GHP hiking-only trails to Spruce and Ragged Mountains access from a Route 17 lot with a Georges River Land Trust sign<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
