  <Placemark>
    <name>Ram Island Ledge Lighthouse Cape Elizabeth ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Ram Island Ledge Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Ram Island Ledge, 1.2 miles offshore from Portland Head Light, Cape Elizabeth, ME<br/><br/>Built after the steamer Californian ran aground on this reef in 1900; Congress authorized the $166,000 lighthouse and fog signal in 1902, completed in 1905. Automated in 1959 and now solar-powered.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned, closed to the public — best seen from Portland Head Light itself or a Portland Discovery boat tour.<br/>- Natural pairing with a Portland Head Light visit — they're visible together from the point.]]></description>
