  <Placemark>
    <name>Ram Island Lighthouse Boothbay Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Ram Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Ram Island, eastern side of Boothbay Harbor's mouth, ME<br/><br/>First lit November 5, 1883 after 45 years of deliberation, this 35-foot cylindrical tower on a granite foundation guides vessels through Fisherman's Island Passage. First keeper Samuel John Cavanor — who had a prosthetic leg — served from 1883 to 1913 through storms that destroyed the walkway and damaged the lantern.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds open, dwelling and tower closed. Distant view from Ocean Point via Route 96, or via Maine Maritime Museum / Cap'n Fish's cruises.<br/>- Original Fresnel lens on display at the Boothbay Regional Historical Society.]]></description>
