  <Placemark>
    <name>Red Hill River Moultonborough NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Red Hill River<br/><br/>📍 Moultonborough, NH<br/><br/>A small river in Moultonborough's Red Hill watershed. Red Hill itself — a few miles from this point — carries a fire tower on the national historic lookout register, with panoramic views spanning both Lake Winnipesaukee and Squam Lake; the Red Hill Fire Tower Loop Trail (3.6 miles, moderate) is the more notable stop if choosing between the two.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- If the goal is the view, head for the Red Hill Fire Tower Loop trailhead rather than this river point specifically.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.7442%2C%20-71.4081]]></description>
