    <name>Rest Plaus Historic District Stone Ridge NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Rest Plaus Historic District<br/><br/>📍 Old Kings Highway / Rest Plaus Road / Lucas Turnpike, Stone Ridge, NY<br/><br/>Encompasses 55 contributing buildings, four sites, ten structures, and one object along a stretch of farmland that has stayed in continuous agricultural use for over 250 years — Colonial, Federal, and Greek Revival farmsteads illustrating the area's agricultural and early industrial development from 1700 to 1949. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1995.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A driving/cycling district rather than a single stop — best experienced along Old Kings Highway between Stone Ridge and High Falls.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.8200%2C%20-74.1645]]></description>
