  <Placemark>
    <name>River-Link Trail Edgecomb ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[River~Link Trail<br/><br/>📍 North trailhead: River Road, Newcastle, ME; south trailhead: McKay Road, Edgecomb, ME (south coordinate is a proxy — nearest River Rd segment, not the exact McKay Rd pin)<br/><br/>A ~5-7 mile wilderness corridor linking Newcastle to Edgecomb without crossing a single road — passes cellar holes and old apple trees near Mount Hunger, an old stone bridge, and beaver flowages. 1,148 ft elevation gain over its length.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Long point-to-point trail — plan a car shuttle or an out-and-back rather than attempting the whole corridor casually<br/>- Also functions as an access trail to Dodge Point from the south end<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/river-link-trail/]]></description>
