  <Placemark>
    <name>Robert A Thompson House Crawford NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Robert A. Thompson House<br/><br/>📍 NY 302, Thompson Ridge, Town of Crawford, Orange County, NY<br/><br/>Built in 1822 in the Federal style along NY 302 in the Thompson Ridge hamlet — one of three historic Thompson family properties in the area, alongside the Alexander Thompson House and the Andrew Thompson Farmstead. Descendants established a Dutch-Belt dairy farm on the land that still operates. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1998.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Well south of the byway's core — a detour destination near Middletown, not a natural stop on the main loop.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.5600%2C%20-74.3422]]></description>
