  <Placemark>
    <name>Rockland Breakwater Lighthouse Rockland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-10T09:00:00<br/><br/>Rockland Breakwater Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Rockland ME<br/><br/>Walk 7/8 of a mile out into Rockland Harbor on a narrow granite block breakwater — completely exposed to the bay, with lobster boats and schooners passing on either side — to reach a 1902 lighthouse still in active service. One of the most distinctive walking experiences in coastal Maine. The return walk faces the Camden Hills.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Allow 45–60 minutes for the round trip.<br/>- The breakwater is unprotected — wear layers even in August.<br/>- The lighthouse keeper's house is occasionally open for tours on weekend afternoons.<br/>- Park at Samoset Resort or Breakwater Park at the end of Samoset Road.]]></description>
