  <Placemark>
    <name>Rockland Harbor Southwest Lighthouse Rockland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Rockland Harbor Southwest Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Rockland Harbor, Rockland, ME<br/><br/>An outlier on this list: privately built by Dr. Bruce Woolett between 1981 and 1987, not a historic government station. It received a fifth-order Fresnel lens from the Doubling Point Range Lights in 1989 and was formally recognized as a Coast Guard aid to navigation that year. Sold for $540,000 in 2018.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned, no public access — a curiosity to know about rather than a stop to plan.]]></description>
