  <Placemark>
    <name>Rockport Harbor &amp; Opera House Rockport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Rockport Harbor & Opera House<br/><br/>📍 Rockport ME<br/><br/>A small, classic Maine harbor village — sailboats and fishing boats below, an adorable downtown just up the hill. The Historic Rockport Opera House (built 1891, 410 seats), overlooking the harbor and Mary Lea Park, anchors the village and hosts recitals, plays, and concerts throughout the season.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A quieter, less touristy alternative to Camden Harbor, just a few minutes away.<br/>- Check the Opera House schedule ahead if you want to catch a show during your stay.<br/>- Easy to combine with Aldermere Farm, which is nearby.]]></description>
