  <Placemark>
    <name>Rockport Shore Preserve Rockport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Rockport Shore Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Beauchamp Point Rd, Rockport, ME (dirt road, closed to vehicles in winter)<br/><br/>650 ft of rocky shore frontage on Rockport Harbor — the longest undeveloped stretch on the harbor — donated anonymously in 2019. Beauchamp Point Rd, a dirt town road through the property, is a popular 0.2-1.6 mi walk, often looped out to Chapel Hill Rd and Calderown Ln.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Closed to vehicle traffic in winter — good winter walking route<br/>- Can also be reached on foot directly from Rockport village<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
