  <Placemark>
    <name>Rogers Ledge Stark NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Rogers Ledge<br/><br/>📍 Kilkenny Ridge Trail, South Pond Recreation Area, Stark, NH<br/><br/>A demanding 7.7-mile round trip (about 1,837 ft of gain, 4.5–5 hours) via the Kilkenny Ridge Trail in White Mountain National Forest, rewarded with sweeping views over the White Mountains and Presidential Range — added to New Hampshire's "52 With a View" list in 2020. Along the way, a short spur diverges into Devil's Hopyard, a steep-walled, moss-covered canyon where you can hear the brook running beneath the rocks even where you can't see it.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Trailhead is at South Pond Recreation Area; the access road has a seasonal closure from mid-October through mid-June.<br/>- The Devil's Hopyard spur is short but very slow going — worth the detour if you have time.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.5501%2C%20-71.3620]]></description>
