  <Placemark>
    <name>Round Top Farm Damariscotta ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Round Top Farm<br/><br/>📍 3 Round Top Lane, Damariscotta, ME (less than 1.5 mi north of downtown on Main St/Business Route 1, opposite Great Salt Bay School)<br/><br/>1.8 miles of trails on former dairy fields along the upper Damariscotta River, managed by Coastal Rivers Conservation Trust and the Maine Bureau of Parks and Lands. Multiple mown trails of varying lengths loop the perimeters of hayfields, following hedgerows and the river shoreline — gentle terrain, upper-river views, and a good sunset spot. Includes the Rhoda and Lee Cohen River Trail, a 0.6-mile universally accessible trail (8 ft wide, gentle grade — wheelchair, stroller, and bike friendly) that also connects directly to Whaleback Shell Midden via a 0.3-mile accessible link trail.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Handicap parking available at both the Round Top Farm and Whaleback Shell Midden trailheads<br/>- The 0.3-mile accessible trail to Whaleback Shell Midden makes this a natural pairing — history plus river views in one stop<br/>- Coordinate is an estimate based on the property's described location (opposite Great Salt Bay School) — no exact trailhead coordinate was independently confirmed, worth double-checking on the ground or via Coastal Rivers' own trail map<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/round-top-farm/]]></description>
