  <Placemark>
    <name>Roy Moore Lobster Co Rockport MA</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Roy Moore Lobster Co<br/><br/>📍 39 Bearskin Neck, Rockport, MA<br/><br/>A weathered dockside lobster shack on Bearskin Neck, Rockport's historic fishing-village strip of shops and galleries — ranked #1 of 27 Rockport restaurants on Tripadvisor, and landed the 47th spot on Yelp's Top 100 Seafood Spots list. Rated 4.6 on both Tripadvisor (965 reviews) and Restaurant Guru (4,685 reviews) — a rare case where two independent sources agree closely, which is a good sign of a genuinely consistent kitchen.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Steamed lobster<br/>- Fresh oysters — specifically praised as huge and fresh<br/>- Fish cakes<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Bearskin Neck itself is worth a slow walk — shops and galleries line the same strip.<br/>- Fair pricing per reviews, not a tourist markup despite the prime location.<br/>- A good pairing with a Cape Ann day that also includes Gloucester or the Rockport waterfront generally.]]></description>
