  <Placemark>
    <name>Sabbaday Falls Albany NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Sabbaday Falls<br/><br/>📍 Kancamagus Highway, near Waterville Valley, NH<br/><br/>A 45-foot multi-cascade waterfall reached via an easy 0.7-mile out-and-back on a wide, gravel path with a gentle grade (steeper, 6–25%, only in short stretches) — manageable for young kids and mostly stroller/wheelchair friendly. Interpretive signs along the way explain how glaciers shaped the gorge over 10,000 years ago. A small loop at the end lets you see the base of the falls and climb wooden steps for a second angle.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Swimming is not allowed; dogs must be leashed.<br/>- Only open in summer/fall — icy conditions near the river make it hazardous otherwise.<br/>- Fee to park at the trailhead; picnic area and restrooms on site.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.9974%2C%20-71.3932]]></description>
