  <Placemark>
    <name>Salt + Pepper Social Newcastle ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Salt + Pepper Social<br/><br/>📍 67 Main St, Newcastle, ME<br/><br/>An elevated plant-based restaurant, gourmet vegan market, and cafe/bakery right on the Damariscotta River, established 2022. Fully seasonal menu — rotating breakfast, lunch, and dinner built around the freshest local and organic produce, plus in-house baked goods. Seating is on an enclosed river-view deck and shelled patio, or indoors at the bar and market space. Described as a beloved community gathering spot with nearly perfect reviews — not just "good for vegan," genuinely well-regarded on its own terms.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Spinach artichoke dip with focaccia<br/>- Zucchini chocolate cake<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Fully vegan — worth knowing going in if the group isn't plant-based by default, but reviews suggest it wins over non-vegans too.<br/>- The river-view deck seating is the draw when weather allows — ask for it.<br/>- Also functions as a market/bakery, so it's worth a stop even outside a full meal if you want provisions for the road.<br/>- Operates seasonally — confirm hours before planning around it.<br/><br/>More info: https://sp-foods.com/]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
