  <Placemark>
    <name>Salt Pond Hancock ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Salt Pond<br/><br/>📍 Point Road, Hancock, ME (3.8 mi from Rt 1, small 2-3 car turnoff)<br/><br/>17.9 acres — a woodland trail (0.4 mi one-way, up to 1.7 mi with road loops) to a tidal salt pond with Frenchman Bay shore frontage on Hancock Point. Connects to Carter's Beach and views of Sullivan Harbor. Not the same place as the existing Rachel Carson Salt Pond Preserve note (New Harbor, ME) — a different, unrelated preserve despite the shared name.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Small turnoff parking — only room for 2-3 cars<br/>- Not the same place as the vault's existing "Rachel Carson Salt Pond Preserve" note in New Harbor — different location entirely]]></description>
