  <Placemark>
    <name>Sam's Point Preserve Ellenville, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Sam's Point Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Ellenville, NY<br/><br/>A National Natural Landmark protecting the rarest natural community in the Shawangunks. Highlights include walking into the ice caves (cool year-round), the dwarf pitch pine barrens found almost nowhere else on Earth, and sweeping views from High Point.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- ~10 miles of trails and carriage roads; hiking, nature observation, and cross-country skiing<br/>- Access via Rt 52 south of the main overlooks, then Cragsmoor Rd<br/>- Managed by The Nature Conservancy<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.6923%2C%20-74.3735]]></description>
