  <Placemark>
    <name>Samuel Butts House Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Samuel Butts House & Store<br/><br/>📍 332–334 Fore Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Built in 1792, the Samuel Butts House at 332–334 Fore Street is one of only a few buildings along Fore Street that survived the Great Fire of July 4, 1866. The large central chimney and small window openings are distinguishing features of Colonial era architecture.<br/><br/>Mr. Butts was a tailor who moved to Portland from Boston in 1784. In 1973, the building was declared a National Landmark.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/332+Fore+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
