  <Placemark>
    <name>Sand Beach Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Sand Beach<br/><br/>📍 Acadia National Park ME<br/><br/>The only sand beach in Acadia National Park — every other shoreline is granite. The crescent of sand is formed primarily from crushed shells and sea organisms rather than quartz, giving it a pinkish cast. Surrounded by pink granite headlands, with Great Head rising on the east end. Water temperature rarely exceeds 55°F even in August.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Arrive early — the small parking area fills completely by 9am in peak season.<br/>- The Great Head Trail begins at the east end of the beach and loops the headland (1.4 miles) with dramatic cliff-top views.<br/>- The Beehive Trail starts from the same parking area — combine for a full morning.<br/>- The water is genuinely cold — most people wade rather than swim.]]></description>
