  <Placemark>
    <name>Satterlee Estate Ruins Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Satterlee Estate Ruins<br/><br/>📍 Near Great Head, Acadia National Park, ME<br/><br/>A former Gilded Age estate site along the eastern shore trail network, marked today by a surviving millstone and a small memorial plaque — the only visible traces of what was once a substantial "cottage era" property.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A minor trailside curiosity rather than a planned destination — worth a glance if you're already passing by on the Great Head/Schooner Head trail network.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3297%2C%20-68.1834]]></description>
