  <Placemark>
    <name>Schoodic Bike Path Network Schoodic ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Schoodic Bike Path Network<br/><br/>📍 Schoodic Peninsula, Acadia National Park, ME<br/><br/>An 8.3-mile network of gravel trails connecting Frazer Point, Wonsqueak Harbor, Bunker Harbor, and Birch Harbor Mountain. Far quieter than the popular auto-only Schoodic Loop Road, this system is ideal for biking or walking and sees only a fraction of the traffic of the main park attractions.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Start from Schoodic Woods Campground ranger station lot for easy access<br/>- Gravel surface suitable for hybrid or mountain bikes; also walkable<br/>- Connects multiple scenic harbor viewpoints<br/>- Excellent for avoiding peak-hour congestion<br/>- Water access and tide-pool opportunities at various points<br/>- Wildlife viewing (seals, birds) is frequent and uncrowded<br/>- Less crowded than any trail on Mount Desert Island]]></description>
