  <Placemark>
    <name>Schoodic Head Gouldsboro ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Schoodic Head<br/><br/>📍 Schoodic Peninsula, Acadia National Park, ME<br/><br/>At 440 feet, the highest point in the Schoodic section of Acadia. A moderate loop combining the Alder, Schoodic Head, and Anvil trails (about 2.5 miles, ~375 ft gain) climbs through varied forest to a summit with sweeping views: Frenchman Bay and its islands to the west, Mount Desert Island and Cadillac Mountain across the water, and two lighthouses visible — Mark Island Light nearby and Egg Rock Light farther off toward MDI.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Start from the small Blueberry Hill parking area, about half a mile past the loop road's junction with Schoodic Point Road.<br/>- A good half-day hike if you want more elevation than the flat coastal walks nearby.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3507%2C%20-68.0530]]></description>
