  <Placemark>
    <name>Schoodic Institute Welcome Center Rockefeller Hall Winter Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Schoodic Institute Welcome Center at Rockefeller Hall<br/><br/>📍 9 Atterbury Circle, Winter Harbor, ME<br/><br/>Built in 1933 to house Navy personnel when this was an active naval base, Rockefeller Hall now serves as the welcome center for the Schoodic Institute — Acadia's research and education partner. Exhibits cover the old Navy base's history alongside general park information; there's a gift shop on site.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open 7 days a week in summer, weekdays the rest of the year — a good first stop when arriving on the Schoodic side of the park.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3362%2C%20-68.0591]]></description>
