  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Schoodic Institute Winter Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Schoodic Institute<br/><br/>📍 Schoodic Peninsula, Acadia National Park, ME<br/><br/>A research and education institute based on Schoodic Peninsula that offers free ranger programs, guided nature walks, and specialized activities like birding walks. These programs provide insider-style access to the peninsula with limited capacity and minimal crowd overlap with typical park day-trippers.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Check the daily program schedule when you arrive<br/>- Free ranger programs often fill up early<br/>- Excellent for learning about local ecology and wildlife<br/>- Birding walks if you're interested in ornithology<br/>- Access to the Sundew Trail and other quiet shoreline areas<br/>- The institute itself is a quiet, educational hub<br/>- Much fewer visitors than main Acadia attractions]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
