  <Placemark>
    <name>Schoodic Peninsula Winter Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Schoodic Peninsula<br/><br/>📍 Schoodic Point, Winter Harbor, ME<br/><br/>If you want Acadia's dramatic pink granite coastline without the Tour Bus traffic, the Schoodic Peninsula is your answer. It's technically part of Acadia National Park, but feels worlds away from the crowded main Loop Road.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Drive or take the ferry across the bay from Bar Harbor (ferry option is scenic in itself)<br/>- The Schoodic Loop Road offers stunning coastal views<br/>- Less crowded than the main Park Loop Road on Mount Desert Island<br/>- Pink granite formations create dramatic photo opportunities<br/>- Various pullouts and short walks along the peninsula<br/>- Bring a jacket; it's often windier than the main island]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
