  <Placemark>
    <name>Schoodic Point Winter Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Schoodic Point<br/><br/>📍 Schoodic Peninsula, Winter Harbor, ME<br/><br/>The southern tip of the Schoodic Peninsula, and the highlight of Acadia's mainland district. Glowing pink granite slopes into the sea, laced with dark basaltic dikes that forced their way through the older rock — some of the best-exposed dikes on the Maine coast. During rough seas, waves shoot through fractures in the granite in dramatic geysers, similar to Thunder Hole but on a grander, less crowded scale.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Rogue waves happen without warning and can sweep people off the rocks — stay well back from the water's edge, especially in rough conditions.<br/>- Far less crowded than Mount Desert Island's equivalent spots — one of the best reasons to make the detour out to Schoodic.<br/>- Wet granite is extremely slippery; watch footing even on calm days.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3324%2C%20-68.0611]]></description>
