    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Schoodic Woods Campground Winter Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Schoodic Woods Campground<br/><br/>📍 1.5 miles southeast of Winter Harbor, ME (Schoodic Peninsula)<br/><br/>Opened in 2015, Acadia's newest campground and the first built in the park since the original Civilian Conservation Corps-era campgrounds. About 93 wooded sites across two loops (most with electric, some with water too), all within a 15-minute walk of the ocean. A 6-mile, one-way loop road offers views of lighthouses, seabirds, and forested islands. Roughly 60-70 minutes from Bar Harbor and the main part of the park.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Reservations only through Recreation. — 90% released 6 months out, the rest 14 days ahead on a rolling basis.<br/>- No showers in the campground itself; showers are available in Winter Harbor.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3813%2C%20-68.0643]]></description>
