  <Placemark>
    <name>Schooner Head Overlook and Anemone Cave Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Schooner Head Overlook / Anemone Cave<br/><br/>📍 Schooner Head Road, Acadia National Park, ME<br/><br/>A dramatic cliff-top viewpoint named for a rock formation resembling a schooner's bow, with views out to Egg Rock Light and across Frenchman Bay. Below the cliffs sits Anemone Cave, historically a spot to view tide pools and sea anemones at low tide.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The overlook itself is a quick, easy roadside stop with a short walk from the parking area.<br/>- Anemone Cave access has become discouraged/hazardous due to erosion in recent years — verify current NPS guidance before attempting the scramble down; the overlook alone is worth the stop regardless.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3456%2C%20-68.1761]]></description>
