  <Placemark>
    <name>Schooner Surprise Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Schooner Surprise<br/><br/>📍 1 Bay View St, Camden Harbor, ME 04843<br/><br/>Two-masted schooner built 1917–18, one of the few surviving vessels designed by noted naval architect Thomas F. McManus. Runs relaxed 2-hour public day sails and private charters on Penobscot Bay for up to 18 passengers.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Historic vessel — the McManus pedigree is a real draw for sailing enthusiasts<br/>- Departs Camden Harbor<br/><br/>More info: https://www.schoonersurprise.com/]]></description>
