  <Placemark>
    <name>Seal Cove Shore Preserve South Bristol ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Seal Cove Shore Preserve<br/><br/>📍 211 S Road, South Bristol, ME<br/><br/>Fresh- and saltwater wetlands, towering white pines, and 3,000 ft of water frontage — crosses a genuine 'primeval wetland' and borders economically significant clam flats. ~1.0-1.2 mi loop, 85 ft gain.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/seal-cove-shore-preserve/]]></description>
