  <Placemark>
    <name>Sears Island Searsport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Sears Island<br/><br/>📍 Sears Island Road, Searsport ME<br/><br/>The largest undeveloped, uninhabited, causeway-accessible island on the U.S. East Coast. No cars allowed on the island itself — park on the causeway and explore on foot or bike. Popular for hiking and birdwatching.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Vehicles aren't permitted on the island — park on the causeway near the gate, then walk or bike in.<br/>- Flat and easy, good for an unhurried nature walk.<br/>- Pairs well with Penobscot Marine Museum or the Antique Mall if you're already spending the day in Searsport.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
