  <Placemark>
    <name>Seawall Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Seawall<br/><br/>📍 Seawall Picnic Area, western Mount Desert Island, Acadia National Park ME<br/><br/>A quiet, less-crowded counterpart to the busier eastern side of the park — a natural boulder seawall built by ocean storms, with picnic tables scattered along the shore and in the woods across the road from Seawall Campground. Good stop for the "quiet side" loop along with Bass Harbor Head Light and Ship Harbor.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Parking lot holds ~2 dozen vehicles at the T-intersection; overflow parking along the road<br/>- Tables split across both sides of the road — some with grills, some without<br/>- Pairs well with a visit to Bass Harbor Head Lighthouse or Ship Harbor Nature Trail nearby]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
