  <Placemark>
    <name>Seguin Island Lighthouse Georgetown ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Seguin Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Seguin Island, ~2.5 miles south of Popham Beach, mouth of the Kennebec River, ME<br/><br/>Authorized by President George Washington and established in 1796 — Maine's second lighthouse. The current granite tower (1857) carries a Henry-Lepaute first-order Fresnel lens, the highest focal plane in the state at 186 feet. In 1998, a petition with over 7,200 signatures helped keep the historic lens in place rather than replace it with a modern optic.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open Memorial Day through Labor Day — climb the tower and visit the small museum in the keeper's dwelling.<br/>- Reach by private charter or Maine Maritime Museum public cruise; Friends of Seguin Island Light maintains a charter list and guest quarters for members.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
