    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Sentinel Pine Covered Bridge Franconia Notch NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Sentinel Pine Covered Bridge<br/><br/>📍 Flume Gorge trail, Franconia Notch State Park, NH<br/><br/>Built in 1939 by the Society for the Protection of New Hampshire Forests, from the wood of the "Sentinel Pine" — a nearly 175-foot pine that had stood on the cliff above The Pool for centuries before the 1938 hurricane toppled it. About 60 feet long, spanning the Pemigewasset River as part of the Flume Gorge walking loop.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Included in the Flume Gorge admission/walk — not a separate stop.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.1043%2C%20-71.6780]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
