    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Sesuit Harbor Cafe Dennis MA</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Sesuit Harbor Cafe<br/><br/>📍 357 Sesuit Neck Rd, East Dennis, Dennis, MA<br/><br/>A counter-service seafood spot on Cape Cod's north side, with outdoor tables overlooking Northside Marina and Cape Cod Bay. Cash only, dog-friendly, and BYOB. Menu runs boiled lobster, fried clams, a full raw bar, Angus steak tips, grilled salmon, and baked stuffed cod — broader than a typical shack. Rated 4.5 on Google across nearly 1,900 reviews.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Lobster roll — shredded meat plus knuckle, specifically praised<br/>- Raw bar selections<br/>- Fried clams<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Cash only — bring enough, there's no card option.<br/>- BYOB is allowed — bring your own drinks if you want them with the meal.<br/>- Open 7am–8:30pm daily — works for breakfast through dinner, unusual for a shack of this type.<br/>- Marina views make it a genuinely scenic stop, not just a food break.<br/><br/>More info: https://sesuit-harbor-cafe.com/]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Restaurant</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>utensils</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>purple</value></Data>
    </ExtendedData>
    <Point>
      <coordinates>-70.152973,41.7540627,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Shawangunk Grasslands National Wildlife Refuge Wallkill, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Shawangunk Grasslands National Wildlife Refuge<br/><br/>📍 Wallkill, NY<br/><br/>Designated an Important Bird Area by Audubon New York. More than 150 species have been recorded, including northern harrier, upland sandpiper, short-eared owl, and bobolink.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Entrance on Hoagerburgh Rd (Rt 18) in the Town of Shawangunk<br/>- Two miles of walking trails through open meadow — a striking contrast to the densely-wooded Shawangunks nearby<br/>- Good winter site for the endangered short-eared owl<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.6120%2C%20-74.1690]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
