      <coordinates>-74.169,41.612,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Shawangunk Ridge</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Shawangunk Ridge<br/><br/>📍 Runs through Ulster, Orange, and Sullivan counties, NY<br/><br/>The "Gunks" — a ridge of white quartz-conglomerate cliffs and pitch pine barrens running roughly north-south, from the Rosendale/High Falls area down through Mohonk, Minnewaska, and Sam's Point, and on into Orange and Sullivan counties. It's the geological spine behind nearly everything on this byway: the climbing at Peter's Kill and the Trapps, the escarpments at Sam's Point, and the white cliffs visible from Route 44/55.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Not a single stop — this note exists to hold the ridge itself as a concept; the actual visitor sites (Mohonk Preserve, Minnewaska, Sam's Point) each have their own notes.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.6505%2C%20-74.4110]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
