  <Placemark>
    <name>Sheldon Hill Dutchess County, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Sheldon Hill<br/><br/>📍 Dutchess County, NY<br/><br/>A modest wooded rise near the Taconic State Parkway, part of the string of small hills and ridgelines that give the byway its rolling, scenic character.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A minor stop best combined with nearby Old Roundtop or James Baird State Park rather than visited on its own.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.755915,-73.743753]]></description>
