  <Placemark>
    <name>Sides Preserve Rockport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Sides Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Route 17, Rockport, ME (roadside parking just after Maces Pond)<br/><br/>8-acre preserve on Maces Pond, a popular warm-water fishing spot bordered by Rt 17. A short 0.4 mi loop trail follows the waterfront with glimpses of neighboring Rockville Cemetery; a hand-carry boat launch sits at the Rt 17 pull-off. Donated 1997 by Andrew and Virginia Sides.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Fishing accessible from shore, by boat, and on the ice<br/>- Look for the Preserve sign right on the road<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
