  <Placemark>
    <name>Simonton Quarry Preserve Rockport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Simonton Quarry Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Main St, Rockport, ME (1.4 mi south of Route 1, past Maine Sport)<br/><br/>Three historic 1800s lime quarries, once served by a narrow-gauge railroad hauling lime to the Rockport harbor kilns. No trail exists — it's a picnic-and-photo pull-off with steep quarry edges. Gifted to The Nature Conservancy in the early 1970s, transferred to Coastal Mountains Land Trust in 2014.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- No trail — use real caution near the quarries' steep edges<br/>- Look for a green gate and small Preserve sign at the pull-off<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
