  <Placemark>
    <name>Somesville ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Somesville<br/><br/>📍 Somesville, Mount Desert, ME<br/><br/>Often called the prettiest village in Maine — the oldest settlement on Mount Desert Island, at the head of Somes Sound. Best known for the arched white Selectmen's Building footbridge over the millpond, a classic New England scene of white clapboard houses and church spires. Quiet and easy to combine with a drive to the quiet side of the island.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The footbridge and millpond are the classic photo — best light in early morning or late afternoon.<br/>- A natural stop on the way to or from Southwest Harbor, Somesville is right at the junction of Routes 102 and 198.<br/>- Coordinates above are an approximation of the village center — worth confirming against Google Maps before you go.]]></description>
