  <Placemark>
    <name>South Peak Kinsman Mountain Franconia Notch NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[South Peak Kinsman Mountain<br/><br/>📍 Franconia Notch, NH (Appalachian Trail)<br/><br/>One of New Hampshire's 48 four-thousand-footers, at 4,358 feet, on the western side of Franconia Notch. A demanding 10.2-mile out-and-back hike starting at Lafayette Place Campground, crossing the Pemigewasset River and climbing via the Lonesome Lake Trail and Lonesome Lake Hut (AMC-operated). The summit is wide open with expansive views in every direction — its neighbor North Kinsman has the more dramatic pointed-peak view across the Notch to the Franconia Range.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Extreme difficulty rating, ~3,100 ft elevation gain — a serious full-day hike, not a casual outing.<br/>- Trailhead parking at Lafayette Place Campground, The Flume, or The Basin along the Franconia Notch Parkway.<br/>- Exposed ridgeline — check weather and bring traction devices in shoulder season.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.1230%2C%20-71.7366]]></description>
