  <Placemark>
    <name>Squam Lakes Natural Science Center Holderness NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Squam Lakes Natural Science Center<br/><br/>📍 23 Science Center Rd, Holderness, NH<br/><br/>Founded in 1966, this 200-acre campus of fields, forests, ponds, and gardens is home to non-releasable native animals living in naturalistic habitats, plus accessible walking trails, Kirkwood Gardens, and the Blue Heron School. The "Discover Squam" pontoon-boat cruise covers the lake's history, geography, and its most famous claim to fame: On Golden Pond was filmed here over 40 years ago.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Lake cruises require advance reservations and payment — space is limited, book ahead.<br/>- Budget 2–3 hours for the trails and animal habitats alone.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.7344%2C%20-71.5880]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
