  <Placemark>
    <name>Squirrel Point Lighthouse Arrowsic ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Squirrel Point Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Arrowsic Island, Kennebec River, near Bath, ME<br/><br/>Named for the frigate Squirrel, which ran aground here in 1717. Built in 1898 following an 1892 Lighthouse Board report on the need for more Kennebec River aids to navigation — a frame tower, dwelling, and barn. The historic fifth-order Fresnel lens is now on display at the Portland Head Lighthouse museum.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds open via a just-over-half-mile footpath from a parking area on Bald Head Road off Route 127; dwelling and tower closed.<br/>- Pairs well with the nearby Doubling Point lights on the same stretch of river.<br/>- Maine Maritime Museum (Bath) and Cap'n Fish's (Boothbay Harbor) cruises pass by.]]></description>
