  <Placemark>
    <name>St Croix River Lighthouse Calais ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[St. Croix River Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Dochet Island, St. Croix River, near Calais, ME (Canadian border)<br/><br/>First lit February 2, 1857, discontinued in 1859, and reestablished in 1869 to serve the busy timber port of Calais. Dochet Island was also the site of a short-lived French settlement in 1604 — among the earliest European footholds in North America. Transferred to the National Park Service in 1958; the original lighthouse was destroyed by fire in October 1976.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The island is largely off-limits; the lighthouse itself is gone. Mainland interpretive exhibits and trails cover the history.<br/>- Extremely far north — realistically a Calais-area stop, not a Bar Harbor day trip.]]></description>
