  <Placemark>
    <name>St. James Episcopal Church Hyde Park NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[St. James Episcopal Church<br/><br/>📍 Albany Post Rd, Hyde Park, NY 12538<br/><br/>Sometimes called "the President's church" because FDR was a member and vestryman of this congregation, formed 1811. President and Mrs. Roosevelt brought King George VI and Queen Elizabeth of Britain here for services during their 1939 visit to the United States and Canada. Destroyed by fire in 1984, it has since been reconstructed.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Visitors welcome.<br/>- Stop 6 of 26 on the Hyde Park, Clinton & Pleasant Valley Scenic Tour (Tour 3).]]></description>
