  <Placemark>
    <name>St. Patrick's Catholic Church Newcastle ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[St. Patrick's Catholic Church<br/><br/>📍 Academy Hill Road, Newcastle, ME<br/><br/>The oldest surviving Catholic church building in New England, built in 1808. A modest brick colonial structure on Academy Hill overlooking the Damariscotta River, listed on the National Register of Historic Places.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Coordinates are an approximate match to Academy Hill Road — no precise street-address geocode was available.<br/>- Still an active parish; check for open hours or services before visiting, and be respectful during services.]]></description>
