  <Placemark>
    <name>Staatsburgh State Historic Site Staatsburg, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Staatsburgh State Historic Site<br/><br/>📍 Staatsburg, NY<br/><br/>A 79-room Gilded Age Beaux-Arts mansion built by the Mills family in 1895, overlooking the Hudson River — one of the finest American Gilded Age estates, with free grounds access.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds free year-round; house tours ticketed and seasonal<br/>- The formal gardens and river views rival any estate in the valley<br/>- Combine with Norrie Point just north — same property, different character<br/>- Also stop 10 of 26 on the Hyde Park, Clinton & Pleasant Valley Scenic Tour (Tour 3)<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Staatsburgh+State+Historic+Site+Staatsburg,+NY]]></description>
