  <Placemark>
    <name>Stephenson Preserve Belfast ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Stephenson Preserve<br/><br/>📍 City Point Rd, Belfast, ME (walk 300 ft down from the Rail Trail parking lot on High St/Rt 137)<br/><br/>A short hike close to downtown Belfast, with a small waterfall that flows during spring melt and heavy rain. Easy to extend into a longer outing via nearby Pendleton Park and the Belfast Rail Trail along the Passagassawakeag River. Donated 2000 by Ralph Stephenson.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Use caution walking down the busy City Point Rd from the Rail Trail lot<br/>- 0.3 mi loop, moderate, 120 ft gain<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
