      <coordinates>-74.1886,41.8111,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Stilwill Westbrook Stone House Accord NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Stilwill Westbrook Stone House<br/><br/>📍 Old Kings Highway, Town of Rochester, near Accord, NY<br/><br/>Also known as the Dirck Westbrook Stone House, at 482 Old Kings Highway. Dirck Westbrook is associated with the property from around 1700, and the earliest surviving stone portion dates to the early 18th century — a century later, a larger Greek Revival front was added. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1999, along with accompanying outbuildings.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Private residence — view from the road, part of a cluster of stone houses (with the nearby Stilwell and Van Wagenen houses) worth driving past together.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.8069%2C%20-74.1953]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Historical</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>scroll</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>green</value></Data>
    </ExtendedData>
    <Point>
      <coordinates>-74.1953,41.8069,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Stockade District Kingston Kingston, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Stockade District Kingston<br/><br/>📍 Kingston, NY<br/><br/>New York's first capital (1777), with a walkable uptown district of 17th-century stone buildings, galleries, and the best concentration of restaurants in Kingston.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Walk the original stockade walls — informational markers throughout<br/>- Highest density of good restaurants on Wall and John Streets<br/>- Allow at least half a day — the district is compact but dense<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Stockade+District+Kingston+Kingston,+NY]]></description>
