  <Placemark>
    <name>Stone Ridge Historic District Stone Ridge, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Stone Ridge Historic District<br/><br/>📍 Stone Ridge, NY<br/><br/>Documents the architectural evolution of Hudson Valley stone houses, from low 1-1/2 story settlement-period dwellings to imposing two-story residences. Nearby, the Rest Plaus historic district covers 725 acres of continuously farmed open space, and Kripplebush preserves stone and clapboard structures with numerous outbuildings.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Main Street, Stone Ridge, on Rt 209<br/>- Hasbrouck House is now the Inn at Stone Ridge<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.8309%2C%20-74.1235]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
