      <coordinates>-71.2062,44.0654,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Stover Preserve Belfast ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Stover Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Doak Rd, Belfast, ME (parking immediately after Doak's Machine Shop, red building)<br/><br/>A scenic nature walk close to downtown Belfast along the Passagassawakeag River — old-field pines, mixed conifer-hardwood stands with extensive bog bridging, and a wild stretch of river. Conserved 2004 in partnership with Lee and Donna Stover.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- 0.9 mi loop, easy, 90 ft gain — extensive boardwalk over the boggy sections<br/>- Can also park just down the street at Head of Tide Preserve<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalmountains.org]]></description>
