  <Placemark>
    <name>Stratton Island South Bristol ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Stratton Island<br/><br/>📍 No road address — boat/paddle access only, small gravel cove on the island's NE end, South Bristol, ME<br/><br/>Coastal Rivers' first and largest island preserve (28 acres) — a moss-carpeted spruce forest loop with traces of an ancient shell midden and early-1900s Stratton family habitation. ~1.2 mi loop.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Boat or paddle-craft access only — no road route exists<br/>- Avoid April-July: active eagle/osprey nesting<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/stratton-island/]]></description>
