  <Placemark>
    <name>Sugar Hill Scenic Vista Kancamagus NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Sugar Hill Scenic Vista<br/><br/>📍 Kancamagus Highway (NH 112), roughly halfway between Lincoln and Conway<br/><br/>A paved overlook with a gazebo, rock walls, and a viewing platform, taking in Mt. Tremont, Owl Cliff, Bear Mountain, and Sugar Hill itself. Ample parking makes it one of the easiest big-view stops on the whole byway — a favorite during fall foliage season.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Not to be confused with the town of Sugar Hill, NH near Franconia — this is an unrelated overlook named after the mountain it faces.<br/>- Best light and color in early October for foliage; expect it to be crowded then.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.0314%2C%20-71.5169]]></description>
