  <Placemark>
    <name>Sundew Trail Schoodic ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Sundew Trail<br/><br/>📍 Schoodic Institute, Schoodic Peninsula, ME<br/><br/>A flat, easy 0.7-mile nature trail departing from the Schoodic Institute that leads to a private rocky shoreline often completely empty of other visitors. Ideal for a low-key nature break, birding, or photography without the crowding of main park attractions.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Accessible from Schoodic Institute parking area<br/>- Completely flat, family-friendly<br/>- Often overlooked by park visitors—genuinely quiet<br/>- Good for early morning walks or afternoon breaks<br/>- Bring binoculars if you're a birder; wildlife viewing is excellent<br/>- Rocky shore access available; tide pools at lower tide]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
