  <Placemark>
    <name>Swift River Covered Bridge Albany NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Swift River Covered Bridge (Albany Covered Bridge)<br/><br/>📍 Passaconaway/Dugway Road, Albany, NH (6 miles west of Conway)<br/><br/>Built in 1858 by Amzi Russell and Leandre Morton for $1,300, this Paddleford truss bridge (with added arches) was destroyed by a flood soon after completion and quickly rebuilt — it then stood for over a century before a 1970 renovation. 120 feet long with a six-ton load limit and a 7'9" vehicle height restriction; closed to traffic in winter but open to foot traffic year-round.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The byway's official POI list also lists this crossing as "Saco River Bridge" — same location, likely just an alternate/mislabeled name from a different data source, since the Swift River joins the Saco nearby.<br/>- A short detour off the Kancamagus on Dugway Road, close to Russell-Colbath House.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.9848%2C%20-71.1194]]></description>
