  <Placemark>
    <name>Tabor Wing House Dover Plains NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tabor Wing House / Dover Plains Hamlet<br/><br/>📍 Mill St, Dover Plains, NY 12522<br/><br/>Dover Plains Hamlet, located on "the Great Rd. from NY," was settled in the late 18th c. but experienced its biggest growth ca. 1850 during the era of the railroad. The Federal style Tabor Wing House (NR), est. 1815 and owned by the Town of Dover Historical Society, houses the town library and the society collection. The J.H. Ketcham Hose Co., opposite, and the Jr. High School have remarkable local WPA era art landscape collections. Maple Lane leads past the Second Baptist Church (est. 1794) to the Railroad Depot, a stop on the Harlem Line.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Park here and walk.<br/>- Stop 38 of 39 on the Union Vale, Beekman, Pawling & Dover Scenic Tour (Tour 6).]]></description>
