  <Placemark>
    <name>Taconic Parkway Pleasant Valley, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Taconic Parkway<br/><br/>📍 Pleasant Valley, NY<br/><br/>A landmark stretch of the Taconic State Parkway, one of the oldest and most scenic limited-access parkways in New York, known for its curving alignment, stone bridges, and wooded medians rather than commercial development along the route.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- No commercial traffic or gas stations directly on the parkway — fuel up before getting on.<br/>- The road's tight curves and lack of shoulders reward an unhurried pace, especially in fall foliage season.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.752766,-73.769301]]></description>
