  <Placemark>
    <name>Taft Point Gouldsboro ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Taft Point<br/><br/>📍 Taft Point Road, Gouldsboro, ME (six-car gravel lot via a 1,500 ft access road)<br/><br/>65 acres (0.5 mi coastal frontage) with views of the Acadia Mountains, Stave Island, Calf Island, and Schoodic Mountain. Rocky beach for tidal exploration, eider ducks and shorebirds, and a historic well. 1.8 mi total across two 0.9 mi loops.]]></description>
