  <Placemark>
    <name>Tea at the Governors House Hyde Park VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tea at the Governor's House<br/><br/>📍 100 Main St, Hyde Park, VT<br/><br/>The 1893 Page Mansion — built in the Victorian era as a reproduction of an earlier Colonial house — now operates as The Governor's House inn, known for a full English afternoon tea service since 2001. Tea is served in the library or on the pillared portico with mountain views, with scones, cream and jam, tea sandwiches, and finger pastries. The inn's Vermont marble foyer, mirrored mantelpieces, and original gas lighting fixtures are preserved throughout. The innkeeper also runs periodic Jane Austen Weekends and an annual in-character weekend.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Tea service runs Thursdays and Sundays, 3-6pm — reservations recommended.<br/>- A distinctive, slightly whimsical stop if traveling with someone who'd appreciate a proper English tea in rural Vermont.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.5933%2C%20-72.6186]]></description>
