  <Placemark>
    <name>Tenants Harbor Lighthouse St George ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tenants Harbor Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Southern Island, Tenants Harbor, St. George, ME<br/><br/>First lit January 1, 1858, this 27-foot brick tower operated until 1933, when a bell buoy took over its job. Andrew Wyeth purchased the property in 1978 and painted it repeatedly; his son Jamie Wyeth, the current owner, continues the tradition.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned, no public access — best viewed by boat or plane.<br/>- Monhegan Boat Line's tours from Port Clyde pass by.]]></description>
