  <Placemark>
    <name>The Armory at the Regency Hotel Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[The Armory at the Regency Hotel<br/><br/>📍 20 Milk Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Designed by Frederick Tompson and constructed in 1895 as the State of Maine Armory, this was said to be one of the finest and best-equipped National Guard armories in New England. The armory's large drill hall was frequently used as a civic auditorium and hosted many concerts and gatherings.<br/><br/>Today it has been reimagined as part of the Portland Regency Hotel & Spa. The Armory is now a bar — a great place to grab a drink and discuss history surrounded by the original architecture.<br/><br/>See also: Portland Regency Hotel Portland ME for architectural history.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Portland+Regency+Hotel,+20+Milk+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
