  <Placemark>
    <name>The Blind Monk West Palm Beach FL</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Overview<br/>Type: Restaurant<br/><br/>Best known for: Small plates, drinks, live music.<br/><br/>Location context: West Palm Beach, FL.<br/><br/>Price level: $20–80 per person.<br/><br/>Visit timing: Typically open for dinner; hours are 5–10 PM, closed Sundays.<br/><br/>Typical Customers<br/>Demographics: Locals and visitors.<br/><br/>Group types: Couples, friends, families.<br/><br/>Common occasions: Casual dinners, date nights.<br/><br/>Vibe & Setting<br/>Atmosphere: Quaint and welcoming.<br/><br/>Noise level: Moderate.<br/><br/>Decor & setting: Indoor and outdoor seating available.<br/><br/>Service style: Friendly; some reviews mention variable service.<br/><br/>Recommended Dishes<br/>Overall dish consensus  <br/>Popular items include the Charcuterie Board and Spaghetti, frequently praised for taste and presentation.<br/><br/>How “top dishes” are determined  <br/>Top dishes were selected based on menu mentions, user reviews indicating favorites, and dishes appearing often in photos.<br/><br/>| Rank | Dish                | Why it stands out                          | How often it’s mentioned         | Ideal for                 |<br/>|------|---------------------|-------------------------------------------|---------------------------------|---------------------------|<br/>| 1    | Charcuterie Board   | Praised for variety and flavor combination.| Mentioned in numerous reviews. | Sharing at the table      |<br/>| 2    | Spaghetti           | Known for rich sauce and satisfying portion. | Repeatedly called out as a favorite. | Hearty main              |<br/>| 3    | Avocado Toast       | Liked for freshness and presentation.    | Mentioned multiple times.     | Lighter option            |<br/><br/>Good alternates / backup choices  <br/>- Shakshouka: Noted for its comforting flavors.<br/>- Juice: Liked for being refreshing and a good accompaniment.<br/><br/>Highlights (non-dish positives from reviews)<br/>Live music: The venue features live music, contributing to a lively atmosphere.<br/><br/>Outdoor seating: Many reviewers appreciate the availability of outdoor seating, especially in good weather.<br/><br/>Common Issues (from reviews)<br/>Inconsistent service: Some reviewers noted variability in service quality during busy times.<br/><br/>Food quality: A few patrons have commented that certain dishes did not meet their expectations.<br/><br/>Practical Notes<br/>Reservation / wait: Walk-in friendly but reservations are recommended.<br/><br/>Accessibility: Not mentioned.<br/><br/>Parking / transit: Street parking available; details not specified.<br/><br/>Best use case: Great for casual dinners with friends or a date night.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/The+Blind+Monk/@26.7073064,-80.0548012,17z/data=!3m1!4b1!4m6!3m5!1s0x88d8d661f1e50ca1:0x478246f106237670!8m2!3d26.7073064!4d-80.0522263!16s%2Fg%2F1thsb4bz?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
