  <Placemark>
    <name>The Blue Hill Peninsula &amp; Deer Isle, Maine Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[While Acadia National Park and Bar Harbor get heavily congested with major cruise lines, turning just a bit further west to the Blue Hill Peninsula offers the exact same rugged maritime beauty in near-total serenity.<br/><br/>- The Scene: Dramatic granite shorelines, hidden coves, fields of wild lupines, and sweeping views of East Penobscot Bay.<br/>    <br/>- The Food: This pocket of Maine has quietly become a sanctuary for world-class, hyper-local gastronomy. It is home to nationally recognized, hyper-seasonal restaurants where chefs work hand-in-hand with local organic farmers and fishermen. You can enjoy elevated multi-course menus, exceptional wood-fired cooking, and pristine local oysters right on the water in small, intimate dining rooms.]]></description>
