  <Placemark>
    <name>The Brick Store Bath NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[The Brick Store<br/><br/>📍 21 Lisbon Road (Route 302), Bath, NH<br/><br/>Operating since the early 1790s, this is billed as the oldest continuously operated general store in the United States. It served as Bath's post office until 1942 — some of the original post office boxes are still inside — and was decorated with antiques and 1834 counters designed to slant in at the bottom to fit the hooped skirts fashionable at the time. Known for smoked cheeses, pepperoni, and fudge. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1985.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Recent listings (Yelp, 2026) mark this store as closed — verify current status before planning a stop, especially if the historic-general-store experience itself (not just the building) is the draw.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.1712%2C%20-71.9631]]></description>
