  <Placemark>
    <name>The Cafe at Coastal Maine Botanical Gardens Boothbay ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[The Cafe at Coastal Maine Botanical Gardens<br/><br/>📍 105 Botanical Gardens Drive, Boothbay, ME (inside the Gardens, near the Great Lawn)<br/><br/>Also known as the Kitchen Garden Cafe — a casual, farm-to-table spot built into the gardens themselves, using local and organic ingredients including produce grown in the on-site Kitchen Garden. Seating is available indoors or on a patio overlooking the Great Lawn. Rated 4.4 on Tripadvisor, ranked around #9 of 22 restaurants in Boothbay — strong for what's essentially an attraction-adjacent cafe rather than a destination restaurant in its own right.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Lobster BLT — the most frequently praised dish<br/>- Tarragon chicken salad sandwich<br/>- Beet burger — the standout vegetarian option<br/>- Salads generally — reviewers consistently note the crispness and use of edible flowers from the gardens<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Seasonal hours only: open daily May 1–October 19, matching the Gardens' regular season — closed the rest of the year.<br/>- Requires Gardens admission to access, since it's inside the grounds — budget it as your lunch stop mid-visit, not a standalone trip.<br/>- Gets crowded at peak lunch hours in summer — arrive early or plan lunch slightly off-peak.<br/>- Good vegetarian, gluten-free, and vegan coverage if the group has mixed dietary needs.]]></description>
