  <Placemark>
    <name>The Century House Historical Society Rosendale NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[The Century House Historical Society<br/><br/>📍 668 Route 213, Snyder Estate, Rosendale, NY<br/><br/>A museum preserving Rosendale's history — the natural-cement industry that once produced nearly half of North America's cement, the Delaware & Hudson Canal, and the railroads that followed. Located at the Snyder Estate alongside the historic Widow Jane Mine, with business documents, photographs, and geological exhibits.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Museum open Sundays 1–4pm through early September (verify current-season hours); grounds open daily 10am–6pm.<br/>- The natural home base for visiting the neighboring Widow Jane Mine and Snyder Estate Natural Cement Historic District.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.8438%2C%20-74.0888]]></description>
