  <Placemark>
    <name>The High-Alpine Wilderness -  Crawford Notch Loop North Conway NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[The High-Alpine Wilderness: Crawford Notch Loop<br/><br/>Heading northwest out of the village on Route 302 leads you directly into the sheer granite walls of Crawford Notch. This route is all about deep valley views, dramatic elevation, and historic grand estates.<br/><br/>- The Route: Follow Route 302 West through Glen, Bartlett, and up into the heart of Crawford Notch State Park.<br/>    <br/>- The Prime Excursion: Book the Mountaineer ride via the _Conway Scenic Railroad_ right from the historic 1874 Victorian station in North Conway Village. This 4.5-hour heritage rail excursion utilizes 1950s-era transcontinental cars to climb the rugged, steep grades over the Frankenstein Trestle and deep into the notch, giving you the grandest views without the driving stress.<br/>    <br/>- Don't Miss: Stop at the historic Omni Mount Washington Resort in Bretton Woods for a drink or lunch on the expansive back veranda. The view of the entire Presidential Range from that porch is completely unmatched. On the way back, stretch your legs with a short walk to Silver Cascade or Flume Cascade, massive waterfalls that tumble right down the mountain to the side of the highway.]]></description>
