  <Placemark>
    <name>The Legendary Drive - The Kancamagus Highway &amp; Lincoln Loop North Conway NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[The Legendary Drive: The Kancamagus Highway & Lincoln Loop<br/><br/>Affectionately known to locals as "The Kank" (Route 112), this nationally designated scenic byway cuts directly through a 34-mile stretch of uninterrupted, protected White Mountain National Forest with zero commercial development.<br/><br/>- The Route: Take Route 16 South down to Conway, then turn west onto the Kancamagus Highway (Route 112), taking it all the way over the pass to Lincoln, and return via Route 3 North to Route 302 East.<br/>    <br/>- Top Stops Along the Highway:<br/>    <br/>    - Sabbaday Falls: An exceptionally easy, 15-minute gravel path walk leading to a striking, multi-tiered waterfall rushing through a tight granite gorge.<br/>        <br/>    - Sugar Hill Overlook: Offers sweeping, multi-layered panoramic vistas of the swift Saco River valley below and the peaks above.<br/>        <br/>- The Destination (Lincoln/North Woodstock): Once you hit the western end of the highway, stop for a hearty pub lunch at the _Moat Mountain Smoke House_ or cross over into North Woodstock to see the spectacular Flume Gorge—a natural, 800-foot chasm at the base of Mount Liberty featuring towering granite walls and covered bridges.]]></description>
