  <Placemark>
    <name>The Loon Center Moultonborough NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[The Loon Center & Markus Wildlife Sanctuary<br/><br/>📍 183 Lee's Mill Road, Moultonborough, NH<br/><br/>Headquarters of the Loon Preservation Committee, with free indoor exhibits, a research lab, and a gift shop, plus the adjoining 200+ acre Markus Wildlife Sanctuary — upland forest, marsh, and nearly a mile of Lake Winnipesaukee shoreline. The Loon Nest Trail and the shorter Forest Walk loop are both easy, and there's a resident breeding pair of loons on the property.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Free admission to the center; trails open dawn to dusk, seven days a week, year-round.<br/>- Good spot for a quiet nature break between the busier Winnipesaukee shoreline towns.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.7375%2C%20-71.3907]]></description>
