  <Placemark>
    <name>The Munching Meeple Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[The Munching Meeple<br/><br/>📍 Camden, ME (in Camden's old mill building)<br/><br/>A board-game café/bistro that opened in 2026 — over 450 board game titles (200+ from owners Greg and Kim Harrison's personal collection), with simple, fresh, well-executed pub food built to let you settle in for a couple of hours. Big windows, casual and whimsical, in Camden's historic old mill building. Locals say the town was missing exactly this.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Burgers and fries — the kitchen's straightforward, solid core menu<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Come for a game, not just a quick bite — the whole design is built around lingering.<br/>- Good option for a rainy-day Camden afternoon or a low-key family evening.<br/>- Motto: "put down the device, pick up the dice" — leave time to actually play something.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/The+Munching+Meeple/@44.2090977,-69.0700049,444m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m13!1m5!2m4!1sRestaurants!5m1!4e9!6e5!3m6!1s0x4cadd7c20995573f:0x7818563e1af47fcf!8m2!3d44.2099894!4d-69.0678395!15sCgtSZXN0YXVyYW50c1oNIgtyZXN0YXVyYW50c5IBCnJlc3RhdXJhbnSaAURDaTlEUVVsUlFVTnZaRU5vZEhsalJqbHZUMjVzZUdSVk1WSmFWV2h4WkdzMU5WSldUalpaYlRGclkya3dlRkl5WXhBQuABAPoBBAgAEB0!16s%2Fg%2F11z217y4qz?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYwOS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
