  <Placemark>
    <name>The Place Bakery Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[The Place Bakery<br/><br/>📍 117 Elm St, Camden, ME<br/><br/>A genuinely tiny neighborhood bakery, operating out of what used to be the owners' garage on Elm Street — small-batch, handmade baked goods built on local ingredients. Named to the New York Times' "Best Bakeries Across the U.S. Right Now" list, with a food reporter singling out its "ethereally flaky croissant dough." Also covered by NBC Boston and the Portland Press Herald for the same recognition. Rated 4.8 on Restaurant Guru and Postcard, 5.0 on Tripadvisor.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Croissants — the specific dish that earned the NYT recognition<br/>- Cheese croissants<br/>- Cinnamon rolls<br/>- Blueberry buns<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Go early — items genuinely sell out, and reviews consistently mention this.<br/>- Preordering online is worth checking if available, per social media tips from locals.<br/>- A small operation — don't expect a big seating area, this is a grab-and-go bakery.]]></description>
