  <Placemark>
    <name>The Turrets Bar Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[The Turrets<br/><br/>📍 College of the Atlantic campus, Bar Harbor, ME<br/><br/>A pink granite Gilded Age "cottage" from the 1890s, one of the most recognizable and photographed surviving cottage-era buildings in Bar Harbor. Now serves as the main administrative building for the College of the Atlantic. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Visible and photographable from the COA campus, which is open to walk through — combine with a stop at the George B. Dorr Museum of Natural History nearby.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3947%2C%20-68.2203]]></description>
