  <Placemark>
    <name>Thompson Block Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Thompson Block<br/><br/>📍 117–125 Middle Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Designed by architect George Harding in 1867, the Thompson Block at 117–125 Middle Street is distinguished by its mansard roof — a hipped gambrel roof with four sloping sides, each becoming steeper halfway down.<br/><br/>Along with the nearby Rackleff Building (127–133 Middle Street) and Woodman Block (133–141 Middle Street), Thompson Block is considered one of the most well-preserved Victorian streetscapes in all of Maine.<br/><br/>In 1973, it was added to the National Register of Historic Places.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/117+Middle+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
