  <Placemark>
    <name>Thundering Falls Trail Killington VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Thundering Falls Trail<br/><br/>📍 River Road, Killington, VT (Appalachian Trail)<br/><br/>An easy, mostly flat 0.5-mile out-and-back on a 900-foot boardwalk built by the Green Mountain Club — the first universally accessible stretch of the Appalachian Trail in Vermont. Crosses the open Ottauquechee River floodplain to reach the sixth-tallest waterfall in the state, a 140-foot cascade with a roaring lower section.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- From the junction of Route 100 and Route 4, drive 2 miles east, turn onto River Road, and continue 1.5 miles to the wheelchair-accessible parking lot.<br/>- Best March through October; dogs welcome on leash.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.6807%2C%20-72.7824]]></description>
