  <Placemark>
    <name>Thuya Garden Northeast Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Thuya Garden<br/><br/>📍 Northeast Harbor, Mount Desert Island, ME<br/><br/>High on a hill overlooking Northeast Harbor, Thuya Garden blends English flower beds with native Maine woodlands. It requires a short climb up historic stone stairs (or a quick drive up the back road) and is rarely crowded.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Parking available at the base; stone stairs climb to the main garden<br/>- English cottage garden aesthetic meets Maine forest<br/>- Seasonal flowering; spring and summer are optimal<br/>- Benches throughout for quiet contemplation<br/>- Views down to Northeast Harbor below<br/>- Much quieter than downtown attractions]]></description>
