  <Placemark>
    <name>Tidal Falls Preserve Hancock ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tidal Falls Preserve<br/><br/>📍 Tidal Falls Rd, Hancock, ME<br/><br/>A small, roughly 4-acre preserve managed by the Frenchman Bay Conservancy, built around a genuine reversing-falls phenomenon: strong tidal shifts through the narrow channel between Hancock and Sullivan create rapids and whirlpools that run one direction, slack, then reverse. Wildlife is a regular feature too — seals, osprey, kingfishers, and eagles are commonly spotted.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Time it right: arrive about an hour before the tide is due to change and stay an hour after, to see the falls run both directions.<br/>- The loop trail is short and wheelchair-accessible — an easy, low-effort stop.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.5195%2C%20-68.2217]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
