    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Time and Temperature Building Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time & Temperature Building<br/><br/>📍 477 Congress Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>As one of Portland's tallest buildings, the 14-story Time & Temperature Building at 477 Congress Street is an iconic part of the city skyline. Originally known as the Chapman Building, it was erected in 1924.<br/><br/>Today the stately edifice houses more than 100 businesses — law firms, nonprofits, tech companies, and retailers. Rising above it all is the famous giant rooftop sign that flashes the time and temperature, as well as frequently changing (and occasionally cryptic) eight-letter messages sponsored by the Law Office of Joe Bornstein, promoting holidays, charitable causes, and local events.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/477+Congress+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
