  <Placemark>
    <name>Tivoli Bays Unique Area Red Hook NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tivoli Bays Unique Area and Scenic Views<br/><br/>📍 Route 9G near CR 79, Red Hook, NY<br/><br/>Established as an estuarine resource area by the state in 1981, this area is the presumed site of Henry Hudson's 1609 visit when Red Hook was named. Nature trails and hiking are available, and just beyond the parking area is one of Dutchess County's most spectacular views of the Catskill Mountains.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Stop 14 of 33 on the Rhinebeck, Red Hook & Milan Scenic Tour (Tour 1).]]></description>
