  <Placemark>
    <name>Tracy Shore South Bristol ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tracy Shore<br/><br/>📍 Off S Road, ~20 ft from Route 129, South Bristol, ME (coordinate approximate — road-level geocode)<br/><br/>Trails past vernal pools, cascading streams, and moss/fern-draped cliffs to the Garber Overlook spur — sweeping views of Jones Cove and the Damariscotta River from a steep drop-off. Town of South Bristol-owned, co-managed with Coastal Rivers. ~1.6 mi, 65 ft gain.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Connects to Library Park via trail — pair the two<br/>- Garber Overlook has a real drop-off — mind footing, not for young kids unsupervised<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/tracy-shore/]]></description>
