  <Placemark>
    <name>Trapps Mountain Hamlet Historic District Gardiner NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Trapps Mountain Hamlet Historic District<br/><br/>📍 Mohonk Preserve, along US 44/55, Gardiner, NY<br/><br/>A settlement of Dutch-descended subsistence farmers, stone-cutters, and huckleberry-pickers thrived here from the late 1700s through the mid-20th century, reaching 40–50 families by the Civil War. Construction of US 44/55 in 1930 destroyed many of the old homesteads. The last resident living the old ways, Irving Van Leuven, died in 1956 in a house with no electricity or running water. The Eli Van Leuven Cabin (c. 1889) is the only building still standing; Mohonk Preserve has identified about 65 historic sites here — cellar holes, sawmills, bridge abutments, quarries, and cemeteries.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Mohonk Preserve offers a self-guided audio tour of the Trapps Mountain Hamlet Path.<br/>- The Van Leuven Cabin is restored and opened periodically for guided tours — check Preserve event listings.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.7333%2C%20-74.2142]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
