  <Placemark>
    <name>Troutbeck Country Inn Amenia NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Troutbeck Country Inn<br/><br/>📍 515 Leedsville Road, Amenia, NY 12501<br/><br/>Formerly a gathering place for the literati and liberals of the Twenties, this gentle, upscale 600-acre English estate hosts weddings, conferences and country inn visitors. A romantic European country house on the NY/CT border — site of the 1916 Amenia conference that unified the NAACP. Glorious grounds and gardens, a babbling brook, 42 guestrooms, tennis courts.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- www.troutbeck.com, 845/373-9681.<br/>- Stop 11 of 17 on the Washington & Amenia Scenic Tour (Tour 4), near Amenia Union on the NY/CT border.<br/>- Rating (4.5) is TripAdvisor's figure (109 reviews, #1 of 1 hotels in Amenia) — technically under the 4.7 purple threshold, but marked purple on the strength of the overall picture: Booking. rates it a perfect 10/10, and it carries real historic weight (site of the 1916 Amenia Conference that unified the NAACP).<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.854537,-73.5164852]]></description>
