  <Placemark>
    <name>Tunk Mountain Franklin ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Tunk Mountain<br/><br/>📍 Donnell Pond Public Reserved Land, off Route 182, Franklin, ME<br/><br/>A moderately challenging climb — 1.8 miles one-way, with a few steep, boulder-scramble sections and a short rung ladder near the top. A side trail around the 0.5-mile mark leads to "hidden ponds" (extending a full loop to about 5 miles). The rocky summit outcrop opens up south and southwest toward Catherine, Caribou, and Black Mountains, with lakes and ponds scattered below and Mount Desert Island visible in the distance.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Well-marked trailhead directly off Route 182.<br/>- Busy on weekends (9am–4pm) — visit outside that window for a quieter hike.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.6397%2C%20-68.0936]]></description>
