  <Placemark>
    <name>Two Bush Lighthouse Tenants Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Two Bush Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Two Bush Island, ~5.7 miles east of Tenants Harbor, ME<br/><br/>Congress appropriated $19,000 in 1894 to mark an important turn in Two Bush Channel; the light was activated November 10, 1897. In 1902, Keeper Norton's dog Smut alerted him to sailors drowning from the wrecked schooner Clara Bella, leading to a successful rescue.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Island closed to the public April–August for seabird nesting, covering the trip window; U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service owns the site.<br/>- Monhegan Boat Line runs lighthouse cruises from Port Clyde that pass by.]]></description>
