  <Placemark>
    <name>U.S. Route 1 Takeout Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[U.S. Route 1 Takeout<br/><br/>📍 254 Belfast Rd, Camden, ME<br/><br/>A small roadside takeout stand on Belfast Road (Route 1) heading north out of town. Lightly reviewed (a handful of reviews, 3.8/5 on Tripadvisor) but the reviews that exist are genuinely enthusiastic — "tasty food cooked fresh and served with a smile," fish and chips and fried clams singled out, lobster rolls and grilled shrimp called "fantastic." Reads as an under-the-radar find rather than a well-known local favorite; worth trying with reasonable expectations given the small review sample.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Easy to drive past — watch for signage on Belfast Road.<br/>- Note the corrected coordinates above — this was previously mis-pinned several miles away.<br/>- Good option if you're heading toward Lincolnville/Belfast and want a quick seafood stop en route.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-red</styleUrl>
