  <Placemark>
    <name>US Courthouse Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[US Courthouse (Edward T. Gignoux)<br/><br/>📍 156 Federal Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>The Edward T. Gignoux United States Courthouse at 156 Federal Street was the first federal courthouse in Maine when completed in 1911. It was designed by James Knox Tyler in Italian Renaissance Revival style.<br/><br/>Fun fact: Many of the historic buildings in Portland display two dates — the older is when the building was originally constructed, and the newer is when it was reconstructed after the Great Fire of 1866.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/156+Federal+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
