  <Placemark>
    <name>US Custom House Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[US Custom House<br/><br/>📍 312 Fore Street, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Constructed over five years from 1868 to 1872, the United States Custom House at 312 Fore Street is both historically and architecturally significant. Completed under the supervision of Alfred Mullett, supervising architect of the U.S. Treasury, the three-story building combines elements of Renaissance Revival and Second Empire styles.<br/><br/>In 1973, the building was designated as a City Landmark and listed on the National Register of Historic Places.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/US+Custom+House,+312+Fore+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
