  <Placemark>
    <name>Umbagog Lake State Park Errol NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Umbagog Lake State Park<br/><br/>📍 Southern end of Umbagog Lake, Errol, NH<br/><br/>Base campground has 27 sites with electric/water hookups and 2 cabins; beyond that, 33 remote campsites and 4 remote cabins are scattered around the lake, accessible only by boat. This is New Hampshire's largest concentration of nesting loons and osprey, with several nesting bald eagle pairs too — common loons are a threatened species in the state, so some remote sites close until July 20 to protect active nests.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Stay at least 400 feet from any loon nest or distressed-looking loon.<br/>- The remote boat-in sites are the real draw here if you want genuine North Woods solitude — book well ahead.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.7326%2C%20-71.0546]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-blue</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Lodging</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>hotel</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>blue</value></Data>
