    <Point>
      <coordinates>-71.0546,44.7326,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Umbagog National Wildlife Refuge Errol NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Umbagog National Wildlife Refuge<br/><br/>📍 Errol, NH (spanning the NH/Maine border)<br/><br/>A national wildlife refuge centered on Umbagog Lake, straddling the New Hampshire/Maine border. Best explored by boat through its marshes and waterways; popular for fishing, hunting, wildlife observation, and hiking, with frequent sightings of eagles, ospreys, and loons.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Combine with adjacent Umbagog Lake State Park, which has the more developed boat launch and camping access.<br/>- Bring binoculars — this is one of the better wildlife-watching spots in the whole North Country.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.7917%2C%20-71.0832]]></description>
