  <Placemark>
    <name>Van Cortlandt Manor Croton-on-Hudson, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Van Cortlandt Manor<br/><br/>📍 525 S Riverside Ave, Croton-on-Hudson, NY<br/><br/>A restored Colonial-era manor and farm complex overlooking the Hudson, operated by Historic Hudson Valley alongside sites like Sunnyside and Kykuit — costumed interpreters and period gardens bring 18th-century Hudson Valley life to life.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Seasonal events (notably the Great Jack O'Lantern Blaze in fall) draw large crowds — check hours before visiting.<br/>- Southernmost historical stop on this Taconic Byway list, near Kensico Dam and Cranberry Lake Preserve.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.191665,-73.876493]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
