  <Placemark>
    <name>Van Wagenen Stone House and Farm Complex Accord NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Van Wagenen Stone House and Farm Complex<br/><br/>📍 Town of Rochester, near Accord, NY<br/><br/>Also known by its Dutch name, Het Kilities Landt — a 1½-story linear stone dwelling dating to the early 18th century with five irregularly spaced dormers. The surviving complex includes a bank barn (c. 1880), several sheds and barns (1890s–1920s), and the remains of a smokehouse and dug well. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1999.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Private property — view from the road; groups this with the nearby Stilwill Westbrook and Stilwell stone houses for a short historic-houses driving loop.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.8056%2C%20-74.1822]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Historical</value></Data>
