    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Van Wyck Homestead Fishkill, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Van Wyck Homestead Museum<br/><br/>📍 504 Route 9, Fishkill, NY 12524<br/><br/>A 1732 Dutch stone farmhouse that anchored the massive Fishkill Supply Depot during the Revolutionary War, serving as headquarters and hospital for the Continental Army. Now a small museum run by the Fishkill Historical Society, furnished with period pieces and war-era artifacts.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Right off Route 9, a short hop from Fishkill Historic District — easy to combine into one stop.<br/>- Limited open hours (seasonal, volunteer-run) — check ahead rather than showing up unannounced.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.5325,-73.9016]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Historical</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>scroll</value></Data>
