  <Placemark>
    <name>Vassar College Poughkeepsie NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Vassar College<br/><br/>📍 124 Raymond Ave, Poughkeepsie, NY 12604<br/><br/>Founded by Poughkeepsie brewer Matthew Vassar in the 1850s. Belle Skinner Hall of Music, built 1932, was inspired by a medieval French village. Main Gate, built 1905, connects Frederick Thompson Memorial Library with Taylor Hall and the Frances Lehman Loeb Art Center. On the campus grounds are the Chapel, with Tiffany stained glass windows, and the Powerhouse Theatre.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Public parking available; visitors welcome to campus and public programs.<br/>- Maps and program information available from the Press and Information Office — call 845/437-7000.<br/>- Stop 19 of 33 on the Poughkeepsie & LaGrange Scenic Tour (Tour 5).]]></description>
