  <Placemark>
    <name>Vernooy Kill State Forest Kerhonkson, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Vernooy Kill State Forest<br/><br/>📍 Kerhonkson, NY<br/><br/>Formerly the Lundy Estate, conveyed to the State by the Open Space Institute and the Trust for Public Land. It's the largest parcel in an important corridor linking the Shawangunks to the Catskills, with habitat for upland wildlife including the protected eastern timber rattlesnake.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Access at Lundy Road and Rt 209 in Wawarsing<br/>- Hunting, fishing, trapping, mountain biking, horseback riding, snowmobiling, cross-country skiing, and camping all permitted<br/>- Native brook trout habitat along six miles of the Vernooy Kill<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=41.7910%2C%20-74.3400]]></description>
