  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Vesper Hill Children's Chapel Rockport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Vesper Hill Children's Chapel<br/><br/>📍 Rockport ME<br/><br/>A hidden open-air stone chapel on a hillside above Rockport, built in 1936 with carved wooden pews arranged in a semicircle facing an altar, a meadow that drops through birch trees to a panorama of Penobscot Bay and its islands. No roof. Flower gardens on three sides. One of the most quietly beautiful spots in Maine — known mostly to locals and largely absent from guidebooks.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Take Route 1 to Rockport, then Calderwood Lane to Vesper Hill Road — no signs.<br/>- The chapel is always open and free.<br/>- Late August wildflowers in the surrounding garden are at their peak.<br/>- Visit in the early morning or evening — the light on the bay is extraordinary.]]></description>
