  <Placemark>
    <name>Victoria Mansion Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Victoria Mansion<br/><br/>📍 Portland ME<br/><br/>The most lavishly decorated Victorian interior in America, built 1858–60 for a New Orleans hotelier. Original gas chandeliers, hand-painted trompe l'oeil ceilings, elaborate carved woodwork, and Herter Brothers furnishings — virtually all intact and original. The exterior understatement makes the interior a genuine shock.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Open May–Oct; allow 60–90 minutes for the guided tour.<br/>- The Christmas season opening (Dec) is worth timing your visit around — the house is decorated with 19th-century ornaments.<br/>- Easily combined with the Portland Museum of Art, two blocks away.]]></description>
