  <Placemark>
    <name>Viera on Main Chatham MA</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Overview<br/>Type: Seafood Restaurant  <br/>Best known for: Fresh shucked oysters, skilled steak preparation  <br/>Location context: Chatham, MA  <br/>Price level: $50–100 per person  <br/>Visit timing: Dinner hours are busier; brunch is also popular<br/><br/>Typical Customers  <br/>Demographics: Mix of locals and tourists  <br/>Group types: Couples, families, friends  <br/>Common occasions: Brunch, casual dinners, special occasions  <br/><br/>Vibe & Setting  <br/>Atmosphere: Casual, cozy with a nautical theme  <br/>Noise level: Moderate  <br/>Decor & setting: Indoor seating, well-decorated interior  <br/>Service style: Generally attentive and friendly<br/><br/>Recommended Dishes  <br/>Overall dish consensus  <br/>Critics agree that oysters and steak dishes are standout options. The swordfish, however, received mixed reviews, being described as bland by some.  <br/><br/>How “top dishes” are determined  <br/>Top dishes were chosen based on frequency in reviews, mentions in photos, and noted popularity on the Google Maps place page. <br/><br/>| Rank | Dish              | Why it stands out                                   | How often it’s mentioned      | Ideal for                     |<br/>|------|-------------------|----------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------|-------------------------------|<br/>| 1    | Fresh Shucked Oysters | Highly praised for freshness and flavor.          | Mentioned in many reviews     | Sharing at the table          |<br/>| 2    | Steak Frites      | Consistently praised for perfect cooking and flavor.  | Appears in numerous photos     | Hearty main                  |<br/>| 3    | Swordfish         | Mixed reviews; specifically noted as bland by some.| Repeatedly noted as featured   | Lighter option                |<br/><br/>Good alternates / backup choices  <br/>- Lobster Ravioli: Described as good but not exceptional.  <br/>- Steak Hash: Noted for being well-cooked and flavorful, especially during brunch.  <br/><br/>Highlights (non‑dish positives from reviews)  <br/>Food Quality: Many reviewers enjoyed the taste of the food and specific dishes, particularly during brunch.  <br/>Service: Generally characterized as friendly and attentive, enhancing the dining experience.  <br/><br/>Common Issues (from reviews)  <br/>Service Speed: Reports of slow service during busy hours were noted.  <br/>Dish Quality: Some dishes, like the swordfish, have been labeled as bland, indicating inconsistency in preparation.  <br/><br/>Practical Notes  <br/>Reservation / wait: Reservations recommended, especially during busy dinner hours.  <br/>Accessibility: Not mentioned  <br/>Parking / transit: Not mentioned  <br/>Best use case: Best for brunch with friends or casual dinners.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Viera+on+Main/@41.6816607,-69.96143,256m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m6!3m5!1s0x89fb14a1df4435d1:0x470de43a93b90b5d!8m2!3d41.6816658!4d-69.9601791!16s%2Fg%2F1thqhszl?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
