  <Placemark>
    <name>Village of Pawling NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Village of Pawling<br/><br/>📍 Pawling, NY 12564<br/><br/>Park here to view Victorian houses and old trees that line the way of village roads. The coming of the railroad in 1849 turned the rural Pawling Station into a busy manufacturing, dairy transport, and resort center. The Railroad Station of the Metro-North Harlem Line replaced the original that burned in 1989. Visible across the railroad tracks is Memorial Ave., with trees honoring WWII servicemen, and the Pawling Chronicle office, est. 1870 as "The Pawling Pioneer" by historian Phillip Smith.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Combine with the Dutcher House and Pawling Central Baptist Church (Eastlake style, ca. 1879) along Main St.<br/>- Stop 23 of 39 on the Union Vale, Beekman, Pawling & Dover Scenic Tour (Tour 6).]]></description>
