  <Placemark>
    <name>Village of Pleasant Valley NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Village of Pleasant Valley<br/><br/>📍 Pleasant Valley, NY 12569<br/><br/>Quakers and Presbyterians from New England and Long Island first settled here in the 1740s where the Wappinger Creek was easily forded. Late 18th-century maps refer to a "great bridge," an open bridge near the fording site, south of the present structure. A covered bridge built over the creek was replaced in 1841 and 1911. This area was the site of former textile mills.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Stop 19 of 26 on the Hyde Park, Clinton & Pleasant Valley Scenic Tour (Tour 3).<br/>- Coordinates are a general village-area point (postal code centroid), not a specific pin.]]></description>
