  <Placemark>
    <name>Walkway Over the Hudson Poughkeepsie, NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Walkway Over the Hudson<br/><br/>📍 Poughkeepsie, NY<br/><br/>The world's longest elevated pedestrian bridge — a 1.28-mile converted railroad trestle with panoramic 360-degree views of the Hudson Valley. Free to walk.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- East approach from Poughkeepsie has more parking; west from Highland for a different angle<br/>- Sunset from the midpoint is exceptional<br/>- The walk takes 30–40 minutes at a leisurely pace<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/Walkway+Over+the+Hudson+Poughkeepsie,+NY]]></description>
