  <Placemark>
    <name>Walpole Woods South Bristol ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Walpole Woods<br/><br/>📍 Route 129, east side, just north of the Walpole post office, South Bristol, ME<br/><br/>50-acre woodlot (1963 gift, town-owned since 1978, co-managed with Coastal Rivers since 2003) with a man-made Birkett Pond, an old rock-lined spring, and an impressive glacial erratic. ~1.0-1.1 mi out and back/loop.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.coastalrivers.org/trails/walpole-woods/]]></description>
