  <Placemark>
    <name>Warren Falls Warren VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Warren Falls<br/><br/>📍 Route 100, ~1.5 miles south of Warren, VT<br/><br/>Widely considered the blueprint for a great Vermont swimming hole — three tiers of waterfalls in a deep, steep-walled gorge, plunging into pools around 12 feet deep that turn a striking turquoise in the right light. A natural waterslide adds to the draw. Clearly marked parking lot on Route 100, roughly 3.5 miles south of Warren village (or reachable heading north from Granville).<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Cliff jumping is a well-known local pastime here, but the rocks stay slippery year-round and strong currents/vortexes above the falls are genuinely dangerous — exercise real caution, especially with kids.<br/>- Gets busy on summer weekends and during foliage season.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.1069%2C%20-72.8596]]></description>
