  <Placemark>
    <name>Waryas Park Poughkeepsie NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Waryas Park<br/><br/>📍 Poughkeepsie, NY 12601<br/><br/>This was formerly a neighborhood of 19th-century immigrant, blue-collar workers and shopkeepers, from England, Ireland and Germany. Waryas Park is named for the late Victor C. Waryas, a popular city mayor. Playground, picnic area, boat launching. Kaal Rock Park, under the Mid-Hudson Bridge, comes from the Dutch "Caul Rugh," the name of a high lookout point near the bridge where traders once watched for sloops. Riverside parking, trails, picnic benches.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Stop 5 of 33 on the Poughkeepsie & LaGrange Scenic Tour (Tour 5).]]></description>
