  <Placemark>
    <name>Wassaic State Forest Multiple Use Area Amenia NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Wassaic State Forest Multiple Use Area<br/><br/>📍 Ten Mile River Road parking area, off Route 22, Amenia (Wassaic), NY<br/><br/>Parallels the tour route, offering 488 acres for hunting, fishing, hiking, and camping. The nearby Wassaic hamlet at the northern edge of the Harlem Valley was a major industrial hamlet and center of the dairy industry — in 1853 Gail Borden opened the nation's first plant for condensing, pasteurizing and bottling milk here. Maxon Mills is built around a 19th-century hotel near the rail line; the red brick Borden Complex (now Pawling Corp.) sits near Worker Row Housing. The former Wassaic Developmental Center, a Depression-era state training center, is also nearby.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Coordinates are NYSDEC's own published parking-area location (Ten Mile River Road); a second parking area exists off Tower Hill Road.<br/>- Stop 12 of 17 on the Washington & Amenia Scenic Tour (Tour 4).]]></description>
