  <Placemark>
    <name>Waterbury Village Historic District Waterbury VT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Waterbury Village Historic District<br/><br/>📍 Downtown Waterbury, VT<br/><br/>Waterbury's historic downtown, devastated by the catastrophic November 1927 flood — floodwaters reached the second story of some buildings, and inscriptions on a few structures still mark where the water rose. The 1938 Waterbury Dam (which created what's now Little River State Park's reservoir) was built partly in response, to control future flooding downstream. Today a walkable, lively Main Street with shops and restaurants.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A good base for exploring the wider Green Mountain Byway — Ben & Jerry's factory and the Cold Hollow Cider Mill are both nearby, just outside the historic core.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.3377%2C%20-72.7569]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
