    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Weeks State Park Lancaster NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Weeks State Park<br/><br/>📍 Mount Prospect, Lancaster, NH<br/><br/>The former 420-acre Mount Prospect estate of John Wingate Weeks — U.S. Congressman (1905–13), Senator (1913–19), and Secretary of War under Harding and Coolidge, best remembered for authoring the Weeks Act of 1911, which let the federal government purchase land to create national forests (including the White Mountain National Forest). The 87-foot Tudor Revival stone tower near the summit lodge, built in 1912 as a water tank, was converted into New Hampshire's only masonry fire tower in 1941 and remains part of the state's fire-watch system. Weeks' children donated the estate to New Hampshire in 1941. The summit was listed on the National Register in 1985, the whole park in 2023.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Climb the tower for wide views over the North Country and Presidential Range.<br/>- Good combination with a Lancaster town stop given the short distance.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.4494%2C%20-71.5786]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Park</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>landmark</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>green</value></Data>
    </ExtendedData>
    <Point>
      <coordinates>-71.5786,44.4494,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Wellfleet Drive-In Theater Wellfleet MA</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Wellfleet Drive-In Theater<br/><br/>📍 Wellfleet MA<br/><br/>The last remaining drive-in theater on Cape Cod, operating since 1957, with a flea market by day and double features by night. One of only a handful of drive-ins left in New England. The screen faces a meadow at the edge of the National Seashore — arriving early means a deer may walk through the frame before the movie starts. An irreplaceable summer ritual that won't exist forever.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Gates open at 7pm; movies start at dusk (around 8:15pm in August).<br/>- Tune to FM radio for the sound — bring a portable if you plan to sit outside the car.<br/>- The snack bar serves classic drive-in food; the onion rings are famous locally.<br/>- Cash only at the gate; check their website for the week's schedule.<br/>- Arrive 30–45 minutes early on weekends — the lot fills completely.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Entertainment</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>ticket</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>green</value></Data>
