      <coordinates>-70.0301,41.9148,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>West Point West Point NY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[West Point<br/><br/>📍 West Point NY<br/><br/>The United States Military Academy occupies one of the most strategically and scenically dramatic sites on the Hudson — a granite promontory where the river makes a sharp bend, commanding the valley in both directions. Washington fortified this position with a great chain stretched across the river to block British ships. The Gothic stone buildings, Trophy Point, the cemetery (Custer, Westmoreland, Patton's father), and the parade ground are all open to the public.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- The visitor center at Pershing Gate is the starting point — free maps of open areas.<br/>- Guided bus tours depart from the visitor center and access areas not open to self-guided visitors.<br/>- Trophy Point overlooks the Hudson bend and displays links from the Revolutionary War chain.<br/>- The cemetery contains the graves of more than 8,000 graduates, including Winfield Scott, George Custer, and Gar Davidson.<br/>- West Point is 45 minutes south of Beacon — combine with Dia:Beacon for a full Hudson Valley day.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
