    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>West Rattlesnake Mountain (Old Bridle Path) Holderness NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[West Rattlesnake Mountain (Old Bridle Path)<br/><br/>📍 Holderness NH<br/><br/>Moderate 3.8-mile out-and-back with one of the best reward-to-effort ratios in the Lakes Region — sweeping summit views over Squam Lake.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Moderate difficulty, big payoff.<br/>- Popular trail — go early on weekends to beat crowds.<br/>- Pet friendly: Generally dog-friendly (on-leash recommended; be mindful of other hikers).<br/>- Parking: Small lot at the trailhead can fill up fast; have a backup plan if it’s full.<br/>- Footing: Expect rocks/roots; wear grippy shoes—especially if wet.<br/>- Weather: Summit is exposed; bring a light layer/wind protection.<br/>- Sun/bugs: Limited shade near the top; use sunscreen and bug protection in warm months.<br/>- What to bring: Water, snacks, and a small first-aid kit.<br/>- Dogs: Bring water for your dog; watch paws on sharp rock and keep away from cliff edges.]]></description>
