  <Placemark>
    <name>Whaleback Ledge Lighthouse Kittery ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Whaleback Ledge Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Entrance to Portsmouth Harbor, Kittery, ME (Maine–New Hampshire border)<br/><br/>The original 1829 lighthouse was so poorly built by corner-cutting contractors that keepers feared it would collapse in storms — remarkably, it stood for over 40 years anyway. It was finally replaced in 1872 by the current granite tower, modeled after England's famous Eddystone Lighthouse.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Tower closed to visitors; best seen by boat via Isles of Shoals Steamship Company or Portsmouth Harbor Cruises, or distantly from Fort Foster Park in Kittery.<br/>- Owned and managed by the American Lighthouse Foundation.]]></description>
