  <Placemark>
    <name>Whaleback Shell Midden State Historic Site Damariscotta ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-07T15:30:00<br/><br/>Whaleback Shell Midden State Historic Site<br/><br/>📍 Damariscotta, ME<br/><br/>An 11-acre park with a half-mile loop trail through the remains of a 2,200-year-old Native American oyster shell heap—a genuinely obscure archaeological site with river views that almost no coastal tourists visit. A unique window into pre-European coastal history.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Half-mile easy loop trail<br/>- 2,200-year-old shell heap<br/>- River views along the trail<br/>- Virtually no tourist crowds<br/>- Educational historical site<br/>- Quiet, contemplative setting<br/>- Connects directly to Round Top Farm via a 0.3-mile universally accessible trail — easy to combine both stops in one visit]]></description>
