  <Placemark>
    <name>Wharf Street Portland ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Wharf Street<br/><br/>📍 Wharf Street, between Union & Moulton Streets, Portland, ME<br/><br/>Less than a block from 3 Dollar Dewey's, Wharf Street is one of Portland's most atmospheric cobblestone streets. Before the mid-1800s, the waters of Casco Bay used to lap against the buildings along Wharf Street — until a substantial portion of Portland's waterfront was filled in to make way for rail transit and other economic development.<br/><br/>Today, Wharf Street bustles during the day with unique shops and restaurants, and at night becomes a mecca for fun and entertainment.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Wharf+St,+Portland,+ME]]></description>
