  <Placemark>
    <name>Whitlocks Mill Lighthouse Calais ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Whitlocks Mill Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 St. Croix River, ~2.5 miles south of Calais, ME<br/><br/>Maine's northernmost and last-built lighthouse. It started as a red lantern hung on a tree in 1892 before the current 25-foot cylindrical brick tower was completed in 1909, guiding timber traffic to the port of Calais. Its light changed from red to green in 1931.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Closed to the public; the keeper's house is a private residence.<br/>- Best viewed from a roadside picnic area on Route 1, about 2.5 miles south of Calais.<br/>- Very far north — pairs with a Calais/St. Croix Island stop, not a casual Bar Harbor detour.]]></description>
