  <Placemark>
    <name>Whittier Bridge Ossipee NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Whittier Bridge<br/><br/>📍 West Ossipee, NH (over the Bearcamp River)<br/><br/>Known locally as the Great Bridge, this crossing dates back to at least 1792, with the current 137-foot Paddleford truss span built in 1870 — one of New Hampshire's few surviving 19th-century covered bridges. Closed to vehicle traffic in 1989, removed for restoration in 2008, and placed back on its abutments in late 2022. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1984.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- A short detour off the main byway loop toward West Ossipee, at the junction of the historic east-west and north-south routes through the region.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.8214%2C%20-71.2124]]></description>
