  <Placemark>
    <name>Wild Gardens of Acadia Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Wild Gardens of Acadia<br/><br/>📍 Sieur de Monts, Acadia National Park ME<br/><br/>A small, easy-to-miss botanical garden at Sieur de Monts, just south of Bar Harbor, featuring over 300 native Acadia plant species labeled and organized into nine habitat displays (bog, woodland, meadow, etc.). Flat, quiet, and typically uncrowded even in peak season.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Pair with the adjacent Abbe Museum (Native American history) and Sieur de Monts Spring — all three sit in the same small area.<br/>- Completely flat and easy — a good low-key stop to break up a driving day.<br/>- Free admission; a nice option if you want a short, calm walk without a hike.]]></description>
