  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>William M Nash House Cherryfield ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[William M. Nash House<br/><br/>📍 River Road, Cherryfield, ME<br/><br/>A house that's been remodeled twice over: starting as a Cape Cod cottage, rebuilt into a Greek Revival "temple" house, then thoroughly redone again in 1888 for William M. Nash into the elaborate High Victorian/Second Empire structure seen today, designed by local architect William A. Allen. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1983 as a contributing property to the Cherryfield Historic District.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Part of a walkable cluster of historic homes with the Archibald-Adams and David W. Campbell houses.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=44.6006%2C%20-67.9283]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
