      <coordinates>-67.9283,44.6006,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>William Rossiter House Claremont NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[William Rossiter House<br/><br/>📍 11 Mulberry Street, Claremont, NH<br/><br/>Built in 1813 by Austin Tyler, then dramatically expanded and remade in the Greek Revival style around 1830-50 by William Rossiter — an executive of the city's Sullivan Woolen Mills, four-term city selectman, and twice-elected state legislator. The five-bay facade's massive two-story temple portico, with fluted Ionic columns rising to a full entablature, is one of the finest examples of the style in the region. Listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1979.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Private property — a drive/walk-past landmark rather than a stop with public access.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.3762%2C%20-72.3437]]></description>
