  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Windjammer Cruises Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Windjammer Cruises<br/><br/>📍 Bayview Landing, Camden Harbor, ME<br/><br/>Camden Harbor is home to a fleet of historic windjammer schooners offering everything from 2-3 hour day sails to multi-night cruises around Penobscot Bay — considered one of the best cruising bays in the world, with uninhabited islands, wildlife, and coastal mountain views. Day sails typically depart Bayview Landing and pass right by Curtis Island Light on the way out. Reviews consistently call it one of the best things to do in Camden, with crews that welcome passengers helping raise sails or take a turn at the wheel. One of the classic Camden experiences — the Windjammer Festival takes over the harbor every Labor Day weekend.<br/><br/>Must consider<br/>- Schooner Olad — a fully restored 1927 classic yacht, offers daily day sails plus custom half/full-day charters.<br/>- Schooner Appledore II — an 86-foot traditional windjammer running day sails, sunset sails, and snorkel sails.<br/>- Mary Day and other multi-night windjammers — for a longer, live-aboard Penobscot Bay experience.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Decide time commitment first: a 2-3 hour afternoon/sunset sail vs. a multi-night live-aboard cruise are very different trips — book accordingly.<br/>- Book ahead in peak season, especially for anything longer than a day sail.<br/>- Bring a water-resistant jacket — it's windy and cool on the water even on warm days.<br/>- A relaxed, non-strenuous way to see the coastline if you want a break from hiking.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Attraction</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>sailboat</value></Data>
