  <Placemark>
    <name>Winnipesaukee Scenic Railroad Meredith NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Winnipesaukee Scenic Railroad<br/><br/>📍 Meredith, NH (also boards at Weirs Beach)<br/><br/>Runs on tracks laid down by the Boston, Concord & Montreal Railroad, which reached Weirs Beach around December 1848 and Meredith by March 1849. Opened as a tourist scenic railroad in 1992; a 2-hour round trip departs Meredith along the lake's western shore, with a shorter 1-hour excursion from a ticket booth on the Weirs Beach boardwalk. Recently acquired by the Granite State Scenic Railroad.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Buy tickets ahead in peak summer season — trains can sell out.<br/>- The Meredith departure gives the longer, more scenic ride; Weirs Beach is the shorter, more convenient option if staying near the boardwalk.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.6511%2C%20-71.4998]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
