  <Placemark>
    <name>Winona's Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Winona's<br/><br/>📍 31 Elm St, Camden, ME<br/><br/>A tiny, 20-seat gem run by owners Hannah Adams (wine) and chef Devin Dearden (kitchen) — a bohemian-modern slow-food experience built around a tight, six-dish micro-seasonal menu that changes every two weeks. Earned 4 stars from the Portland Press Herald for "marvelous micro-seasonal food." Rated 4.5 on Tripadvisor. Very close to Mosaic on the same street — easy to conflate, but a distinct, much smaller, more ambitious kitchen.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- Whatever's currently on the six-dish seasonal menu — past standouts include halibut crudo with cherry-lime ponzu, sumac-cured salmon, and cod en papillote<br/>- The sea-salted fudge — the one fixed dessert on an otherwise fully rotating menu<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Only 20 seats — reserve well ahead, this is not a walk-in spot.<br/>- The menu is genuinely different every two weeks, so don't go in expecting a specific dish to still be there.<br/>- Trust the wine pairings — Hannah's pairings are specifically called out as a highlight.<br/>- Reservation deadline noted at 2026-06-30 in this note's records — confirm current booking status.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Winona's/@44.2090611,-69.0674547,246m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m13!1m5!2m4!1sRestaurants!5m1!4e9!6e5!3m6!1s0x4cadd70079fe6581:0xa69955b2425ef962!8m2!3d44.2091229!4d-69.065945!15sCgtSZXN0YXVyYW50c1oNIgtyZXN0YXVyYW50c5IBE2FtZXJpY2FuX3Jlc3RhdXJhbnSaAURDaTlEUVVsUlFVTnZaRU5vZEhsalJqbHZUMnRXZGs1RVFrSlZiSEJtV1ROR1lVeFdSbWhqVldNMFVtcGtlbVF3UlJBQuABAPoBBAgzEEs!16s%2Fg%2F11lmkkcw6v?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYwOS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
