  <Placemark>
    <name>Winter Harbor Lighthouse Winter Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Winter Harbor Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Mark Island, Winter Harbor, ME<br/><br/>Built in 1857, this 19-foot white brick tower with a fifth-order Fresnel lens served for 76 years (1857–1933) under just nine keepers. After decommissioning it passed through several private owners — including writer Bernice Richmond, who chronicled island life in two books — before current owner William Holden restored it and reinstalled a private beacon in 1996.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Privately owned, closed to the public.<br/>- Distant views from Schoodic Road in Acadia National Park (Schoodic section); closer views by boat tour or scenic flight from Bar Harbor.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
