  <Placemark>
    <name>Wonderland Trail Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Wonderland Trail<br/><br/>📍 Route 102A, Tremont ME (Acadia National Park, quiet side)<br/><br/>An easy, flat 1.3-mile out-and-back coastal trail on the quiet side of the island near Bass Harbor/Tremont — family-friendly, good tidepooling and birding at Bennett Cove, and consistently less crowded than the Park Loop Road hotspots.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Completely flat, no exposure — a good easy option.<br/>- Bring bug spray; mosquitoes are a common complaint in warmer months.<br/>- Pairs naturally with Ship Harbor Nature Trail, about half a mile down the same road.]]></description>
