  <Placemark>
    <name>Wood Island Lighthouse Biddeford Pool ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Wood Island Lighthouse<br/><br/>📍 Wood Island, ~2 miles east of the Saco River mouth, near Biddeford Pool, ME<br/><br/>The original wooden octagonal tower was activated in 1808; two more towers followed due to poor construction before the current stone tower was completed in 1854. Keeper Thomas Orcutt's dog Sailor (1886–1905) became locally famous for ringing the fog bell by pulling its cord with his teeth to salute passing vessels.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Seasonal tours through Friends of Wood Island Lighthouse; grounds, dwelling, and tower open seasonally.<br/>- Also viewable from an Audubon trail out of Biddeford Pool, though water access gives the better view.]]></description>
