  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Woodlawn - The Black House Ellsworth ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Woodlawn (The Black House)<br/><br/>📍 19 Black House Dr, Ellsworth, ME<br/><br/>A 180-acre estate built 1824–27 for lumber merchant baron John Black, in a restrained Neo-Federal style with rare original furnishings still intact inside. The grounds include gardens and walking trails; the house itself is a ticketed, guided-tour museum.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Grounds open daily, dawn to dusk, year-round, and free — walking the trails and park costs nothing.<br/>- The seasonal house museum runs June–September, Thursday–Saturday, 9am–3pm, with guided tours on the hour (10am–3pm); there's a fee to tour the house or play croquet on the lawn.<br/>- Right on the way between Bar Harbor/Acadia and points west — an easy add-on stop rather than a special trip.<br/>- Audio tours are also available if guided-tour timing doesn't line up.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.woodlawnellsworth.org/]]></description>
