  <Placemark>
    <name>Wright Museum of WWII Wolfeboro NH</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Wright Museum of World War II<br/><br/>📍 Wolfeboro, NH<br/><br/>Founded in 1994 by David Wright, this nonprofit is America's premier museum on the WWII home front — rationing, victory gardens, scrap drives, factory work — alongside more than 20 military vehicles and thousands of battlefield artifacts, totaling over 14,000 items. Nearly 300,000 visitors have come through in its first two decades.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Budget 1.5–2 hours; the vehicle collection alone is a highlight for history and military buffs.<br/>- Combine with the Wolfeboro Historical Society and Abenaki Tower for a full Wolfeboro-area stop.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=43.5892%2C%20-71.2052]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-green</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
