    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Young’s Lobster Pound Belfast ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Young’s Lobster Pound<br/><br/>Young’s Lobster Pound is a long-running Belfast seafood institution that began in the 1930s as an extension of the Young family’s fishing business. Maine Memory Network notes that Bud and Belle Young sold steamed lobsters and clams from a small stand with outdoor picnic tables, establishing the casual harborside style the place is still known for today.[cite:64]<br/><br/>The business is now described as a four-generation family-run lobster source and restaurant, and it also ships live lobsters beyond Maine. That combination of working waterfront roots, family continuity, and fresh local catch helps explain why it remains one of the town’s signature food stops.[cite:63][cite:65]]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-red</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Restaurant</value></Data>
