  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Zoot Coffee Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Zoot Coffee<br/><br/>📍 5 Elm St, Camden, ME<br/><br/>A cafe-roaster right downtown, roasting its own beans and preparing coffee and tea in-house. Reviewers describe a calm, welcoming atmosphere with genuine community spirit, and the cafe stands out for its dietary flexibility — almond, soy, and oat milk options plus several vegan baked treats, alongside solid gluten-free choices. Rated 4.5 on Google — Restaurant Guru shows a higher 4.8 and Tripadvisor a lower 4.2, so Google's figure is used here as the more broadly representative middle ground.<br/><br/>Must Order<br/>- House-roasted coffee — the core draw<br/>- Ask about current gluten-free/vegan baked options, which rotate<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Good option if the group has mixed dietary needs — genuinely broader accommodation than a typical coffee shop.<br/>- Some reviewers note prices run a bit high for coffee — go in expecting a slight premium for the quality.<br/>- Laid-back atmosphere suited to lingering, not just a quick grab-and-go.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
