  <Placemark>
    <name>✅ Salt Wharf Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-09T18:30:00<br/><br/>Salt Wharf is a dining establishment known for its seafood, particularly dishes like mussels and lobster tortellini. It caters to a variety of customers, including couples celebrating special occasions and groups looking for a memorable dining experience. The overall vibe is a mix of casual and upscale, with a lively atmosphere, especially during happy hour.<br/><br/>Customers consistently praise the delicious food, stunning location, and excellent cocktails. Additionally, the service, although sometimes noted as feeling intimidated, is generally described as decent.<br/><br/>Some common downsides include the need for reservations due to limited space, and the potential for close seating with other parties which may affect privacy during dining.<br/><br/>Reservation confirmation (Aug 9)<br/><br/>Salt Wharf Camden Maine: Best Dishes for Tonight<br/><br/>Most Highly Rated Overall<br/><br/>The dishes that come up most often in current menu listings and diner praise are the Maine oysters, deviled eggs with caviar, seared scallops, lobster dishes, and several steak preparations. Recent review and menu evidence also points to the smash burger as a strong casual option on the rooftop side. [web:77][web:76][web:78][web:84][web:95]<br/><br/>Best Bets If You Eat Meat Sometimes<br/><br/>Because you do enjoy meat periodically, the recommendations should include both seafood and a couple of standout meat options.<br/><br/>- Fresh Maine oysters with black-lime mignonette; one of the most consistently praised and signature-feeling starters. [web:77][web:76]<br/>- Deviled eggs with caviar; a popular starter that shows up repeatedly in review mentions. [web:76][web:78]<br/>- Seared scallops; among the most commonly highlighted seafood mains in recent reviews. [web:77][web:76]<br/>- Maine-lobster fra diavolo or other lobster pasta dishes; a strong richer entrée choice if you want something indulgent. [web:77][web:86]<br/>- Smash burger; specifically praised in recent Yelp review text and a good fit if you are in the mood for something more casual and satisfying. [web:76][web:86]<br/>- Steak frites or ribeye-style steak dishes; multiple recent mentions describe the steak as very good, and one post specifically called out “2 fantastic steaks.” [web:84][web:95][web:75]<br/><br/>What I Would Order<br/><br/>If you want the most “Salt Wharf” dinner, start with oysters and deviled eggs, then choose scallops or lobster pasta for the main course. [web:77][web:76]<br/><br/>If you want to lean into your periodic meat preference, the best alternate path is oysters first, then either the smash burger if you want relaxed rooftop-bar energy, or the steak if you want a fuller dinner in the dining-room style. [web:76][web:79][web:84][web:95]<br/><br/>Best Choice by Mood<br/><br/>- For a classic Maine waterfront meal: oysters plus scallops. [web:77][web:76]<br/>- For something richer and more memorable: oysters plus lobster pasta. [web:77][web:86]<br/>- For your stated tastes specifically: oysters plus steak, or oysters plus the smash burger. [web:76][web:84][web:95]<br/>- For the most casual good-time order: burger, fries, and a drink on the rooftop. [web:79][web:86]<br/><br/>Practical Note<br/><br/>Salt Wharf’s dining room is listed as open daily from 4:00 PM to 8:00 PM, while the rooftop is listed as open later and is described as the easiergoing side with lobster rolls, cold beer, and casual fare. That makes the rooftop the more natural place to aim for the burger, while the dining room is the better fit for scallops, halibut, lobster pasta, or steak. [web:79][web:77]<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Salt+Wharf/@44.2092873,-69.0624444,181m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m6!3m5!1s0x4cadd75917dd6427:0xa1440bf2564023cb!8m2!3d44.2091477!4d-69.060989!16s%2Fg%2F11rv9bpsgv?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
