  <Placemark>
    <name>✅❌ Earls Kitchen + Bar Boston MA</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-02T18:30:00<br/><br/>Here is a detailed summary of your reservation, followed by a scannable overview of the restaurant’s details formatted perfectly for you to copy and paste directly into your Markdown notes.<br/><br/>---<br/><br/>📅 Reservation Summary<br/><br/>- Guest Name: Tom Rubel<br/>    <br/>- Restaurant: Earls Kitchen + Bar - Boston - Prudential Center<br/>    <br/>- Party Size: 2 people<br/>    <br/>- Date: Sunday, August 2, 2026<br/>    <br/>- Time: 6:30 PM EDT<br/>    <br/>- Confirmation Number: 1007703<br/>    <br/>- Important Policy: There is a 15-minute grace period. If you are running later than 15 minutes past 6:30 PM, you must call the restaurant directly.<br/>    <br/><br/>---<br/><br/>🍽️ Restaurant Information<br/><br/>_Copy and paste the section below straight into your Markdown files:_<br/><br/>Markdown<br/><br/>```<br/>Earls Kitchen + Bar (Boston Prudential Center)<br/><br/> Address: 800 Boylston St, Boston, MA 02199<br/> Phone: (857) 957-0949<br/> Location Notes: Located right in the Prudential Center in Back Bay.<br/> Ambiance & Dining Areas: Features both indoor dining and a highly popular outdoor patio space (seating depends on your specific booking selection).<br/> Key Policies:  Strict 15-minute grace period for reservations.<br/>    * Due to high demand for large party reservations, seating smaller parties at neighboring tables cannot always be guaranteed.<br/>```<br/><br/>Earls Kitchen + Bar at the Prudential Center in Boston offers a highly rated (4.7 stars), polished casual dining experience that stands out for its energetic vibe and massive, all-year-round rooftop patio in the heart of the Back Bay.<br/><br/>Here is a thorough breakdown of the dining experience, what patrons love, areas that fall short, and the absolute must-order items on the menu.<br/><br/>---<br/><br/>🏛️ Overall Vibe & Atmosphere<br/><br/>Earls expertly straddles the line between a chic, upscale lounge and a friendly neighborhood hangout. The layout features a lively lower-level bar, a 300-seat open-kitchen main dining room, and an expansive rooftop terrace.<br/><br/>- The Vibe: Energetic, modern, and fashionable. It transitions seamlessly from a corporate lunch spot to a high-energy evening destination for after-work drinks, dates, or lively group dinners.<br/>    <br/>- The Rooftop: This is arguably the restaurant's crown jewel. During the warmer months, it’s a premier sunny destination overlooking Back Bay; in the winter, it transforms into a cozy, fully enclosed "Winter Wonder Lounge."<br/>    <br/><br/>---<br/><br/>👍 The Likes (What Patrons Rave About)<br/><br/>- Attentive & Energetic Service: Reviewers consistently highlight the staff for going above and beyond. The hospitality is crisp, quick, and impeccably friendly.<br/>    <br/>- Extreme Menu Diversity: The "scratch kitchen" global menu means a single table can comfortably order high-quality sushi rolls, street tacos, local New England seafood, and prime rib without anyone compromising.<br/>    <br/>- The Cocktail Program: Handcrafted by world-renowned mixologists, the drinks feature freshly squeezed juices and small-batch house syrups.<br/>    <br/>- The Happiest Hour: Their daily happy hour (running 3:00 PM – 6:00 PM and 9:00 PM – close) offers phenomenal value with major discounts on popular shared plates like truffle fries and wings.<br/>    <br/><br/>👎 The Dislikes (What to Look Out For)<br/><br/>- Noise Levels: Because the space is large, bustling, and features upbeat music, the dining room and lounge can get incredibly loud during peak weekend hours. It is not the best spot for a quiet, intimate whisper-conversation.<br/>    <br/>- Upselling and Over-Ordering: Some patrons note that the service strategy can lean heavily into encouraging multiple small plates per person (tapas-style recommendations). However, the portions are actually quite American and hearty, which can easily lead to accidentally over-ordering.<br/>    <br/>- Occasional Execution Slips on Seafood: While the raw bar and sushi are generally praised, a few reviewers have noted that delicate hot fish entrees (like the halibut) can occasionally lean slightly overcooked during chaotic peak hours.<br/>    <br/><br/>---<br/><br/>🍽️ The Best Items on the Menu<br/><br/>If you are looking for the absolute standouts that define the Earls experience, prioritize these scratch-made favorites:<br/><br/>🍣 Sushi & Shareables<br/><br/>- Spicy Tuna Sushi Press: Exceptionally popular. It features layers of spicy soy-marinated ahi tuna, avocado, and pickled ginger pressed onto sushi rice, finished with sriracha mayo.<br/>    <br/>- Dynamite Roll: A brilliant, fresh flavor profile combining tempura prawn, tangy mango, avocado, sriracha mayo, and a sweet maple unagi glaze.<br/>    <br/>- Korean Hot Wings: Crispy, high-quality wings tossed in a spicy red pepper glaze, topped with crispy onions and sesame seeds. (An absolute steal if ordered during Happy Hour).<br/>    <br/><br/>🥗 Salads & Bowls<br/><br/>- Santa Fe Chicken Salad: This is a fan-favorite meal salad. It features perfectly blackened chicken breast, rich feta cheese, avocado, black beans, sweet dates, and a signature peanut lime vinaigrette that brings it all together beautifully.<br/>    <br/><br/>🥩 Mains & Specialties<br/><br/>- Steak + Sushi: A brilliant signature pairing that allows you to experience the best of both worlds—perfectly seared steak sliced alongside a premium sushi roll.<br/>    <br/>    Tip: If you go on Steak Wednesday, they offer $5 off all steak cuts!<br/>    <br/>- Blackened Swordfish Tacos: Served on flour tortillas with melted white cheddar, a smoky roasted jalapeño crema, pico de gallo, and fresh cilantro.<br/>    <br/><br/>🍹 Can't-Miss Cocktails<br/><br/>- The Paper Plane: A flawless, modern classic made with Buffalo Trace bourbon, Amaro Montenegro, Aperol, and fresh lemon juice.<br/>    <br/>- Frozen Pink Lemonade: A playful, highly refreshing house specialty perfect for lounging on the rooftop terrace.<br/>    <br/><br/>---<br/><br/>Are you looking to book a table for a specific occasion, or are you hoping to check out their weekend brunch offerings?<br/><br/>Cancellation<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Earls+Kitchen+%2B+Bar/@42.3472291,-71.0844681,812m/data=!3m3!1e3!4b1!5s0x89e37a0dd77182cf:0x7f4bdaf4bd326028!4m6!3m5!1s0x89e37a103d153b47:0xd9e2a9e2c1c46ca5!8m2!3d42.3472252!4d-71.0818932!16s%2Fg%2F11f06k55nq?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYwOS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
