  <Placemark>
    <name>✅❗️ Ports of Italy, Rockport Rockport ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-12T18:30:00<br/><br/>Ports of Italy, Rockport: Best Dishes to Order<br/><br/>What This Restaurant Does Best<br/><br/>Ports of Italy is a traditional Italian restaurant centered on pasta, ravioli, bread, focaccia, and desserts made in-house daily. Its food is more authentic Italian than Italian-American: do not expect chicken Parmesan or spaghetti and meatballs; instead, expect fresh pasta, seafood, veal, porchetta, and seasonal specials. [web:109][web:107]<br/><br/>Most Highly Regarded Dishes<br/><br/>- Lobster ravioli; the restaurant’s most frequently cited seasonal signature dish, with Maine lobster and local ricotta in a light prosecco-aurora sauce. [web:102][web:107][web:110]<br/>- Housemade tagliatelle or pasta with classic Bolognese; a strong choice when you want a true meat-centered pasta rather than seafood. [web:105][web:110][web:112]<br/>- Branzino; whole fish imported from Italy, roasted with rosemary and garlic, then deboned tableside. This is one of the restaurant’s signature experiences. [web:109][web:114]<br/>- Grilled octopus; specifically praised by diners and a good starter if you want something savory and more distinctive than a standard salad. [web:103][web:105]<br/>- Caprese in a fried Parmigiano basket; an especially popular antipasto presentation. [web:105][web:107]<br/>- Squid-ink spaghetti or Chitarrucci Neri Frutti di Mare; good choices if you want a more seafood-forward pasta. [web:105]<br/>- Gnocchi; repeatedly recommended by diners, especially when you want a comforting pasta-forward entrée. [web:102]<br/><br/>Best Choices for Your Meat Preferences<br/><br/>Because you enjoy meat periodically, the Bolognese, porchetta, and veal dishes should be added to the shortlist rather than filtered out.<br/><br/>- Pasta with classic Bolognese; likely the best first choice if you want a hearty but balanced meat entrée. [web:110][web:112]<br/>- Porchetta; the restaurant calls its roasted suckling pig an in-house specialty. Choose it if it is available and you want an authentically Italian meat dish rather than a steak. [web:109][web:110][web:114]<br/>- Veal scallopini or veal ravioli; both have appeared in diner praise and catering/menu descriptions, making them good options if they are on the dinner menu or offered as specials. [web:102][web:105][web:110]<br/>- Braised beef or another rotating meat special; specials change regularly and are often where the kitchen gets more creative with seasonal ingredients. [web:107][web:116]<br/><br/>Best Order by Mood<br/><br/>- For the classic first visit: Caprese in the Parmigiano basket, then lobster ravioli. [web:105][web:107]<br/>- For your periodic meat craving: grilled octopus to start, followed by Bolognese, porchetta, or veal if available. [web:103][web:109][web:110]<br/>- For a seafood-forward Italian dinner: grilled octopus, followed by branzino or squid-ink seafood pasta. [web:103][web:109][web:105]<br/>- For a shared meal: Caprese, octopus, lobster ravioli, and one meat-centered pasta or entrée. This gives you both the restaurant’s Maine-seafood strength and its traditional Italian side. [web:102][web:103][web:109]<br/><br/>What Not to Order It For<br/><br/>Ports of Italy is not the right destination specifically for hamburgers or a conventional American steak. Go instead for handmade pasta, Italian seafood, Bolognese, porchetta, veal, and the seasonal specials; those are the choices most aligned with its stated cooking style and diner praise. [web:107][web:109][web:110]<br/><br/>Practical Note<br/><br/>Ports of Italy lists daily lunch and dinner service, with current stated hours of 11:30 AM to 9:00 PM. The restaurant is at 141 Commercial Street in Rockport, and its menu changes enough that asking about the nightly special is worthwhile—particularly if you are hoping for a special meat or seasonal lobster dish. [web:109][web:107][web:116]<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Ports+of+Italy,+Rockport/@44.1906546,-69.0824852,784m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m14!1m7!3m6!1s0x4cadd7f58c73a11d:0xd0a50cc550173421!2sPorts+of+Italy,+Rockport!8m2!3d44.1906546!4d-69.0799103!16s%2Fg%2F11hpbwk0qb!3m5!1s0x4cadd7f58c73a11d:0xd0a50cc550173421!8m2!3d44.1906546!4d-69.0799103!16s%2Fg%2F11hpbwk0qb?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxNi4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
