  <Placemark>
    <name>✅❗️ The Lenox Hotel Boston MA</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-02T18:00:00<br/><br/>The Lenox Hotel, Boston – Review<br/>Overall: Charming, historic boutique hotel in an unbeatable Back Bay location, with standout service and a cozy, classic feel.[tripadvisor +2]<br/>---<br/>Fast Facts<br/>•	Location: 61 Exeter St, at Boylston, in Boston’s Back Bay, steps from Newbury Street and Copley Square; very close to the Boston Marathon finish line.[yelp +1]<br/>•	Style: Historic 1900 landmark building with classic architecture, traditional decor, and modern updates.[cntraveler +1]<br/>•	Scale: ~215 guest rooms and suites.[lenoxhotel]<br/>•	Vibe: Warm, “old Boston” character with a neighborhood feel; lots of repeat guests.[cntraveler +1]<br/>---<br/>Location & Neighborhood<br/>The Lenox sits in the heart of Back Bay, one block from Newbury Street’s shops and cafés and a short walk from the Prudential Center and Copley Square.  The area is excellent for dining, strolling after dinner, and accessing public transit (a few minutes’ walk to the T).[travelweekly +2]<br/>For first‑time visitors, the location balances a lively neighborhood feel with easy access to major sights; you can reach many attractions by foot or a quick train ride.[facebook +1]<br/>---<br/>Rooms & Suites<br/>Rooms are traditionally styled (think classic Boston rather than ultra‑modern), generally clean, comfortable, and well‑maintained, with some showing the quirks of an older building.  Guests often praise the charm and comfort of the rooms but note that some bathrooms could be more updated, even though they are kept clean.[tripadvisor +1]<br/>Suites, especially the Back Bay Suite, are more spacious and upscale, offering separate bedroom and living/dining areas, wet bar, and upgraded finishes.  Certain suites feature wood‑burning fireplaces and marble baths with embedded flat‑screen mirrors, giving a more luxurious, apartment‑style feel.[lenoxhotel]<br/>---<br/>Cleanliness & Maintenance<br/>Reviews consistently highlight good overall cleanliness across rooms and public areas.  Guests report feeling comfortable during their stay, with no pattern of issues around housekeeping.[jessicalitras +1]<br/>Because it is a historic property, you may notice minor signs of age (smaller bathrooms in some rooms, slightly older fixtures), but these usually do not impact function or basic comfort.[tripadvisor +1]<br/>---<br/>Service & Staff<br/>Service is one of The Lenox’s strongest points. Staff are frequently described as warm, professional, and genuinely helpful, contributing significantly to repeat visits.  Many guests call out front desk, bell staff, and concierge for going out of their way to assist, from luggage to local recommendations.[yelp +2]<br/>The general tone of reviews suggests a personal, boutique feel rather than a big‑chain, transactional experience.[cntraveler +1]<br/>---<br/>Amenities & On‑Site Features<br/>The hotel blends classic character with modern conveniences: Wi‑Fi, contemporary entertainment centers in upgraded rooms, and comfortable public spaces.  Select suites add features like fireplaces, wet bars, and enhanced bath amenities, which are appealing for longer stays or special occasions.[lenoxhotel +2]<br/>Dining and bar options on‑site are positioned as cozy, local‑feeling spots rather than scene‑driven venues, which fits the overall boutique atmosphere.[lenoxhotel +1]<br/>---<br/>Atmosphere & Design<br/>The Lenox leans into its historic 1900s roots, with classic architecture and traditional interiors rather than minimalist or ultra‑modern design.  Guests often comment on the hotel’s “Boston character” and boutique charm, which contrasts with newer glass‑and‑steel properties nearby.[travelweekly +2]<br/>Common areas feel intimate and warm, with a residential vibe that appeals to travelers who prefer personality over a corporate feel.[yelp +1]<br/>---<br/>Pros<br/>•	Excellent Back Bay location for shopping, dining, and walking.[facebook +1]<br/>•	Boutique, historic charm with a strong sense of place.[travelweekly +1]<br/>•	Consistently praised service and friendly, attentive staff.[tripadvisor +2]<br/>•	Comfortable, clean rooms; upgraded suites offer fireplaces and great views (including toward the Boston Marathon finish line in some cases).[lenoxhotel +2]<br/>---<br/>Cons<br/>•	Some bathrooms and room details can feel a bit dated compared with brand‑new luxury hotels, even if they are clean.[tripadvisor]<br/>•	Historic building means rooms and layouts may vary more than in newer properties; not ideal if you want a very standardized, modern look.[cntraveler +1]<br/>---<br/>Best For<br/>•	Travelers who value character, service, and location over cutting‑edge design.[yelp +1]<br/>•	First‑time visitors wanting to be in the middle of Back Bay near restaurants, shops, and the Marathon finish line.[facebook +1]<br/>•	Couples, solo travelers, and business guests who like a boutique feel; suites work well for longer stays or small gatherings.[lenoxhotel +1]<br/>---<br/>Personal Take<br/>If you want a classic Boston stay in Back Bay—able to walk to Newbury Street, Copley, and plenty of restaurants—The Lenox is a strong choice, especially if warm, attentive service matters to you.  If your priority is ultra‑modern design and big, spa‑like bathrooms, a newer luxury high‑rise might suit you better, but you would be trading away some of the Lenox’s historic charm and boutique atmosphere.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/The+Lenox+Hotel/@42.3492329,-71.0821029,812m/data=!3m2!1e3!5s0x89e37a0e8226384f:0x5413612e15e98680!4m11!3m10!1s0x89e37a0c29b7312d:0xb695c161551d8451!5m4!1s2026-09-21!2i4!4m1!1i2!8m2!3d42.349229!4d-71.079528!16s%2Fm%2F0bbxqhr?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYwOS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
