  <Placemark>
    <name>✅❗️ The Norumbega Camden ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-08T19:00:00<br/><br/>Quick lowdown<br/><br/>- What to expect: Upscale, cozy dinner/drinks in a historic 1886 stone “castle” inn. Think date-night vibes, polished service, and a slower, relaxed meal.<br/>- What people rave about: Warm hospitality and high-end comfort are the consistent highlights; food praise tends to center on local seafood.<br/>- What to order: Prioritize seafood-forward dishes and chef’s seasonal specials (usually the safest “best of” at places like this).<br/>- What’s special/unique: The setting is the main draw—castle-like historic property, romantic atmosphere, and a “destination” feel even if you’re just dining.<br/>- Hidden-gem angle: If timing allows, arrive a bit early (or linger after) to enjoy the property/ambience—it’s the kind of place where the surroundings are part of the experience.<br/>- Heads up: It’s an upscale spot—dress a bit nicer than casual, and reservations are a good idea (you already have one).<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/The+Norumbega/@44.2178556,-69.0566583,17z/data=!4m11!3m10!1s0x4cadd7a47e75b3db:0x96cf127c84ea6021!5m4!1s2026-09-21!2i4!4m1!1i2!8m2!3d44.2178556!4d-69.0566583!16s%2Fg%2F11cn8xlqjz?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYyNC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
