  <Placemark>
    <name>✅❗️❌ Deuxave</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-02T18:30:00<br/><br/>Booking Details<br/>- Name: Tom Rubel<br/>- Date: Sunday, August 2, 2026<br/>- Time: 6:30 PM<br/>- Party Size: 2 Guests<br/>- Confirmation Number: 2109997237 <br/>- Restaurant Information<br/>	- Address: 371 Commonwealth Avenue, Boston, MA 02115<br/>	- Phone: 75175915 Important Policies<br/>	- Grace Period: 15 minutes. You must contact the restaurant if you anticipate being later than this.<br/>	- Cancellation Policy: Cancellations or no-shows within 24 hours of the reservation will incur a $50 per person charge. Modifying the guest count within 24 hours incurs a $25 per person charge.<br/><br/>Description<br/><br/>Location: 371 Commonwealth Avenue, Back Bay, Boston, MA  <br/>Phone: 617-517-5915 | Hours: Sun-Thu 5pm–9:30pm, Fri 5pm–10pm, Sat 5pm–10:30pm<br/><br/>The Vibe & Atmosphere<br/><br/>- Chic elegance without stuffiness.Glamorous chandelier-lit dining room that feels special-occasion-worthy but genuinely welcoming.<br/>- Forbes 4-Star rated (retained since 2017); "Best French Restaurant" winner from Boston Magazine multiple times (2014, 2017, 2023, 2025)<br/>- Warm lighting and cream-colored palette with marble & stone accents; windows overlook Commonwealth and Massachusetts Avenues<br/>- Heated outdoor patio (perfect in season); fireplace in main dining room<br/>- Unique feature: wall of mirrors reflecting Back Bay skyline<br/>- Beautiful windows framing historic Back Bay architecture<br/><br/>The Crowd<br/><br/>- Special occasion diners (celebrations, anniversaries, round-number birthdays)<br/>- Date night couples seeking romance<br/>- Boston's top chefs (professional endorsement—they dine here)<br/>- Upscale but not pretentious clientele<br/>- Mixed business/leisure crowds<br/><br/>What Diners Rave About<br/><br/>Best Dishes (from reviews):<br/><br/>- Duck Confit — Signature dish; crispy exterior, melting meat, often with lentils and Port reduction<br/>- Roast Duck — Pistachio-crusted or traditional; called "best duck in the city"<br/>- Foie Gras — Luxurious preparations; sometimes paired with prunes soaked in Port<br/>- Roast Chicken — Perfectly executed French classic<br/>- Crème Brûlée — Coconut version with orange sorbet receives particular praise<br/>- Lobster Bisque — Elegant French preparation<br/>- Prime Beef Tartare & Wagyu Carpaccio — Described as "ambitious appetizers"<br/><br/>Wine Program (Major Strength)<br/><br/>- 630 selections from 2,600-bottle inventory<br/>- Wine Spectator Award of Excellence(since 2015)<br/>- Sommelier Nick Daddona (10+ years experience) curates exceptional pairings<br/>- Specialties: French Burgundy, Bordeaux, Rhône, Bordeaux, Italy, California<br/>- Many bottles under 50;extensive50;extensive100+ selection<br/>- World-class wine program—described as one of Boston's best<br/><br/>Service<br/><br/>- Consistently praised as "impeccable," "attentive," and "solicitous"<br/>- Friendly yet professional tone<br/>- Knowledgeable staff about dishes and wine pairings<br/>- Responsive to special occasions<br/><br/>Dress Code<br/><br/>- Casual-but-smart to dressy evening wear<br/>- Upscale atmosphere suggests something trendier than business casual<br/><br/>What Reviewers Say<br/><br/>"Exquisite, nouvelle French–inflected cuisine to linger over, beautifully served in a sexy space with a cool bar." — Zagat<br/><br/>"Glamorous, chandelier-lit dining room creates special-occasion-feel, but there isn't a hint of stuffiness thanks to friendly vibe." — Time Out<br/><br/>"That rare American with a perfect French accent." — Boston Magazine (2025)<br/><br/>To Maximize Your Experience at Deuxave<br/><br/>1. Reserve in advance (8+ parties book via OpenTable as "Experiences"; 13+ via info@deuxave.com)<br/>2. Ask for wine pairing recommendations — the sommelier is a major asset<br/>3. Mention occasion — special attention to celebrations/dates<br/>4. Try the seasonal tasting menu (145,addfoiegrassupplementfor 145,addfoiegrassupplementfor 30)<br/>5. Arrive dressed elegantly — the beautiful room invites sophistication<br/>6. Dine in shoulder seasons (spring/early fall) for patio access<br/>7. Consider the duck confit or roast duck as signature dishes<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Deuxave/@42.3495174,-71.0916957,812m/data=!3m2!1e3!4b1!4m6!3m5!1s0x89e37a04c2ac1b6f:0xb67531643a81095!8m2!3d42.3495135!4d-71.0891154!16s%2Fg%2F1tj1t2rv?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYyOS4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
