  <Placemark>
    <name>❌ Beehive Trail Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Beehive Trail<br/><br/>📍 Acadia National Park ME<br/><br/>A 1.4-mile loop that ascends the sheer southeastern face of the Beehive via iron rungs and ladder-like iron bars bolted into the granite — essentially a via ferrata without equipment. The exposure is real but the moves are straightforward. At the top, views over Sand Beach, Great Head, and the open Atlantic are extraordinary. Returns via the Bowl, a glacial pond on the summit plateau.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Not suitable for those uncomfortable with heights or exposure — the cliff drops away beneath you.<br/>- Wet rock is dangerous; skip this trail in or after rain.<br/>- Start from the Sand Beach parking area on the Park Loop Road.<br/>- Do the loop counterclockwise — ascend the Beehive, descend via the Bowl trail.<br/>- Combines naturally with Sand Beach immediately below the trailhead.]]></description>
