  <Placemark>
    <name>❌ Precipice Trail Acadia National Park ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Precipice Trail<br/><br/>📍 Acadia National Park ME<br/><br/>Acadia's most thrilling trail: a 1.6-mile round trip up the nearly vertical east face of Champlain Mountain on iron rungs, handholds, and narrow ledge traverses. The summit delivers the best view in the park — the Porcupine Islands, Frenchman Bay, Schoodic Peninsula, and the full sweep of the Maine coast. Often closed in spring for peregrine falcon nesting; check status before going.<br/><br/>Tips<br/>- Check the NPS website before going — closed annually Feb–Aug for peregrine falcon nesting.<br/>- Not suitable for dogs or those uncomfortable with serious exposure.<br/>- The trailhead is on the Park Loop Road, 3 miles south of Bar Harbor.<br/>- Return via the North Face Trail for a loop rather than retracing the exposed route.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-purple</styleUrl>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="vault_type"><value>Footpath</value></Data>
      <Data name="icon"><value>footprints</value></Data>
      <Data name="color"><value>purple</value></Data>
    </ExtendedData>
    <Point>
      <coordinates>-68.2003,44.3574,0</coordinates>
    </Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>❤️ Dinner Bar Harbor ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Time: 2026-08-21T19:00:00<br/><br/>What it is: A highly-rated American restaurant known for its flavorful, "home-cooked" style cuisine, with standout dishes including lobster risotto, schnitzel, curry mussels, and panko-encrusted halibut.<br/><br/>Customers: Attracts locals and travelers alike, including world travelers and families looking for a high-quality, memorable dining experience in a welcoming setting.<br/><br/>Vibe: Small-town energy; warm, unpretentious atmosphere where food is described as being "cooked with love."<br/><br/>Strongest positives:<br/><br/>- Exceptional, flavorful food that many reviewers rank among the best they have ever eaten<br/>- Very kind, friendly, and attentive staff<br/>- Highly praised signature dishes like lobster risotto, schnitzel, and French onion soup<br/>- Great "small-town" atmosphere<br/><br/>Downsides:<br/><br/>- No significant recurring issues or downsides identified in recent reviews.<br/><br/>Note: Reservation confirmed by telephone — (207) 901-0018. No email confirmation exists for this booking.<br/><br/>More info: https://www.google.com/maps/place/Dinner/@44.3886629,-68.2235514,1584m/data=!3m2!1e3!5s0x4caebf79398c221d:0x760efaa8d0294f9f!4m13!1m5!2m4!1sRestaurants!5m1!4e9!6e5!3m6!1s0x4caebf005b379c81:0xc72ad7b501a68b23!8m2!3d44.3886633!4d-68.2140236!15sCgtSZXN0YXVyYW50c1oNIgtyZXN0YXVyYW50c5IBE2FtZXJpY2FuX3Jlc3RhdXJhbnSaAURDaTlEUVVsUlFVTnZaRU5vZEhsalJqbHZUMjVrVmxwNmFHeGxha0V5V2pCV1psWXdkRnBaTTJod1dqQkdkMW94UlJBQuABAPoBBAguEEM!16s%2Fg%2F11vxy0p6s6?entry=ttu&g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDYxMC4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]]></description>
