  <Placemark>
    <name>Bar Harbor, ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[```base<br/>filters:<br/>  or:<br/>    - destination == this<br/>    - list(trail).filter(value == this). 0<br/>    - file == this.<br/>views:<br/>  - type: map<br/>    name: Map<br/>    coordinates: note.Coordinates<br/>    markerIcon: note.<br/>    markerColor: note.<br/>    mapHeight: 400<br/>    defaultZoom: 12<br/>```<br/><br/>Points of interest<br/><br/>```base<br/>filters:<br/>  or:<br/>    - destination == this<br/>    - list(trail).filter(value == this). 0<br/>views:<br/>  - type: table<br/>    name: Places<br/>    order:<br/>      - file.<br/>      - type<br/>      - Rating<br/>      - icon<br/>      - Coordinates<br/>    sort:<br/>      - property: rating<br/>        direction: DESC<br/>```<br/><br/>Overview<br/>Bar Harbor is the gateway town to Acadia National Park on Mount Desert Island—known for rugged coastline, granite peaks, carriage roads, and waterfront dining.<br/><br/>---<br/><br/>Must-See & Do<br/><br/>Acadia National Park Highlights<br/>- Cadillac Mountain: sunrise views (often requires a reservation in peak season)<br/>- Park Loop Road: classic scenic drive with major pull-offs<br/>- Jordan Pond: easy walk + famous popovers at Jordan Pond House<br/>- Sand Beach + Ocean Path: iconic coastal stroll; nearby Thunder Hole at the right tide<br/><br/>Hiking & Viewpoints<br/>- Popular routes include Beehive Trail (steep/ladder rungs), Gorham Mountain, and Great Head (scenic loop)<br/><br/>Carriage Roads<br/>- Bike or walk the historic gravel roads and stone bridges (great for a lower-impact Acadia day)<br/><br/>On the Water<br/>- Whale watching / wildlife cruises, sea kayaking, and sunset sails from Bar Harbor<br/><br/>In Town<br/>- Stroll the Shore Path, browse shops/galleries, and enjoy lobster/seafood on the waterfront<br/><br/>---<br/><br/>Pro Tips<br/>- Parking and park access can be busy—start early and consider the Island Explorer shuttle (seasonal)<br/><br/>---]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#c-orange</styleUrl>
