  <Placemark>
    <name>Bristol, ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[```base<br/>filters:<br/>  or:<br/>    - destination == this<br/>    - list(trail).filter(value == this). 0<br/>    - file == this.<br/>views:<br/>  - type: map<br/>    name: Map<br/>    coordinates: note.Coordinates<br/>    markerIcon: note.<br/>    markerColor: note.<br/>    mapHeight: 400<br/>    defaultZoom: 12<br/>```<br/><br/>Points of interest<br/><br/>```base<br/>filters:<br/>  or:<br/>    - destination == this<br/>    - list(trail).filter(value == this). 0<br/>views:<br/>  - type: table<br/>    name: Places<br/>    order:<br/>      - file.<br/>      - type<br/>      - Rating<br/>      - icon<br/>      - Coordinates<br/>    sort:<br/>      - property: rating<br/>        direction: DESC<br/>```<br/><br/>Overview<br/>A picturesque harborside town on Maine's Midcoast with maritime heritage, scenic views, and excellent local dining. Perfect for a 4-6 hour visit.<br/><br/>---<br/><br/>Must-See & Do<br/><br/>Pemaquid Point Lighthouse<br/>- Iconic red-and-white striped lighthouse (1835) perched on dramatic rocky outcrop<br/>- Short walking path to lighthouse; worth the photo op<br/>- Small museum inside; nominal entry fee<br/><br/>Harborfront & Waterfront Park<br/>- Stroll the working harbor; watch lobster boats unload<br/>- Benches with views perfect for lunch or coffee break<br/>- Art galleries and shops line the streets<br/><br/>Pemaquid Falls & Reversing Falls<br/>- Tidal phenomenon: waterfall reverses direction with tide changes<br/>- Scenic walking trail; best visited at slack tide<br/>- Free; ~15 min from downtown<br/><br/>Colonial Pemaquid Historic Site<br/>- Ghost town archaeology site with ruins dating to 1630s<br/>- Small museum with artifacts<br/>- Peaceful, lesser-known gem<br/><br/>---<br/><br/>Best Places to Eat<br/><br/>Sea Monsters Lobster Company<br/>- Fresh lobster rolls, casual waterfront setting<br/>- No-frills, excellent quality<br/><br/>Coveside Restaurant<br/>- Upscale casual with harbor views<br/>- Fish & chips, fresh seafood, cocktails<br/>- Better for lingering over dinner<br/><br/>Pemaquid Brewery<br/>- Craft beers, food trucks or simple fare<br/>- Friendly vibe; outdoor seating<br/><br/>The Cod Fish Ball (5 min away in Damariscotta)<br/>- Legendary fried seafood; takeout only<br/>- Lines move fast; grab and find a picnic spot<br/><br/>---<br/><br/>Pro Tips<br/>- Allow extra time if catching the reversing falls—check tide times first<br/>- Lighthouse best photographed in late afternoon light<br/>- Parking is ample but can fill mid-day; arrive before noon<br/>- Bring a sweater; coastal wind picks up quickly<br/><br/>---]]></description>
