    <name>Castine, ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[```base<br/>filters:<br/>  or:<br/>    - destination == this<br/>    - list(trail).filter(value == this). 0<br/>    - file == this.<br/>views:<br/>  - type: map<br/>    name: Map<br/>    coordinates: note.Coordinates<br/>    markerIcon: note.<br/>    markerColor: note.<br/>    mapHeight: 400<br/>    defaultZoom: 12<br/>```<br/><br/>Points of interest<br/><br/>```base<br/>filters:<br/>  or:<br/>    - destination == this<br/>    - list(trail).filter(value == this). 0<br/>views:<br/>  - type: table<br/>    name: Places<br/>    order:<br/>      - file.<br/>      - type<br/>      - Rating<br/>      - icon<br/>      - Coordinates<br/>    sort:<br/>      - property: rating<br/>        direction: DESC<br/>```<br/><br/>Overview<br/>One of New England's oldest and quietest towns, with a historical trail marking the 1779 Penobscot Expedition.<br/><br/>---<br/><br/>Must-See & Do<br/><br/>Dyce's Head Lighthouse<br/>- Historic lighthouse at the tip of the Castine peninsula<br/><br/>Penobscot Expedition Historical Trail<br/>- Walking trail through town marking the 1779 Penobscot Expedition<br/><br/>---<br/><br/>Best Places to Eat<br/><br/>The Farmhouse Inn<br/>- Traditional New England fare in a historic, atmospheric setting<br/><br/>Dennett's Wharf<br/>- Waterfront dining with a focus on fresh local catches and a classic pub feel<br/><br/>Bah's Bakehouse<br/>- High-quality sandwiches and pastries for a picnic on the town common<br/><br/>---]]></description>
