  <Placemark>
    <name>Schoodic Peninsula, Winter Harbor, ME</name>
    <description><![CDATA[Schoodic Peninsula — Complete Guide<br/><br/>📍 Acadia National Park, Eastern Maine (~1 hour from Bar Harbor by road; ~45 min by ferry)<br/><br/>Schoodic Peninsula is Acadia's clearest "escape hatch" from August crowds. The peninsula receives only about 8% of Acadia's total visitor traffic—everyone else clusters on Mount Desert Island. You get the same dramatic pink granite coastline, moderate hikes with sweeping views, and coastal Maine authenticity, but with noticeably fewer people.<br/><br/>Full-Day Itineraries<br/><br/>Two distinct itineraries split to avoid retracing ground:<br/><br/>- Day 1: Park Loop, Trails & Points — Core park experience: ferry arrival, Frazer Point, Schoodic Loop Road, Anvil Trail/Raven's Nest hike, Schoodic Point tide pooling<br/>- Day 2: Villages, Byway & Water — Beyond-the-park experience: Corea fishing village, 29-mile Schoodic National Scenic Byway, gravel bike trail network, Sundew Trail, tide-dependent Little Moose Island walk<br/><br/>Key Trails & Activities<br/><br/>Hiking:<br/>- Anvil Trail to Schoodic Head — 2-mile moderate hike, 440-foot summit, far less crowded than Jordan Pond or Jordan Cliffs<br/>- Sundew Trail — Easy 0.7-mile flat walk to private rocky shoreline, often empty<br/>- Little Moose Island tide walk — Unique low-tide coastal exploration<br/><br/>Biking & Walking:<br/>- Schoodic Bike Path Network — 8.3-mile gravel trail system, connects multiple quiet harbors<br/><br/>Scenic & Stops:<br/>- Frazer Point Picnic Area — Waterfront, docks, early morning quiet<br/>- Schoodic Institute — Free ranger programs, birding walks, limited crowds<br/><br/>Getting There<br/><br/>- By road: ~1 hour from Bar Harbor via Ellsworth (route crowds around the town)<br/>- By ferry: Downeast Windjammer Ferry — 45-minute scenic crossing from Bar Harbor, lands directly in Winter Harbor, avoids Ellsworth entirely (recommended for Day 1)<br/><br/>Dining<br/><br/>- The Pickled Wrinkle — Local favorite in Birch Harbor, well below Bar Harbor wait times and prices<br/>- Winter Harbor and Birch Harbor have casual local options; no need to rush back downtown<br/><br/>Unique Stops (Beyond the Park)<br/><br/>- Corea — Genuine working lobster village, zero tourist infrastructure<br/>- U.S. Bell — Working bell foundry, casual visits welcome<br/><br/>Why Schoodic<br/><br/>- Crowds: ~8% of Acadia's traffic vs. 92% on Mount Desert Island<br/>- Scenery: Same dramatic pink granite coastline and Frenchman Bay views<br/>- Authenticity: Fewer cruise-ship tourists, more local feel<br/>- Water access: Ferry option, tide-dependent walks, harbor explorations<br/>- Flexibility: Two full days of distinct experiences without repeating attractions<br/><br/>```base<br/>filters:<br/>  or:<br/>    - destination == this<br/>    - list(trail).filter(value == this). 0<br/>    - file == this.<br/>views:<br/>  - type: map<br/>    name: Map<br/>    coordinates: note.Coordinates<br/>    markerIcon: note.<br/>    markerColor: note.<br/>    mapHeight: 400<br/>    defaultZoom: 12<br/>```<br/><br/>Points of interest<br/><br/>```base<br/>filters:<br/>  or:<br/>    - destination == this<br/>    - list(trail).filter(value == this). 0<br/>views:<br/>  - type: table<br/>    name: Places<br/>    order:<br/>      - file.<br/>      - type<br/>      - Rating<br/>      - icon<br/>      - Coordinates<br/>    sort:<br/>      - property: rating<br/>        direction: DESC<br/>```]]></description>
